{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant","id":943084,"title":"Alchemist Rant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T16:17:25-07:00","id":943084,"title":"Alchemist Rant","content":"Trigger Warning: This is not a very positive post.<br /> <br /> Coming into Promethean 2e I knew I shouldn't get my hopes up for playable Alchemists, I'd whittled down my expectation to getting some half passable rules that I could hammer into shape. But reading the Alchemists section...it broke me. It's like the book isn't content not giving a 'friendly' treatment to Alchemists, it has to go a step further and repeatedly finger waggle, hush hush, and wrist slap everyone who might want to include less mustache twirling examples of the splat.<br /> <br /> Some relevant quotes to illustrate my point:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Playing God pg. 257</b><br /> The difference between alchemists and these pioneers of the occult and the mundane is that alchemists have come to hate the human condition. They are so terrified of death, infirmity, and ignorance that they have lost sight of love, fellowship and the value of mundane accomplishment. Bit by bit, they sacrifice their humanity for power and knowledge, until they have turned themselves into something monstrous. Scientists, engineers, and occult explorers spend their lives trying to make the world better for their species \u2014 alchemists spend their lives running from death. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sidebar pg. 257</b><br /> Sane, rational, and cautious alchemists are unlikely to come into a Promethean story, however. Because they are more interested in knowledge than power, they are generally content with lesser alchemical workings and don\u2019t have the same hunger for Pyros and Vitriol as the mad alchemists described here. Without the self-hating obsession of those who despise their own humanity, they are not driven to commit atrocities against the Created. Most importantly, sane alchemists just know better. Chasing Prometheans is a good way to end up insane, maimed, or dead. These cautious alchemists rarely enter into the lives of Prometheans, and when they do, it\u2019s usually because the Prometheans sought them out, hoping for guidance </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Furnaces of Innumerable Alchemists pg. 258</b><br /> Alchemists who don\u2019t hunt the Created still form small cells and larger organizations, but since they are likely to avoid Prometheans, they aren\u2019t included. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Emerald Crucible pg. 259</b><br /> All alchemy \u2014 even the sane and cautious alchemy of those who avoid the Created </div> </div> </div>Now I get that this book is called Promethean, not Alchemist, and that the Created are the core focus. I also get that painting a picture of Prommies being buddy-buddy with Alchemists flies in the face of the whole isolationist theme. But does the book really need to flaunt that? Does it really need to commit word count to shutting down any possibility of non-antagonistic Alchemists. It probably wouldn't bother me as much if the book wasn't so outright about the exclusion. Like, if the text just said, &quot;there are less extreme Alchemists, but this is the Antagonists section so we're going to focus on the ones who are definitive villain material.&quot; That, in my eyes, would be a better handling that saying outright that &quot;sane&quot; alchemists never target Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Indeed even that statement is contradictory as the book goes on to explain that Prometheans are invaluable sources of knowledge, which all Alchemists seek (even the 'good' ones), and that the Created are rare enough that many aspiring Alchemists will never meet one. Plus there is disquiet, which would draw them in against their will regardless. It just doesn't add up, the explanations all read like flimsy excuses for why all Alchemists Prometheans meet should be evil psychopaths. It's a my way or the highway sort of vibe, that I can't help but feel is a deliberate shutdown of everyone who wanted to see Alchemists as a viable subsplat.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps it's just me, maybe I'm the only one reading it that way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR - Pendragon is irritated about the handling of alchemists. Also the sky is blue, and water is wet. Sorry.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Forgot to add, the rules for Alchemists are pretty good. Better, in fact, than I'd hoped for. They are 90% to being a playable subsplat, all they need are Experience Costs and a minor subsystem for determining when they get Conditions. Kudos to whoever wrote them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-03-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:37:31-07:00","id":943094,"title":"","content":"They're people who gain their powers by cracking open the player characters and stealing their most fundamental life force. What kind of treatment did you expect? When the easiest way to get Pyros is by ripping it out of living (almost) human beings, you're not gonna get a nice sort people people dedicated to the practice.<br /> <br /> You also gloss over the Alchemist guilds, many of which have very noble motivations despite being an antagonist group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:39:37-07:00","id":943096,"title":"","content":"I understand and empathize with where you're coming from, but I'm not sure if I share your frustration. Like literally not sure, I'm reading cover-to-cover in order and I'm not nearly to the antagonist section yet, so without having seen these quotes in context I don't know if I agree with your conclusions about them or not. However, just reading the passages you quoted out of context, it seems to me less like an admonition against including non-antagonistic alchemists in your game, and more of an explanation of why the book didn't dedicate space to non-antagonistic alchemists. It reads like a &quot;mea-culpa&quot; to me, apologizing for not being able to include details on more sympathetic or &quot;sane&quot; alchemists* and justifying the reasoning for their absence - they are less likely to end up in conflict with the game's protagonists than the ones that are actively out to get 'em.<br /> <br /> I'll come back to this when I reach that section so I can give a better-informed response.<br /> <br /> *as an aside, this is one place where I agree with you, I really hate seeing mental health associated with morality in this way. The &quot;sane&quot; ones are the good guys and the bad guys are all &quot;mad&quot;. As if mental illness isn't stigmatized enough already. But, I digress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:01:53-07:00","id":943117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943094#post943094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're people who gain their powers by cracking open the player characters and stealing their most fundamental life force. What kind of treatment did you expect? When the easiest way to get Pyros is by ripping it out of living (almost) human beings, you're not gonna get a nice sort people people dedicated to the practice.<br /> <br /> You also gloss over the Alchemist guilds, many of which have very noble motivations despite being an antagonist group.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, no. I get all that. As I said, I understand the writers don't want to dedicate book space to subsplats (even though Vampire, Werewolf, Mage &amp; Demon all do so to their betterment, but I digress.) My gripe is exclusively with the degree to which the book seems to go out of its way to make is excessively clear that Prometheans should not be running into 'sane' Alchemists...ever. Which to me feels artificial and a tad cloying.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943096#post943096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*as an aside, this is one place where I agree with you, I really hate seeing mental health associated with morality in this way. The &quot;sane&quot; ones are the good guys and the bad guys are all &quot;mad&quot;. As if mental illness isn't stigmatized enough already. But, I digress.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't digress at all, in fact you've touched another point I was struggling with but hadn't put to thought. <br /> <br /> Weirdly the sample Alchemist is a sincerely relatable and indeed pitiable figure. A young woman, marred by cancer and afraid for her life. Which really makes me think the entire divide between White Alchemists and Black Alchemists is...well...pointless. Let them all be deeply flawed people, relatable and repulsive in their own ways, and dispense with breaking them down into wise and &quot;Insensate&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:10:41-07:00","id":943129,"title":"","content":"Now I <b>really </b>want to play an Alchemist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, even with the puppy kicking, they are not worse than some Conspiracies of <u><i>playable </i></u>hunters, like Cheiron Group or the Faithful of Shulpae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-03-2016, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:15:12-07:00","id":943133,"title":"","content":"Insatiate is a viable classification, as non-insatiate alchemists don't run around cracking Prometheans open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:23:55-07:00","id":943141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943133#post943133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insatiate is a viable classification, as non-insatiate alchemists don't run around cracking Prometheans open.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like a weird distinction though, especially with disquiet in the mix. Like the line between 'sane' and 'insensate' is less a matter of morality and more about opportunity. Given enough time around a Promethean any Alchemist (driven by knowledge as they are) would end up trying to crack them open. Perhaps that's the reason 'sane' Alchemists avoid them? Though that, to me, suggests a breadth of knowledge about Prometheans that seems counter-intuitive for such a reclusive splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:25:29-07:00","id":943143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943141#post943141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like a weird distinction though, especially with disquiet in the mix. Like the line between 'sane' and 'insensate' is less a matter of morality and more about opportunity. Given enough time around a Promethean any Alchemist (driven by knowledge as they are) would end up trying to crack them open. Perhaps that's the reason 'sane' Alchemists avoid them? Though that, to me, suggests a breadth of knowledge about Prometheans that seems counter-intuitive for such a reclusive splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like arguing that there shouldn't be a distinction between murderers and normal people. The 'good' Alchemists don't steal Pyros; the Insatiate do. Surely that's worthy of a distinction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:28:47-07:00"