se than some Conspiracies of <u><i>playable </i></u>hunters, like Cheiron Group or the Faithful of Shulpae.</div> </div> </div> </div>And don't get me started on the Seers. I mean, look at this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/M5iALbv.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyway, what's the topic? It's kinda awkward replying to rants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:31:03-07:00","id":943149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943146#post943146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> And don't get me started on the Seers. I mean, look at this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/M5iALbv.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyway, what's the topic? It's kinda awkward replying to rants.</div> </div> </div> </div>How cool Alchemists are, and to see transhumanism represented in contrast to the simple Promethean need to just become regular human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:33:53-07:00","id":943151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943146#post943146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> And don't get me started on the Seers. I mean, look at this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/M5iALbv.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyway, what's the topic? It's kinda awkward replying to rants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't reply to them? The topic is &quot;I am dissatisfied with the presentation of alchemists and wanted to share my thoughts on the matter, and invite others to share their own thoughts on it.&quot; If you don't have anything to say on the subject, you don't have to say anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:38:43-07:00","id":943156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943143#post943143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's like arguing that there shouldn't be a distinction between murderers and normal people. The 'good' Alchemists don't steal Pyros; the Insatiate do. Surely that's worthy of a distinction?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do you get the Pyros to do the cool stuff without stealing it from a Promethean anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:43:39-07:00","id":943159,"title":"","content":"I'm having deja vu of the first Beast draft. Is this going to go a theme in Chronicles of Darkness going forward? Creating an antagonist group and actively seeking to quash any interpretation of them that isn't outright hostile.<br /> <br /> And I <i>like</i> Promethean's rejection (or at least willful ignoring) of transhumanism as a buy-in, regardless of my personal beliefs on the subject. I wonder if Deviant will continue the campaign to darken those shades of grey into black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-03-2016, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:45:57-07:00","id":943160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943143#post943143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like arguing that there shouldn't be a distinction between murderers and normal people. The 'good' Alchemists don't steal Pyros; the Insatiate do. Surely that's worthy of a distinction?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as we might like to pretend the distinction between murderer and normal person is pretty blurry. What with war, self-defense, insanity, accident, and plain old growing up. Certainly for a Promethean's purposes its a distinction they'd like to make, but narratively it creates a false dichotomy. On one side being the Prommie hunting Insensate Alchemists, afraid of death and fucking in the head by flux and disquiet, and on the other the 'sane' ones who never seek out Prometheans. What of the new blood Alchemists who don't yet know the ropes? or the desperate case of the 'sane' Alchemist driven to terrible length for reasons not entirely selfish?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of fertile plot points in that middle ground, challenging stories about humanity, that go down the drain when you throw away the possibility of friendly (or at least non-murderous) Alchemists.<br /> <br /> Again though, let me make this clear, my beef is not with the many fucked up Alchemical societies presented in the book. Those are fine. It's exclusively with the book's often black-and-white presentation of the subsplat. Mind you, the book (thankfully) doesn't shoehorn in rules to prevent them, but the text irked me enough that I had to say something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:47:08-07:00","id":943162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943160#post943160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as we might like to pretend the distinction between murderer and normal person is pretty blurry. What with war, self-defense, insanity, accident, and plain old growing up. Certainly for a Promethean's purposes its a distinction they'd like to make, but narratively it creates a false dichotomy. On one side being the Prommie hunting Insensate Alchemists, afraid of death and fucking in the head by flux and disquiet, and on the other the 'sane' ones who never seek out Prometheans. What of the new blood Alchemists who don't yet know the ropes? or the desperate case of the 'sane' Alchemist driven to terrible length for reasons not entirely selfish?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of fertile plot points in that middle ground, challenging stories about humanity, that go down the drain when you throw away the possibility of friendly (or at least non-murderous) Alchemists.<br /> <br /> Again though, let me make this clear, my beef is not with the many fucked up Alchemical societies presented in the book. Those are fine. It's exclusively with the book's often black-and-white presentation of the subsplat. Mind you, the book (thankfully) doesn't shoehorn in rules to prevent them, but the text irked me enough that I had to say something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for being so civil about it. Even if we disagree, one less flaming mess of a thread is something to be happy about.<br /> <br /> How are you liking the rest of the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:02:15-07:00","id":943179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant#post943084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But does the book really need to flaunt that? Does it really need to commit word count to shutting down any possibility of non-antagonistic Alchemists. It probably wouldn't bother me as much if the book wasn't so outright about the exclusion. Like, if the text just said, &quot;there are less extreme Alchemists, but this is the Antagonists section so we're going to focus on the ones who are definitive villain material.&quot; That, in my eyes, would be a better handling that saying outright that &quot;sane&quot; alchemists never target Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the sidebar you quoted is a pretty fair point, though: even if there are friendly alchemists we should ask, &quot;Well, do they need stats, then?&quot; I know the answer's, &quot;Yes, so we can play them&quot; but whatever. The 'playable' antagonist group here are supposed to be Centimanni.<br /> <br /> I will say it does come across heavy-handed, especially considering that <i>first edition's core book adventure</i> had a <i>friendly</i> (IIRC?) alchemist. There's precedent in the game-line.<br /> <br /> It all just reminds me of <b>Beast</b>'s Heroes. The books so heavy-handedly try to assure us they're antagonists that it's clunky and forced. My stance is confusing, I suppose, because I agree with the developer that these two characters should be antagonists but I disagree with how they're written.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I <i>love</i> the Seers picture. I never gave a damn about them until seeing it and now I love them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:05:04-07:00","id":943182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943159#post943159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having deja vu of the first Beast draft. Is this going to go a theme in Chronicles of Darkness going forward? Creating an antagonist group and actively seeking to quash any interpretation of them that isn't outright hostile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to point fingers, but weren't both books developed by Matthew McFarland? That might just be his style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943159#post943159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I <i>like</i> Promethean's rejection (or at least willful ignoring) of transhumanism as a buy-in, regardless of my personal beliefs on the subject. I wonder if Deviant will continue the campaign to darken those shades of grey into black.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, humanism is the first thing listed under themes on page 11. And I've seen two <i>different</i> gender-neutral pronouns used for nonbinary characters in the first 22 pages alone.<br /> <br /> ...What's that? Wait, you mean it's <i>transhumanism</i>, not trans humanism? Ohhhhh.... Carry on.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I'm sorry. I couldn't help it. I've been holding onto that pun for a <i>long</i> time</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:06:58-07:00","id":943183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943182#post943182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to point fingers, but weren't both books developed by Matthew McFarland? That might just be his style.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thought did cross my mind, I'll admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:08:09-07:00","id":943185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943162#post943162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for being so civil about it. Even if we disagree, one less flaming mess of a thread is something to be happy about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to hug you for this comment. Too few of these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How are you liking the rest of the book? </div> </div> </div>For me it's a mixed bag. Prommie has always been to me a flawed diamond, with lots of squandered potential. Plus I hack the shit out of everything I run, so take what I say with a grain of salt.<ul><li>The Bestowments are cool, as are the different flavors of Torment. I'll be subbing out a DIY Lineage system for what I consider an excessively restrictive set of X-splats, but I don't like X-Splats in general so that's probably me.</li> <li>Transmutations are largely fine, a couple I feel need tweaking, but that's fairly high praise from my camp. They are a definitive step up from 1e, that's for sure, and give Prommies a nice powerset at a level that doesn't jeopardize their themes (Mage supremacists will no doubt be pleased to hear).</li> <li>There are a lot of subsystems built in to help players along in the game, from Roles to Milstones, to their Vice/Virtue analogs. Though the milage of that may vary I'm personally not fond of such clearly directed gameplay, but others may enjoy the sense of direction.</li> <li>I could do without Centimanus being presented as antagonists, a more nuanced approach (like the Seers received in Awakening 2e) would have been appreciated. But I knew better than to expect one.</li> <li>Firestorm rules are cool. They weren't something I had any idea what to do with, so the book provided great direction there.</li> <li>Can't comment on the storytelling or regional chapters too much.</li> <li>Weirdly I think the game perhaps puts too much emphasis on the New Dawn. It is so prevalent that I fear players (especially new ones) will prioritize hitting milestones and racing too humanity over digging into the story and giving real life to their character.</li> </ul>All in all I'd give it maybe 3 of 5 stars. &quot;Good for what it is intended for, but too restrictive for much else.&quot; Mind you, this is all based off power skimming, and the joint reading of myself and a friend. Bottom line though, anyone who loved Prommie 1e will probably enjoy 2e, anyone who didn't will probably continue to dislike the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:16:57-07:00","id":943196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943182#post943182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to point fingers, but weren't both books developed by Matthew McFarland? That might just be his style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bit my tongue hard to not say it because I didn't want a mod (the irony) to think I was attacking a poster. Besides, if I ever need to read about how people hate Matt McFarland I can just go to 4chan<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:19:00-07:00","id":943200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943179#post943179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the sidebar you quoted is a pretty fair point, though: even if there are friendly alchemists we should ask, &quot;Well, do they need stats, then?&quot; I know the answer's, &quot;Yes, so we can play them&quot; but whatever. The 'playable' antagonist group here are supposed to be Centimanni.<br /> <br /> I will say it does come across heavy-handed, especially considering that <i>first edition's core book adventure</i> had a <i>friendly</i> (IIRC?) alchemist. There's precedent in the game-line.<br /> <br /> It all just reminds me of <b>Beast</b>'s Heroes. The books so heavy-handedly try to assure us they're antagonists that it's clunky and forced. My stance is confusing, I suppose, because I agree with the developer that these two characters should be antagonists but I disagree with how they're written.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Charlaquin said, this is probably McFarland's style. I suspect both Alchemists and Heroes were playable (or at least have rules for making them) in their original, pre-editing versions. There are still a couple of places in the Alchemists writeup that suggest rolls and subsystems were clearly cut from the final product. Which suggests to me he (or someone) deliberately does not want antagonist splats as PCs. Maybe it's a wordcount thing, I dunno.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I <i>love</i> the Seers picture. I never gave a damn about them until seeing it and now I love them </div> </div> </div>I think the Seers might be my ChroD antagonist gold standard. Even though I don't use them I respect how the authors painted such an enticing picture of the group, going so far as to present them as a legitimate playable option. Beyond giving players more options it does a brilliant job of painting the world in shades of gray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:21:42-07:00","id":943202,"title":"","content":"Heroes were never playable.<br /> <br /> I can't say the same with certainty about Alchemists, but I wouldn't be surprised if they were also never playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:26:05-07:00","id":943208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943202#post943202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes were never playable.I can't say the same with certainty about Alchemists, but I wouldn't be surprised if they were also never playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant there were more rules for them. One paragraph references giving Rote Quality to distilling potions (not using them, but just crafting them for later use), an act for which there is no apparent roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:31:15-07:00","id":943213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943208#post943208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant there were more rules for them. One paragraph references giving Rote Quality to distilling potions (not using them, but just crafting them for later use), an act for which there is no apparent roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not yet read Alchemists, so I wouldn't know. I'm going through from beginning to end.<br /> <br /> While that might point at playable Alchemists(I doubt it for a Core book, given the focus is Prometheans-maybe a supplement), it's just as likely that the writer thought the distilling potions thing warranted rolls and later did a quick revision when they figured it didn't fit with an NPC-&quot;when would it come up in their play?&quot; sort of thing. I've seen that more often than playable character scrubbing, as a fan and my more limited time as a freelancer.<br /> <br /> Again, I have thoughts on this, but by the time I get there, this thread might be done, so meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:42:12-07:00","id":943226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943196#post943196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bit my tongue hard to not say it because I didn't want a mod (the irony) to think I was attacking a poster. Besides, if I ever need to read about how people hate Matt McFarland I can just go to 4chan</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have assumed it was an attack. It's interesting to note certain tendencies in a particular writer's work. I'm not a fan of this specific trend, but there are trends in the writing of a lot of authors I like that I don't particularly like. Some pieces are just good enough to overlook the flaws.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the Alchemist section doesn't seem to be so bad as to make me outright uncomfortable the same way Beast did. The association of evil alchemists with mental illness is deeply troubling, and seems to arbitrarily rule out any plausible justification an Alchemist might have for their actions, but at least the authorial voice isn't oozing with vitriol (heh) towards their subject this time. I'll likely end up portraying Alchemists a little bit differently in my own games, but hey, that's the point of an RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:43:42-07:00","id":943228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943196#post943196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bit my tongue hard to not say it because I didn't want a mod (the irony) to think I was attacking a poster. Besides, if I ever need to read about how people hate Matt McFarland I can just go to 4chan</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite some protestations I've seen to the contrary, we don't look on any and all criticism of the writers and/or developers' work as personal attacks against them. It's just important that the object of critique be the <i>work, </i>not the <i>artist</i>, and that it be written in a respectful manner. I think pointing out an immerging pattern of Blackhatmatt presenting his antagonist factions as unabashedly and irredeemably antagonistic is perfectly reasonable, as long as we aren't making implications about his character as a person in the same breath (or in a different breath).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:51:37-07:00","id":943235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943226#post943226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't have assumed it was an attack. It's interesting to note certain tendencies in a particular writer's work. I'm not a fan of this specific trend, but there are trends in the writing of a lot of authors I like that I don't particularly like. Some pieces are just good enough to overlook the flaws.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the Alchemist section doesn't seem to be so bad as to make me outright uncomfortable the same way Beast did. The association of evil alchemists with mental illness is deeply troubling, and seems to arbitrarily rule out any plausible justification an Alchemist might have for their actions, but at least the authorial voice isn't oozing with vitriol (heh) towards their subject this time. I'll likely end up portraying Alchemists a little bit differently in my own games, but hey, that's the point of an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It does have a bit more empathy. It helps that an explicit goal of beating Amalgama Ltd is freeing the good alchemists from their blackmail, and that it's explicitly possible to meet one who's not interested in cannibalizing you for Pyros.<br /> <br /> I don't see the association with &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;mental illness&quot; though. The Divine Fire's always been associated with madness, so it makes sense that people who toy with it, particularly in such a reckless fashion, are a little...off. But that's me (I go &quot;Well, they tinker with neurochemistry when trying to enhance their minds, and they have no fucking clue what they're doing. Of course their sanity takes a beating, the idiots&quot;).<br /> <br /> Really, the reason insatiates are so antagonistic is less their profaning of being and more the fact that they profane the being by <i>murdering people for their spare parts. </i>That they also tie into the fundamental tragedy of reckless transhumanism (ie, losing what you had in pursuit of what you want) is just their particular &quot;spice.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:56:32-07:00","id":943242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943200#post943200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Seers might be my ChroD antagonist gold standard. Even though I don't use them I respect how the authors painted such an enticing picture of the group, going so far as to present them as a legitimate playable option. Beyond giving players more options it does a brilliant job of painting the world in shades of gray.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say, I'm kind of surprised. I don't disagree, in fact, I love the Seers for much the same reason. The new Mage core book does a fantastic job of expressing both why the Seers are antagonists by default <i>and</i> why so many people would want to join them, as well as giving plenty of options for Seer PCs. But what with your general distaste for antagonist factions, I didn't expect you to share this assessment of them. In my experience you tend to perceieve more contrast in the shading of protagonist/antagonist factions than I do, and I've seen an awful lot of people who see the relationship between the Pentacle and the Seers as straight-up Sin City black-and-white.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:59:33-07:00","id":943248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943226#post943226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily, the Alchemist section doesn't seem to be so bad as to make me outright uncomfortable the same way Beast did. The association of evil alchemists with mental illness is deeply troubling, and seems to arbitrarily rule out any plausible justification an Alchemist might have for their actions, but at least the authorial voice isn't oozing with vitriol (heh) towards their subject this time. I'll likely end up portraying Alchemists a little bit differently in my own games, but hey, that's the point of an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly it's nowhere near the caliber of Beast (looking at your trilby hero). If anything the Alchemist section feels...confused. Like it can' quite decide on the tone its going for. In one paragraph Alchemists are gleefully painted as monstrous fuckwads who tear apart Prometheans to feed their own monstrous gains, then another paints them as sad, terrified souls, damaged in life and terrified of death. Yet another sidebar goes onto explain that the real sociopaths all work alone, as the assorted factions quickly recognize them (which, IMO, is not particularly realistic towards Sociopaths namesake ability to blend in) and give them the boot.<br /> <br /> And let me make it clear, I quite like the damaged, terrified souls take. At least as an explanation for how most Alchemists get their foot in the Prommie slaying door. But that comes to odds with them being painted as Insensate and Insane. Two descriptors which seem too broad for a game which is intended to storytell a nuanced look into the human condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943242#post943242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, I'm kind of surprised. I don't disagree, in fact, I love the Seers for much the same reason. The new Mage core book does a fantastic job of expressing both why the Seers are antagonists by default <i>and</i> why so many people would want to join them, as well as giving plenty of options for Seer PCs. But what with your general distaste for antagonist factions, I didn't expect you to share this assessment of them. In my experience you tend to perceieve more contrast in the shading of protagonist/antagonist factions than I do, and I've seen an awful lot of people who see the relationship between the Pentacle and the Seers as straight-up Sin City black-and-white.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason I don't use them is because I removed their god heads smashed them together with the Diamond. Indeed in some senses I use them more than I do the Diamond orders.<br /> <br /> As for Antagonists, my main beef is with write-ups that present human beings, nuanced people, as black-and-white baddies. Groups like Belial's Blood and the Pure who harken back the the Black Spiral Dancers of cWoD. Alchemist currently wobble between this, with some paragraphs making me want to scream and others (like the sample character) doing an excellent job of selling them as real, complete, people.<br /> <br /> The only other antagonist concern I have is whether they play double duty. The Seers, for example, are the dark mirror of the Diamond. My thought was, why does that reflection need to be external? Especially given the sort of games I run, which focus largely on internal and interpersonal conflicts, Seer style antagonists are far more interesting when they come from within, or better, when it's one of the players themselves. Alchemists, obviously, can't fit within the Prommie mold, so they must remain external.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-03-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:03:17-07:00","id":943254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943235#post943235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. It does have a bit more empathy. It helps that an explicit goal of beating Amalgama Ltd is freeing the good alchemists from their blackmail, and that it's explicitly possible to meet one who's not interested in cannibalizing you for Pyros.<br /> <br /> I don't see the association with &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;mental illness&quot; though. The Divine Fire's always been associated with madness, so it makes sense that people who toy with it, particularly in such a reckless fashion, are a little...off. But that's me (I go &quot;Well, they tinker with neurochemistry when trying to enhance their minds, and they have no fucking clue what they're doing. Of course their sanity takes a beating, the idiots&quot;).<br /> <br /> Really, the reason insatiates are so antagonistic is less their profaning of being and more the fact that they profane the being by <i>murdering people for their spare parts. </i>That they also tie into the fundamental tragedy of reckless transhumanism (ie, losing what you had in pursuit of what you want) is just their particular &quot;spice.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>An in-universe justification only goes so far. A writer has total control over what they write, so anything they write is subject to that control. Which means if they write a reason for their bad guys to all be insane, that doesn't alleviate responsibility for writing a group of bad guys as all being insane.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not arguing with the themes used in the Alchemists. Reckless transhumanism is perfectly fine as the basis for a villain. The insistence that they're all a bit crazy though feels wrong when a villain can easily have rational, &quot;ends justify the means&quot; arguments for during abominable things. Do you take apart a dozen malformed would-be child-things in the hope that it prevents any child from dying ever again? There's a character you can make there with reasons for why he thinks this is a good idea, who can have a rational argument for his actions, who isn't automatically mentally ill. Still a character who, I would argue, is wrong in their actions, is certainly a villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:09:18-07:00","id":943257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943235#post943235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the association with &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;mental illness&quot; though. The Divine Fire's always been associated with madness, so it makes sense that people who toy with it, particularly in such a reckless fashion, are a little...off. But that's me (I go &quot;Well, they tinker with neurochemistry when trying to enhance their minds, and they have no fucking clue what they're doing. Of course their sanity takes a beating, the idiots&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the very idea of &quot;madness&quot; is a little ableist. Obviously it isn't always when it's handled responsibly, but doing so requires a great deal of care and intentionality. It's one thing to say that Alchemists regularly deal with powers that are dangerous for the human mind and as a result often end up traumatized and/or mentally scarred. It's another thing to call all the Alchemists who don't murder perople for their spare parts &quot;sane&quot;. Doing so implies by contrast that all the ones that do murder people for their spare parts are &quot;insane&quot;, and paints a picture of the world where mentally healthy people are not murderous and mentally ill people are. Which apart from being untrue on both counts contributes to an ongoing stigma about mental illness, where people with visible mental illness are to be feared and people without visible mental illness are to be trusted. The RPG industry has a long history of stigmatizing mental illness, and in general CofD 2e has made great strides to remedy that. <i>Particularly</i> in products that David Hill has been involved in. But there are still lingering issues with the RPG idea of &quot;madness&quot; being perpetuated, particularly in Mage and Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:10:31-07:00","id":943258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943179#post943179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say it does come across heavy-handed, especially considering that <i>first edition's core book adventure</i> had a <i>friendly</i> (IIRC?) alchemist. There's precedent in the game-line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was, of all things? a Redeemed, yeah.<br /> <br /> The OP replies to all his own questions/regards: Why such a heavy handed disposition? Because the focus of the game are the walking &amp; breathing Pyretic Engines. If the game allows Centimani being playable, it needs something to fill that niche. I don't particularly agree with the editorial vision, but the thing about Promethean is just that: Exploration of the human condition by means of cultural dissonance.<br /> <br /> There's something to be said about humanity's capability for monstrous acts. I believe this is what the Alchemist hoped to highlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:20:30-07:00","id":943272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943258#post943258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which was, of all things? a Redeemed, yeah.<br /> <br /> The OP replies to all his own questions/regards: Why such a heavy handed disposition? Because the focus of the game are the walking &amp; breathing Pyretic Engines. If the game allows Centimani being playable, it needs something to fill that niche. I don't particularly agree with the editorial vision, but the thing about Promethean is just that: Exploration of the human condition by means of cultural dissonance.<br /> <br /> There's something to be said about humanity's capability for monstrous acts. I believe this is what the Alchemist hoped to highlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemists are painted so heavily as antagonistic because they are the thematic inverse of the Created; as the latter strive to be human, the former strain to leave humanity behind. So long as the Pilgrimage is on center stage, its antithesis will be demonized.<br /> <br /> I can see perfectly acceptable Alchemists having much more of a place outside of the Promethean corebook or possibly the line as a whole, perhaps as kindred spirits to Ascension-seeking mages or the mummies who emulate The Heretic. But in a game where basic humanity is the end goal, those looking to surpass it must be viewed negatively in the name of thematic consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:27:00-07:00","id":943280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943254#post943254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An in-universe justification only goes so far. A writer has total control over what they write, so anything they write is subject to that control. Which means if they write a reason for their bad guys to all be insane, that doesn't alleviate responsibility for writing a group of bad guys as all being insane.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not arguing with the themes used in the Alchemists. Reckless transhumanism is perfectly fine as the basis for a villain. The insistence that they're all a bit crazy though feels wrong when a villain can easily have rational, &quot;ends justify the means&quot; arguments for during abominable things. Do you take apart a dozen malformed would-be child-things in the hope that it prevents any child from dying ever again? There's a character you can make there with reasons for why he thinks this is a good idea, who can have a rational argument for his actions, who isn't automatically mentally ill. Still a character who, I would argue, is wrong in their actions, is certainly a villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I see where you're coming from. And yes, &quot;madness&quot; can be a bit ableist as a concept-it's just easier to use one word than &quot;maladaptive behaviors that may pose a risk to themselves and those around them, but may and likely often belong to an otherwise good or okay person.&quot; Which a compulsion to collecting dead bodies to imbue with life is generally an example of, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Still, it makes sense that they would develop bad Persistent Conditions, or that they already had them-the latter case is what drove them to insatiate alchemy, the former the inevitable aftereffects of toying with what you don't understand by sticking your ungloved hand into the the bright hot flickering thing that has signs saying &quot;DANGER: APPROACH WITH CAUTION&quot; all over it. I also meant to imply that madness was not something I was associating with &quot;evil&quot; but what happens when the inevitable burns manifest as brain damage, which was meant to include things like losing an arm, no longer being able to tolerate sunlight...one of a number of Pyros-induced disabilities that underline the question &quot;was this worth it?&quot; And as motives to overcome humanity's limitations to begin with in such an extreme way.<br /> <br /> (I fundamentally agree with the criticism that it increasingly seems like Matt has a difficult time writing sympathetic villains, or acknowledging the potential for sympathy-the whole subsection felt like a step in the right direction, but yeah, this has flaws in it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-03-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:27:17-07:00","id":943281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943272#post943272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alchemists are painted so heavily as antagonistic because they are the thematic inverse of the Created; as the latter strive to be human, the former strain to leave humanity behind. So long as the Pilgrimage is on center stage, its antithesis will be demonized.<br /> <br /> I can see perfectly acceptable Alchemists having much more of a place outside of the Promethean corebook or possibly the line as a whole, perhaps as kindred spirits to Ascension-seeking mages or the mummies who emulate The Heretic. But in a game where basic humanity is the end goal, those looking to surpass it must be viewed negatively in the name of thematic consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give the all-seeing eye a cookie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:36:11-07:00","id":943292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943272#post943272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemists are painted so heavily as antagonistic because they are the thematic inverse of the Created; as the latter strive to be human, the former strain to leave humanity behind. So long as the Pilgrimage is on center stage, its antithesis will be demonized.<br /> <br /> I can see perfectly acceptable Alchemists having much more of a place outside of the Promethean corebook or possibly the line as a whole, perhaps as kindred spirits to Ascension-seeking mages or the mummies who emulate The Heretic. But in a game where basic humanity is the end goal, those looking to surpass it must be viewed negatively in the name of thematic consistency</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure demonization was the right call. They come off like strawmen, heavy handed D.A.R.E. style cautionary tales. &quot;Transhumanism, not even once.&quot; What they fail to do is paint a picture of <b>why</b> Transhumanism is terrible. This is actually where some rules would be beneficial, a sort of show, don't tell. If there was some system by which we could see how Vitriol fucks Alchemists in the head (or even the line &quot;Vitriol fucks people in the head&quot;) it'd be easier to see how Transhumanism drives people mad.<br /> <br /> As is the buy-in is just too steep. I'm totally ready to accept that Humanism is the right call (in Promethean that is), but I'd appreciate it if the assertion was argued at least a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-03-2016, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:42:06-07:00","id":943296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943292#post943292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure demonization was the right call. They come off like strawmen, heavy handed D.A.R.E. style cautionary tales. &amp;quot;Transhumanism, not even once.&amp;quot; What they fail to do is paint a picture of <b>why</b> Transhumanism is terrible. This is actually where some rules would be beneficial, a sort of show, don't tell. If there was some system by which we could see how Vitriol fucks Alchemists in the head (or even the line &amp;quot;Vitriol fucks people in the head&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> it'd be easier to see how Transhumanism drives people mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine you're a Promethean, a few years into you Pilgrimage; you understand some things about humanity, you know what sets you apart from it, and your days are spent striving towards becoming it. You come across a human being - a real human being, born into glorious normalcy with a genuine soul - who wants to kill you for the fire inside you. Somehow things reach a point where the two of you talk about things, and when you ask them why they want to steal your flame, they explain that they want to become more, become stronger and smarter and immortal and to surpass the circumstances of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would find that infuriating. Here's some jerk who has everything you've ever wanted by no virtue or effort of their own other than a luckier origin than you're own, and they're not happy with it. They want more. They want to leave being human (magnificently human!) for another state of being, and worse, they want to kill you to fuel it.<br /> <br /> You don't need &quot;Pyros drives them hopeless maaaaaaaad!&quot; for that to be an incredible point of ohilosophical contention in a game about the beauty of basic fundamental humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:46:48-07:00","id":943304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943292#post943292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure demonization was the right call. They come off like strawmen, heavy handed D.A.R.E. style cautionary tales. &quot;Transhumanism, not even once.&quot; What they fail to do is paint a picture of <b>why</b> Transhumanism is terrible. This is actually where some rules would be beneficial, a sort of show, don't tell. If there was some system by which we could see how Vitriol fucks Alchemists in the head (or even the line &quot;Vitriol fucks people in the head&quot;) it'd be easier to see how Transhumanism drives people mad.<br /> <br /> As is the buy-in is just too steep. I'm totally ready to accept that Humanism is the right call (in Promethean that is), but I'd appreciate it if the assertion was argued at least a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hope something like that is addressed in the Firestorm Anthology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:48:33-07:00","id":943308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943296#post943296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, a few years into you Pilgrimage; you understand some things about humanity, you know what sets you apart from it, and your days are spent striving towards becoming it. You come across a human being - a real human being, born into glorious normalcy with a genuine soul - who wants to kill you for the fire inside you. Somehow things reach a point where the two of you talk about things, and when you ask them why they want to steal your flame, they explain that they want to become more, become stronger and smarter and immortal and to surpass the circumstances of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would find that infuriating. Here's some jerk who has everything you've ever wanted by no virtue or effort of their own other than a luckier origin than you're own, and they're not happy with it. They want more. They want to leave being human (magnificently human!) for another state of being, and worse, they want to kill you to fuel it.<br /> <br /> You don't need &quot;Pyros drives them hopeless maaaaaaaad!&quot; for that to be an incredible point of ohilosophical contention in a game about the beauty of basic fundamental humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd instantly adopt Stanum, croak the fucker and raise his former corpse as my progeny. Probably etch &quot;You asked for this&quot; somewhere in his hide while at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:50:16-07:00","id":943311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943308#post943308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd instantly adopt Stanum, croak the fucker and raise his former corpse as my progeny. Probably etch &amp;quot;You asked for this&amp;quot; somewhere in his hide while at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend, calm down! Your choleric humour has seized control of you! Resist the alluring call of Torment!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:55:19-07:00","id":943320,"title":"","content":"&quot;I will see this person as an object as I vivisect them for scientific advancement&quot; is pretty textbook insane. &quot;I will strive to achieve this goal, even to the point of destruction of myself or everything I hold dear&quot; is also textbook insanity. &quot;I care only about my well being to the exclusion of everything and everyone else&quot; is also another example of insanity. These are the viewpoints and attitudes you see in the Alchemists that pursue Prometheans as a means to an end. This is why they are considered insane while alchemists that wisely avoid Prometheans, the ones that know the dangers of interacting with Prometheans, are considered sane. I don't see one group of alchemists as being inherently &quot;eeevil&quot; and the other &quot;bastions of moral goodness&quot;. But I sure do see one group as being more conscious of the repercussions associated with their actions and behavior, and that is very much an indicator of one's sanity or lack thereof. I don't see sanity being conflated with morality here the way some others do. If anything there seems to be a large dose of amorality on the alchemists' part.<br /> <br /> Insanity is measured by degrees, it isn't an all or nothing proposition, but the alchemists in the antagonist section seem to be the people who are well on the extreme negative end of that spectrum. These aren't people that would just like to be a little better physically and mentally than other people, these are people who are absolutely driven to cast aside humanity along with the weaknesses they believe it entails, and don't care about how they achieve that end. These antagonist alchemists are like heroin junkies who don't care about how they get their next fix, just that they get it. I've specifically dealt with people like that, they most certainly were not sane.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yes, you can count me in the camp of people who are just fine with the antagonist splat not being suitable player options straight out of the core rules. Focus on the Proetheans in the core book about Prometheans, leave playable antagonists for later projects, if ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:03:34-07:00","id":943323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943296#post943296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine you're a Promethean, a few years into you Pilgrimage; you understand some things about humanity, you know what sets you apart from it, and your days are spent striving towards becoming it. You come across a human being - a real human being, born into glorious normalcy with a genuine soul - who wants to kill you for the fire inside you. Somehow things reach a point where the two of you talk about things, and when you ask them why they want to steal your flame, they explain that they want to become more, become stronger and smarter and immortal and to surpass the circumstances of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would find that infuriating. Here's some jerk who has everything you've ever wanted by no virtue or effort of their own other than a luckier origin than you're own, and they're not happy with it. They want more. They want to leave being human (magnificently human!) for another state of being, and worse, they want to kill you to fuel it.<br /> <br /> You don't need &quot;Pyros drives them hopeless maaaaaaaad!&quot; for that to be an incredible point of ohilosophical contention in a game about the beauty of basic fundamental humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>A splendidly reasonable scenario, and one the text fully enables. Let me try one it hampers.<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, hunted by this desperate, haunted man at least as disquieting as yourself. Being used to people trying to murder you, and finding yourself in a rare position to converse with this clearly Disquiet riddled soul. What he reveals to you is not the standard &quot;I want to be more&quot; spiel. As it turns out the mans child, a 4 year old babe just headed for kindergarden, suffers an incurable ailment. Science has failed him, common Alchemy failed him, Vitriol is the only hope she has left. Do you gamble your vitriol on another? Or do you let the child die?<br /> <br /> That take on Alchemists is one I'd very much like to see. A presentation in which Transhumanism seems an enticing option. Later the child could go all pandoran and devour her father, or some similar backlash to prove that humanism is #1, or not, perhaps it could be the impetus that drives the Prommie doesn the Centimanus path (to his ruin). So much possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:12:02-07:00","id":943328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943323#post943323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A splendidly reasonable scenario, and one the text fully enables. Let me try one it hampers.<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, hunted by this desperate, haunted man at least as disquieting as yourself. Being used to people trying to murder you, and finding yourself in a rare position to converse with this clearly Disquiet riddled soul. What he reveals to you is not the standard &quot;I want to be more&quot; spiel. As it turns out the mans child, a 4 year old babe just headed for kindergarden, suffers an incurable ailment. Science has failed him, common Alchemy failed him, Vitriol is the only hope she has left. Do you gamble your vitriol on another? Or do you let the child die?<br /> <br /> That take on Alchemists is one I'd very much like to see. A presentation in which Transhumanism seems an enticing option. Later the child could go all pandoran and devour her father, or some similar backlash to prove that humanism is #1, or not, perhaps it could be the impetus that drives the Prommie doesn the Centimanus path (to his ruin). So much possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly this. The idea that doing desperate, amoral things for power is the province of the insane ignores the vast story potential in <i>even more terrifying</i> reasons that might lead one to perform such actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:15:53-07:00","id":943331,"title":"","content":"Again, not there, but in the spirit of what 1E had to say on the subject:<br /> <br /> Healthy Minds do not seek the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:23:57-07:00","id":943335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943331#post943331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, not there, but in the spirit of what 1E had to say on the subject:<br /> <br /> Healthy Minds do not seek the Divine Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of on par with claiming that your lead female character can only wear a bikini because she breathes through her skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:25:31-07:00","id":943337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943331#post943331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, not there, but in the spirit of what 1E had to say on the subject:<br /> <br /> Healthy Minds do not seek the Divine Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excluding, of course, all the sane Alchemists who are apparently in full control of their faculties despite using and containing Pyros.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: That was a tad too snarky, sorry. Let me try a more reasoned approach.<br /> <br /> Why? Why don't healthy minds seek the divine fire? Does tapping pyros demand madness? Clearly no, as the text admits there are wholly sane alchemists. Do healthy minds have better resorts? Sometimes, but I know enough scientists to say with certainty that if Alchemy worked, reasonable people would pursue it and not for exclusively selfish reasons. And if walking fonts of Alchemical mystery were walking about, dammit, those sane men would absolutely seek them out. To study them, to protect them, and, yes, to dissect them.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd be happier if all Alchemists were unhinged, if the requirement to wield divine fire be intrinsically tied to desperate obsession. Sometimes the text says as much, then sometimes it contradicts that with things like White Alchemists who Prometheans apparently never meet. It just doesn't add up, and when I can't rationally reason my way to how a set piece came about (such as why all the Alchemists that seek Prometheans are dead bent on tearing them apart) then the whole thing starts to seem absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-03-2016, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:26:10-07:00","id":943338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943296#post943296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, a few years into you Pilgrimage; you understand some things about humanity, you know what sets you apart from it, and your days are spent striving towards becoming it. You come across a human being - a real human being, born into glorious normalcy with a genuine soul - who wants to kill you for the fire inside you. Somehow things reach a point where the two of you talk about things, and when you ask them why they want to steal your flame, they explain that they want to become more, become stronger and smarter and immortal and to surpass the circumstances of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would find that infuriating. Here's some jerk who has everything you've ever wanted by no virtue or effort of their own other than a luckier origin than you're own, and they're not happy with it. They want more. They want to leave being human (magnificently human!) for another state of being, and worse, they want to kill you to fuel it.<br /> <br /> You don't need &quot;Pyros drives them hopeless maaaaaaaad!&quot; for that to be an incredible point of ohilosophical contention in a game about the beauty of basic fundamental humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that this is coming from the perspective of a human? I'd recognize some &quot;grass is greener&quot; going on. I might well be interested in working together - I'll help you in your research on transcending humanity if you help me understand what it means to be human. But, of course, if he seems intent on killing me, I probably wouldn't trust him with such an arrangement, nor that he'd really have much understanding of humanity if he's so eager to leave it behind. I'd probably pity him for being born with the gift of humanity, but understanding it less than I even do. I'd definitely be afraid of him. Hating him would seem misplaced, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:28:45-07:00","id":943342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943331#post943331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, not there, but in the spirit of what 1E had to say on the subject:<br /> <br /> Healthy Minds do not seek the Divine Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so, but the issue is that the impression people are getting is that the only type of mind that seeks the Fire seems to be not only unhealthy, but also shitty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:29:01-07:00","id":943343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943337#post943337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excluding, of course, all the sane Alchemists who are apparently in full control of their faculties despite using and containing Pyros.</div> </div> </div> </div>The warning applies, but I'ma go on a limb and say I won't be surprised if I end up questioning their stability too.<br /> <br /> Some form for mental disquiet are subtler than others, but the Divine Fire responds to desperation, that mightiest of emotions. That's a poor stage for purity of intentions and executions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:40:47-07:00","id":943348,"title":"","content":"I kind of see alchemists as, weirdly enough, the wife of the main villain in my novel I am working on. She was someone who was raised to be good person, a fair ruler and a Hound of God (yes she is a werewolf). But then her court wizard diagnosed her with a degenertive illness that his magic couldn't cure, one that would cripple and kill her all the fast due her werewolf healing factor turning against her. Long story short, she cut a deal a demon for ritual that required her to kill people to stave off the illness. At first she did it reluctantly.... but she went from self-justification to taking a guilty pleasure in it to straight up Cruella de Vil evil decadence.<br /> <br /> Alchemists are the same way, the ones that hunt Prometheans and kill them don't so much go mad so much their justifications to themselves push themselves down a slippery slope until eventually they enjoy what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:46:27-07:00","id":943351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943337#post943337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excluding, of course, all the sane Alchemists who are apparently in full control of their faculties despite using and containing Pyros.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have any sense of pattern-recognition whatsoever you will have noticed the tendency for going neck-deep into any given supernatural power source in this setting to have a causal relationship to or root origin in a beginning or developed lack of regard for caution when dealing with overwhelming powers that can and will try to eat you. The Shadow does it, the Underworld does it, the Fae do it, vampirism does it, and so on around the dinner table.<br /> <br /> Experienced dabblers who remain dabblers tend to do so as a conscious choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-11-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:47:50-07:00","id":943353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943320#post943320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I will see this person as an object as I vivisect them for scientific advancement&quot; is pretty textbook insane. &quot;I will strive to achieve this goal, even to the point of destruction of myself or everything I hold dear&quot; is also textbook insanity. &quot;I care only about my well being to the exclusion of everything and everyone else&quot; is also another example of insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>By what textbook? Not the DSM 5, that's for sure.<br /> <br /> If you define horrible acts as insane, then yes, people who commit horrible acts will be insane by that definition. But such a definition ignores the fact that perfectly mentally healthy people can just as easily commit those acts. It ignores the fact that there are legions of mentally ill people who would never dream of committing such acts. It paints the world in terms of good people and madmen, and that's not a healthy attitude to have. I would say that vivisecting people in the name of scientific advancement, self-destruction in pursuit of a goal, and extreme lack of empathy are all awful things that &quot;sane&quot; and &quot;insane&quot; people alike are equally capable of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943320#post943320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the viewpoints and attitudes you see in the Alchemists that pursue Prometheans as a means to an end. This is why they are considered insane while alchemists that wisely avoid Prometheans, the ones that know the dangers of interacting with Prometheans, are considered sane. I don't see one group of alchemists as being inherently &quot;eeevil&quot; and the other &quot;bastions of moral goodness&quot;. But I sure do see one group as being more conscious of the repercussions associated with their actions and behavior, and that is very much an indicator of one's sanity or lack thereof. I don't see sanity being conflated with morality here the way some others do. If anything there seems to be a large dose of amorality on the alchemists' part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Alchemists are wise enough to put their own safety above pursuit of their goals, some are not. Some Alchemists are altruistic enough not to want to kill people in pursuit of their goals (and not to rationalize Prometheans as acceptable to kill because they're &quot;not really people&quot;) and others are not. Some Alchemists fall victim to Disquiet and others do not. It would be nice if these were not dichotomous categorizations, and if they were not associated with the Alchemists' Sanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943320#post943320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insanity is measured by degrees, it isn't an all or nothing proposition, but the alchemists in the antagonist section seem to be the people who are well on the extreme negative end of that spectrum. These aren't people that would just like to be a little better physically and mentally than other people, these are people who are absolutely driven to cast aside humanity along with the weaknesses they believe it entails, and don't care about how they achieve that end. These antagonist alchemists are like heroin junkies who don't care about how they get their next fix, just that they get it. I've specifically dealt with people like that, they most certainly were not sane.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yes, you can count me in the camp of people who are just fine with the antagonist splat not being suitable player options straight out of the core rules. Focus on the Proetheans in the core book about Prometheans, leave playable antagonists for later projects, if ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get that the Alchemists detailed in the Antagonist section are naturally the ones that are prone to hunting and killing Prometheans - that's what makes them antagonists, and the reason they were able to justify having wordcount dedicated to them that could have gone towards Zeka. In a game about Prometheans striving to become human, human antagonists striving to shed their humanity make compelling additions to the story, where more reasonable Alchemists don't really add much. Indeed, I think the right call was made in that respect. However, I don't think Pendragon is wrong to feel that the commentary about why non-antagonistic Alchemists are unlikely to show up in Promethean games are misplaced. I also don't appreciate the associations between antagonists and &quot;madness&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:48:30-07:00","id":943354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943351#post943351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pendragon, if you have any sense of pattern-recognition whatsoever you will have noticed the tendency for going neck-deep into any given supernatural power source in this setting to have a causal relationship to or root origin in a beginning or developed lack of regard for caution when dealing with overwhelming powers that can and will try to eat you. The Shadow does it, the Underworld does it, the Fae do it, vampirism does it, and so on around the dinner table.<br /> <br /> Experienced dabblers who remain dabblers tend to do so as a conscious choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Sekhem sorcerers will be dif I can't even finish this sentence.<br /> <br /> This is a horror universe first and foremost. Good intentions pave the path to hell and lead good people into degrading Integrity and exploration of unnatural magical forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-12-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:49:38-07:00","id":943356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943343#post943343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The warning applies, but I'ma go on a limb and say I won't be surprised if I end up questioning their stability too.<br /> <br /> Some form for mental disquiet are subtler than others, but the Divine Fire responds to desperation, that mightiest of emotions. That's a poor stage for purity of intentions and executions.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, sorry, that first response was awfully snarky. I edited the first post with more than a quip.<br /> <br /> Second, I'd be happy to get on board with your take. I quite like your take. The Chronicles of Darkness have enough healthier ways to Transhumanism that I'd be perfectly happy if Pyros was for fucked up people, by fucked up people. But that's not what the book says. What the book says is that there are comparatively sane, altruistic alchemists who all somehow agree not to pursue.<br /> <br /> That is what I was ranting about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:53:01-07:00","id":943360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943331#post943331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Healthy Minds do not seek the Divine Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree, but it does leave a faint taste of texas sharpshooter fallacy in my mouth. Healthy minds do not seek the Divine Fire, therefore all who seek the Divine Fire must have unhealthy minds. A logically sound conclusion, but are the foundations it is drawn from sound? All it takes is one example of a healthy mind that would have reason to seek the Divine Fire to prove that they are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:00:28-07:00","id":943365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943356#post943356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, sorry, that first response was awfully snarky. I edited the first post with more than a quip.<br /> <br /> Second, I'd be happy to get on board with your take. I quite like your take. The Chronicles of Darkness have enough healthier ways to Transhumanism that I'd be perfectly happy if Pyros was for fucked up people, by fucked up people. But that's not what the book says. What the book says is that there are comparatively sane, altruistic alchemists who all somehow agree not to pursue.<br /> <br /> That is what I was ranting about.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I get there, I can more directly comment on the affair. I want the context* that builds to that discussion. As is, I'm dealing with the periphery here.<br /> <br /> Based on what I gather from the periphery, though, I don't think it's unfair to focus on those who are the more likely to have the Divine Fire call to them, that the moths among the alchemists are the ones focused on. These are the powers that this game runs on. The alchemists most likely to come across Prometheans are going to be screwed up, and willing to do <i>things</i> to get the Fire.<br /> <br /> Now, I get it-the text seems to lean heavily on &quot;Not desperate, merely assholes&quot;. I can't comment on that, because even though I have your comments, I haven't read the section it all fits into, and I don't know what I'm supposed to know prior to reading that for interpretation. I can go and argue speculations why it might come across like that ranging from construction issues to writer and developer tastes to narrative functions. When I have the picture, I might properly assert that.<br /> <br /> I don't. So, again, keep in mind-I am dealing with the periphery of the subject. I am not quite shooting at the heart of the matter when I comment.<br /> <br /> *I'm in the Complex Refinements, as an aside. It's gonna be a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:02:00-07:00","id":943367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943351#post943351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pendragon, if you have any sense of pattern-recognition whatsoever you will have noticed the tendency for going neck-deep into any given supernatural power source in this setting to have a causal relationship to or root origin in a beginning or developed lack of regard for caution when dealing with overwhelming powers that can and will try to eat you. The Shadow does it, the Underworld does it, the Fae do it, vampirism does it, and so on around the dinner table.<br /> <br /> Experienced dabblers who remain dabblers tend to do so as a conscious choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you didn't need the pattern recognition comment. That's a senseless attack and adds nothing and could really derail the conversation.<br /> <br /> Second, as stated above, I'm happy to accept that pyros is accessible only to crazy people. That's fine, well in line with the ChroD's other lines. But the book has to convey that. As is there is an entire sidebar that makes it aggressively clear that there are (and I'm legitimately quoting here) &quot;Sane, rational, and cautious alchemists&quot;. Page 257, I encourage everyone to read it. That sidebar covers an easy 90% of my issue. I'd prefer your interpretation be true, but the text is clear: sane alchemists exist, they desire knowledge, not power (a statement that caused me a to utter an audible &quot;dwaaaa?&quot;) and don't pursue Prometheans because <b>all</b> of them know that it's too dangerous. Despite Prometheans being, again I quote, &quot;a wealth of alchemical wisdom&quot; (also pg. 257).<br /> <br /> I hope you can at least see how this could be a source of frustration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:02:42-07:00","id":943368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943360#post943360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree, but it does leave a faint taste of texas sharpshooter fallacy in my mouth. Healthy minds do not seek the Divine Fire, therefore all who seek the Divine Fire must have unhealthy minds. A logically sound conclusion, but are the foundations it is drawn from sound? All it takes is one example of a healthy mind that would have reason to seek the Divine Fire to prove that they are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certain values of seek, with some seeking and others seeking and finding. Desperation drags.<br /> <br /> Again, lacking 2E context. Desperation may no longer be a hallmark of non-Promethean Divine Fire interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:34:16-07:00","id":943381,"title":"","content":"I feel like a lot of the frustration comes from the idea that only Alchemists (capital A) can use alchemy. From what I gathered... that's not true. Alchemists are simply those foolish enough to harness Pyros within themselves in order to achieve their goals (no matter the goal).<br /> <br /> You can be a scientist who stumbled upon alchemy and is now trying to understand what's going on.<br /> You can be an occult dabbler who learned how to brew a potion but you have no clue what &quot;Pyros&quot; is or how to distill it<br /> And you can be a cancerous, intelligent women who discovered the existence of Prometheans and decided that stealing the fire of life in order to become a goddess was a good idea. (Actual game I ran)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:41:43-07:00","id":943388,"title":"","content":"Oops, wrong thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:02:03-07:00","id":943403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943367#post943367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you didn't need the pattern recognition comment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prior experience demonstrates to the contrary, lest you forget the time you got so mad about Beast that you bolted a rule that already existed onto the Horror mechanics as a fix for something that wasn't broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, as stated above, I'm happy to accept that pyros is accessible only to crazy people. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Crazy&quot; is not an optimal choice of words for people who have lost some notable degree of control over themselves and/or their lives even if I were suggesting any phrase with an &quot;only&quot; in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As is there is an entire sidebar that makes it aggressively clear that there are (and I'm legitimately quoting here) &quot;Sane, rational, and cautious alchemists&quot;. Page 257, I encourage everyone to read it. </div> </div> </div>I would encourage <i>you</i> to read it, because you're committing the cardinal sin of this fandom and looking at the individual pieces without regard for the thing they're a part of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd prefer your interpretation be true, but the text is clear: sane alchemists exist, they desire knowledge, not power (a statement that caused me a to utter an audible &quot;dwaaaa?&quot;) </div> </div> </div>Waste less time on making noises and look at what the dabblers are being contrasted with.<br /> <br /> Alchemists who are trying to accomplish something drastic with the Pyros are after knowledge as an expression of a desire for power to do something rather than as a function of curiosity and a more casual desire to understand the world around them.<br /> <br /> The common idiom about the nature of knowledge does not make this distinction moot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and don't pursue Prometheans because <b>all</b> of them know that it's too dangerous. Despite Prometheans being, again I quote, &quot;a wealth of alchemical wisdom&quot; (also pg. 257). </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of geologists who don't take lava samples from active volcanoes even without the existence of volatile mountain-monsters who warp the world around them and anyone unlucky enough to live there. The Created are not, as a rule, safe people to be around even at their best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope you can at least see how this could be a source of frustration? </div> </div> </div>The company this matter keeps in the collection of Things PenDragon Has &quot;Gotten Frustrated&quot; About does very little to render this a compelling point in your favor.<br /> <br /> Turn off the Hacking Goggles on your baseline consumption of the material, read without preconception, and refrain from attributing motivations to the text that only serve to agitate you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:46:37-07:00","id":943425,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Civility please. That's an awful lot of personal attacks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:53:44-07:00","id":943427,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Satchel, that was completely inappropriate. I'm issuing you a suspension, and I highly recommend examining the way you communicate with other members on this site. This is not the first time you've been disrespectful to other users, and I would hate for your continuing curt attitude to lead to the banning of an otherwise highly valued member of this community.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:59:58-07:00","id":943432,"title":"","content":"Warning: I've only skimmed the thread, so much of what I'm about to say may already have been addressed. With that in mind:<br /> <br /> My initial impression of the Alchemists section is that it's <i>not</i> saying \u201call, or even most, alchemists are power-hungry horrors\u201d; it's saying \u201cmost alchemists <i>that Prometheans are likely to encounter</i> are power-hungry horrors\u201d. That's why it coins the term \u201cInsatiate\u201d (i.e., one with a hunger that cannot be satisfied). <br /> <br /> That said, it occurs to me that there's a perfectly viable role for non-Insatiate alchemists in a <b>Promethean</b> chronicle; and it's one that was touched on way back in <b>Promethean 1e</b>'s <i>Water of Life</i> story: the alchemist as mentor. Similar in some ways to the role that Elpidos are designed to fill, but with a much more human face and less of a <i>deus ex machina</i> aspect to it. <br /> <br /> Granted, they're playing with fire; but by definition, the non-Insatiate alchemists do so with due caution. And unless they're also Redeemed who chose to retain their memories, they're probably well-meaning bumblers who know about as much about the Pilgrimage as an Extempore does, and are likely to be as much a hindrance as a help. But these are plot fodder \u2014 reasons to incorporate them into a chronicle rather than to dismiss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T02:15:49-07:00","id":943494,"title":"","content":"Asking again: is there any way for alchemist to produce Pyros without hunting down Prometheans, even if costly and /or inefficient ( like dr. Frankenstein from storms in the book ) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-04-2016, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T02:28:09-07:00","id":943497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943494#post943494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking again: is there any way for alchemist to produce Pyros without hunting down Prometheans, even if costly and /or inefficient ( like dr. Frankenstein from storms in the book ) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if I am wrong, but wouldn't this essentially be a demiurge you're asking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T02:31:19-07:00","id":943500,"title":"","content":"Yes. Their Potency stat, \u201cMagnitude\u201d, determines how much Pyros they can use per turn (1 or maybe 2), how much Pyros they can store in alchemical reagents at any given time (5 to 9), and how quickly they can replenish their stocks (1 to 3 Pyros/week). Pyros stolen from Prometheans doesn't count toward these limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:30:24-07:00","id":943520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943323#post943323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A splendidly reasonable scenario, and one the text fully enables. Let me try one it hampers.<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, hunted by this desperate, haunted man at least as disquieting as yourself. Being used to people trying to murder you, and finding yourself in a rare position to converse with this clearly Disquiet riddled soul. What he reveals to you is not the standard &quot;I want to be more&quot; spiel. As it turns out the mans child, a 4 year old babe just headed for kindergarden, suffers an incurable ailment. Science has failed him, common Alchemy failed him, Vitriol is the only hope she has left. Do you gamble your vitriol on another? Or do you let the child die?<br /> <br /> That take on Alchemists is one I'd very much like to see. A presentation in which Transhumanism seems an enticing option. Later the child could go all pandoran and devour her father, or some similar backlash to prove that humanism is #1, or not, perhaps it could be the impetus that drives the Prommie doesn the Centimanus path (to his ruin). So much possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see how the text precludes it. Easy enough scenario to come up with if you're good at coming up with morally grey scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:58:23-07:00","id":943546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943226#post943226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily, the Alchemist section doesn't seem to be so bad as to make me outright uncomfortable the same way Beast did. The association of evil alchemists with mental illness is deeply troubling, and seems to arbitrarily rule out any plausible justification an Alchemist might have for their actions, but at least the authorial voice isn't oozing with vitriol (heh) towards their subject this time. I'll likely end up portraying Alchemists a little bit differently in my own games, but hey, that's the point of an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I thought about this a lot last night at work. To summarize:<ul><li>I agree that Alchemists should be presented as primarily an antagonist, but their portrayal as unsympathetic villains does the game a massive injustice.</li> </ul><br /> Good villains are sympathetic.* It inherently makes them complex which means, in a sense, they get more word-count, but that's a weird aside. Sympathetic villains make us want to <i>play</i> them so we can explore their perspective.<br /> <br /> Seers are no bullshit evil because they sold their souls to cosmic symbols of tyrannical oppression, but they're <i>Mages</i> just like us. We're one step away from that. Centimanni are monsters except they've given up hope on the Pilgrimage which, hey, is really tough. They're disillusioned and bitter, but we're just like them. We're one step away from that.<br /> <br /> Alchemists are in a weird spot. Unsympathetic villains do have their place but 1) irredeemable <i>mortals</i> in the <b>CofD</b> are pretty non-existant and 2) Pandorans cover this niche anyway because <i>they eat your face</i>. Alchemists are <i>human</i>, you know, the thing every Promethean wants to be. They deserve nuance, they deserve moral greyness. They should show that the human world Prometheans desperately want to join has a wide spectrum of morality. Their motives are such a so-good-how-did-I-not-think-of-them-first that it's shocking they're written like a brick.<br /> <br /> How is it that Alchemists written as being crazed by lust for the Divine Fire is okay but it's not okay for <b>Beast</b>'s Heroes to be driven to murder by a Beast's Astral rampages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:23:14-07:00","id":943669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943432#post943432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, they're playing with fire; but by definition, the non-Insatiate alchemists do so with due caution. And unless they're also Redeemed who chose to retain their memories, they're probably well-meaning bumblers who know about as much about the Pilgrimage as an Extempore does, and are likely to be as much a hindrance as a help. But these are plot fodder \u2014 reasons to incorporate them into a chronicle rather than to dismiss them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with 'Sane' Alchemist is that we make false White and <b>b</b>lack dichotomy - as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> mentioned few times, even those well meaning <i>should</i>, sooner or later, end looking for Prometheans as Vitriol fodders, <b>especially</b> if Divine Fire is known to make people unhinged.<br /> <br /> Really, we should have two possible, realistic models for Alchemists - 'They all are Grey' ( and have complex motivations, not truly egoistic, not truly altruistic ) or 'They all are Black' ( and showing that Divine Fire just lead <i>all</i> people to madness ). / Myself, I'm all more on first Grey take on them. /<br /> <br /> We <b>cannot</b> have the same situation like with Heroes in that 'we have good ones, but we also have minority that is really bad' as Alchemists, from setting standpoint, are not doing something truly noble - at best they are study arcane discipline ( neutral ), at worse they are harvesting Prometheans ( very bad ). When we add Divine Fire to the mix, split on White and Black Alchemists is just <b>unrealistic</b>. It could work made if most of White Alchemists are Redeemed and somehow sheltered from Divine Fire, but I suspect it's really almost non-existing case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:28:13-07:00","id":943675,"title":"","content":"*bold emphasis and capitals mine<br /> <br /> So, I've been following this thread since last night, and have been interested in it enough that I've jumped ahead in my reading to the Alchemists section to hopefully contribute. Now, here's where I have to put a bit of a disclaimer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant#post943084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trigger Warning: This is not a very positive post.<br /> <br /> Now I get that this book is called Promethean, not Alchemist, and that the Created are the core focus. I also get that painting a picture of Prommies being buddy-buddy with Alchemists flies in the face of the whole isolationist theme. But does the book really need to flaunt that? Does it really need to commit word count to shutting down any possibility of non-antagonistic Alchemists. It probably wouldn't bother me as much if the book wasn't so outright about the exclusion. Like, if the text just said, &quot;there are less extreme Alchemists, but this is the Antagonists section so we're going to focus on the ones who are definitive villain material.&quot; That, in my eyes, would be a better handling that saying outright that &quot;sane&quot; alchemists never target Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Indeed even that statement is contradictory as the book goes on to explain that Prometheans are invaluable sources of knowledge, which all Alchemists seek (even the 'good' ones), and that the Created are rare enough that many aspiring Alchemists will never meet one. Plus there is disquiet, which would draw them in against their will regardless. <b>It just doesn't add up, the explanations all read like flimsy excuses for why <b>ALL</b>* Alchemists Prometheans meet should be evil psychopaths. It's a my way or the highway sort of vibe, that I can't help but feel is a deliberate shutdown of everyone who wanted to see Alchemists as a viable subsplat.</b><br /> <br /> Or perhaps it's just me, maybe I'm the only one reading it that way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR - Pendragon is irritated about the handling of alchemists. Also the sky is blue, and water is wet. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really have a hard time understanding how this is your take-away from the reading.<br /> <br /> Over and over again on the opening page alone for Alchemists the book caveats that the 'nice' Alchemists are the ones Prometheans are least likely to meet, but that it can and does happen, albeit very rarely. It's just that, since this is the antagonist section that's the aspect and organization they're going to focus on. I'm not getting any sense of being punished (which is how your post made it seem you felt) for incorporating the non-homicidal kind, or that Alchemists can't have complex motivations. It's just that's rare and not the focus of this section, so it'll be left up to ST discretion. Which to me says that means its up to your group how you want to define 'rare' I myself for instance have never been comfortable with the notion that there are only 100 Prometheans worldwide, so I tick that number up in my head. I don't feel dissuaded as a reader from doing so.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is, after reading the section, I feel like your impression is really selective. I don't mean to be insulting, but am I making sense? Should I provide quotes from the text explaining why I feel this way? Do you think I'm off my rocker, how so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 08-04-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:59:56-07:00","id":943719,"title":"","content":"In any case, how dangerous is an alchemist as antagonist for a Promethean? I'm not talking about a rich guy who can afford hiring professional thugs, expert tracking detectives and costly security systems, but your average university professor with a research grant. <br /> I'm asking because I still remember back when I read the rules for Heroes and thought &quot;so, these are the guys who are supposed to bring down Beasts? Pffff...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-04-2016, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T11:08:28-07:00","id":943725,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1705_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1705\" data-vbnamecard=\"1705\">Okami</a>: So, after reading your post, I went and did the same. Read through the Alchemist section, skimming a bit at parts, but trying to develop my understanding within the context of their presentation in the book. Here are my own thoughts.<br /> <br /> On the whole, I really like the section. But I do wish the presentation of Insensate Alchemists' motivations was a bit more nuanced. There's a lot of focus on the hatred of the human condition, but precious little dedicated to the fear that drives that self-hate. Or the ambition not just to abandon humanity but to improve upon it. I am down with Promethean's humanistic themes and understand why it would want to portray such inherently transhumanist characters in a negative light, but I feel the message would be considerably more powerful if the deeply human drives that can turn people towards Insensate Alchemy were made clearer.<br /> <br /> The Alchemists and Their Prey section <i>almost</i> does what I'm looking for when it talks about Alchemists as tragic antagonists and points out that the theme is made stronger if the Alchemist doesn't start out wanting to kill the throng. But then instead of exploring the possibility of an Alchemist villain who goes from sympathetic to Insensate over the course of play, it presents an example of an Alchemist who wanted to kill the throng all along, but pretended not to at first to earn their trust. That's not a tragic antagonist, that's a one-dimensional antagonist pretending to be sympathetic as part of his nefarious scheme.<br /> <br /> The other part I didn't care for was the Great Work sidebar. I think it comes from a good place. I understand and appreciate the attempt to explain that while not all Alchemists murder Prometheans for Pyros or Vitriol, the ones that are most likely to play an important role in a Promethean game do, so that's what this section is going to focus on. The core idea behind the sidebar is great. My beef with it (complaints about prepetuating the stigmatization of mental illness aside) is that it sets up a dichotomy between cautious, rational alchemists who don't kill Prometheans and therefore aren't covered in this section, and power-hungry, Vitriol-crazed alchemists who do kill Prometheans. It doesn't leave room for otherwise rational, cautious alchemists who are driven to kill a Promethean out of desperate circumstances, or those just starting down the slippery slope towards becoming Insensate, nor for corrupt extreme-transhumanists who would have no compunctions about killing Prometheans but lack the opportunity, or the means, or those who's fear of the power Prometheans wield just barely outweighs their hatred of the human condition. The classification of Alchemists who kill Prometheans as Insensate and the attempt to explain why only the Insensate are covered in this book is appreciated, but the lack of nuance in the analsys of what constitutes an Insensate Alchemist is disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-04-2016, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:19:42-07:00","id":943771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943725#post943725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1705_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1705\" data-vbnamecard=\"1705\">Okami</a>: So, after reading your post, I went and did the same. Read through the Alchemist section, skimming a bit at parts, but trying to develop my understanding within the context of their presentation in the book. Here are my own thoughts.<br /> <br /> On the whole, I really like the section. But I do wish the presentation of Insensate Alchemists' motivations was a bit more nuanced. There's a lot of focus on the hatred of the human condition, but precious little dedicated to the fear that drives that self-hate. Or the ambition not just to abandon humanity but to improve upon it. I am down with Promethean's humanistic themes and understand why it would want to portray such inherently transhumanist characters in a negative light, but I feel the message would be considerably more powerful if the deeply human drives that can turn people towards Insensate Alchemy were made clearer.<br /> <br /> The Alchemists and Their Prey section <i>almost</i> does what I'm looking for when it talks about Alchemists as tragic antagonists and points out that the theme is made stronger if the Alchemist doesn't start out wanting to kill the throng. But then instead of exploring the possibility of an Alchemist villain who goes from sympathetic to Insensate over the course of play, it presents an example of an Alchemist who wanted to kill the throng all along, but pretended not to at first to earn their trust. That's not a tragic antagonist, that's a one-dimensional antagonist pretending to be sympathetic as part of his nefarious scheme.<br /> <br /> The other part I didn't care for was the Great Work sidebar. I think it comes from a good place. I understand and appreciate the attempt to explain that while not all Alchemists murder Prometheans for Pyros or Vitriol, the ones that are most likely to play an important role in a Promethean game do, so that's what this section is going to focus on. The core idea behind the sidebar is great. My beef with it (complaints about prepetuating the stigmatization of mental illness aside) is that it sets up a dichotomy between cautious, rational alchemists who don't kill Prometheans and therefore aren't covered in this section, and power-hungry, Vitriol-crazed alchemists who do kill Prometheans. It doesn't leave room for otherwise rational, cautious alchemists who are driven to kill a Promethean out of desperate circumstances, or those just starting down the slippery slope towards becoming Insensate, nor for corrupt extreme-transhumanists who would have no compunctions about killing Prometheans but lack the opportunity, or the means, or those who's fear of the power Prometheans wield just barely outweighs their hatred of the human condition. The classification of Alchemists who kill Prometheans as Insensate and the attempt to explain why only the Insensate are covered in this book is appreciated, but the lack of nuance in the analsys of what constitutes an Insensate Alchemist is disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First off, I'm my post made you take a second look at the material, that means a lot, so thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm going to try tackling this bit by bit;<br /> <br /> Paragraph 1) I think that clarity was provided in certain sections, but more on that next.<br /> <br /> Paragraph 2) I lied, I think I need to roll all this into one and tackle it.<br /> <br /> The Thing) Ok, Your reading, whether its the sidebar or in general, seems to want a more nuanced take on the motivations of the Alchemists, Promethean killers or not. A few things here, first I would argue the example NPC is a good one of someone driven by their desperation to do terrible things. She's a deeply damaged cancer survivor, and fears both re-occurrence of the disease and now other signs of death so deeply that she is now willing to torture and kill beings that aren't human to stop it. I think that's a good mix of 'your evil as all get-out, but I can understand what drove you to this'. In terms of how you think it sets up a dichotomy I again took it as dichotomy only so far as the focus of this sections goes. The writing makes it clear there <b>are</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943725#post943725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">otherwise rational, cautious alchemists who are driven to kill a Promethean out of desperate circumstances, or those just starting down the slippery slope towards becoming Insensate <b>et. al</b></div> </div> </div> </div>*<br /> <br /> *bold and et. al mine<br /> <br /> They just aren't discussed here. That, I think, is where you and I primarily differ. You view that discussion, the one left out, as the one that's more compelling and interesting, and want to see it, and think the book would be better if it had that instead, or in addition to whats there.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily agree with this, and here's why, first I'll cover the 'instead' notion. I think it's important to cover villains seen as villains, so long as you caveat along the way that its not this black and white and simple. I think the book does that throughout, letting you know the somewhat simplistic picture they're painting isn't the whole thing, but it is an important and necessary part they need to cover. That leads to the natural response 'why not make the game better then and give us both? Tell us how they're villains but explore those grey areas, give that more nuanced view in addition to the villain-y picture we get wouldn't that make it better?'<br /> <br /> In short, I do think that's right, it would, so why don't I have a problem with it not happening and in fact seem opposed to readings calling for just that? One main reason; practicality. At the end of the day this book had a limited word count the writer's had to work with, and including more on the Alchemists meant sacrificing elsewhere. Given that this is the Core Book for the new Promethean line I think the focus needed to be kept where its at, on the Prometheans and how they see and experience their Pilgrimage and their Great Work. A more nuanced view would have been better in presentation perhaps, but would have detracted, due to word count, on the villainous perspective that the Prometheans themselves experience, and as you yourself pointed out has so many rich variations to explore it likely wouldn't have done itself justice. Hence the approach the book took and one I agree with. Keep the focus tightened down on the Promethean experience, as simplistic as that might be for these complex villains, but let the players know there's a wealth of gray for them to explore. That exploration though, we'll need to leave up to them until some other books come out perhaps.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the wall of text, hope all that's clear. If you'd like to go into anything like the importance of the more simplistic villainous view as it is in the core book let me know, same if any of this is confusing or doesn't seem to add up, its a lot and I want to be clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:55:46-07:00","id":943797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943257#post943257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the very idea of &amp;quot;madness&amp;quot; is a little ableist. Obviously it isn't always when it's handled responsibly, but doing so requires a great deal of care and intentionality. It's one thing to say that Alchemists regularly deal with powers that are dangerous for the human mind and as a result often end up traumatized and/or mentally scarred. It's another thing to call all the Alchemists who don't murder perople for their spare parts &amp;quot;sane&amp;quot;. Doing so implies by contrast that all the ones that do murder people for their spare parts are &amp;quot;insane&amp;quot;, and paints a picture of the world where mentally healthy people are not murderous and mentally ill people are. Which apart from being untrue on both counts contributes to an ongoing stigma about mental illness, where people with visible mental illness are to be feared and people without visible mental illness are to be trusted. The RPG industry has a long history of stigmatizing mental illness, and in general CofD 2e has made great strides to remedy that. <i>Particularly</i> in products that David Hill has been involved in. But there are still lingering issues with the RPG idea of &amp;quot;madness&amp;quot; being perpetuated, particularly in Mage and Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry I can't see anyone chopping up people being sane, something has to be wrong, its against healthy human nature.<br /> <br /> For the record I don't concider people with mental health problems as insane, having OCD or depression doesn't make you insane.<br /> <br /> Insane is were you're mental illnesses have reached the point where you are violent and dangerous to others.<br /> <br /> I have experienced my own mental health issues such as depression, suicidal thoughts, and I a variety of pyscholical issues, nothing major, but I do not seriously concider myself insane, as I'm not an uncontrolable threat of voilence to those around me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:59:08-07:00","id":943800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943797#post943797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I can't see anyone chopping up people being sane, something has to be wrong, its against healthy human nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever taken apart a computer?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:16:26-07:00","id":943809,"title":"","content":"Playing an Alcemist in a Changeling, Beast, or Mage game instead of Prommie avoids most of these issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:18:15-07:00","id":943810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943800#post943800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever taken apart a computer?</div> </div> </div> </div> A computer is not a human being, heck at our current tech level its not even a self aware being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:23:32-07:00","id":943814,"title":"","content":"Or hunter.<br /> <br /> As much as the book tries to portray Prometheans as would-be saints and alchemists as hand-wringing evil-doers, Prometheans are monsters that lie, cheat, steal and murder. We already have two hunter groups about stealing powers from monsters, alchemists practically fit as another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943810#post943810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A computer is not a human being, heck at our current tech level its not even a self aware being</div> </div> </div> </div>Either is a Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:30:33-07:00","id":943823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943814#post943814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or hunter.<br /> <br /> As much as the book tries to portray Prometheans as would-be saints and alchemists as hand-wringing evil-doers, Prometheans are monsters that lie, cheat, steal and murder. We already have two hunter groups about stealing powers from monsters, alchemists practically fit as another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Either is a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>A computer doesn't bleed, scream, and beg you to stop killing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:43:45-07:00","id":943837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943823#post943823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A computer doesn't bleed, scream, and beg you to stop killing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but an Unfleshed 'bleeds' oil and might not scream or beg you to stop killing it so much as start throwing fireballs. Remember, while a Promethean feels pain, it doesn't debilitate them the way it does living creatures.<br /> <br /> We kill animals, too, that don't like it, to make sure people have food on the table. It's grisly, but it's not insane.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, too, have the Savage, Vigilante, and Psychopomp roles. These all involve killing people or letting them die when you could have helped. Fulfilling these acts are a step forward on their Pilgrimage. As far as I can see, there's no special caveat that if the person they're killing bleeds, screams, or begs for you to stop killing it, it doesn't count.<br /> <br /> A Promethean is expected to do certain things because it helps them on their journey. An alchemist on their own journey is an awful entity.<br /> <br /> The buy-in for the game is made very clear, and was made clear months ago. It's about humanism, the goods and the bads. Except then we get a section portraying the bads in the form of alchemists and they're just wrong for it. The game goes a good distance in reaffirming the humanism angle by pointing out how disgusting Prometheans consider Centimani. The stereotypes about them make Prometheans out to be like the cast of Mean Girls, and they're called 'freaks,' for standing outside of the race for humanity. In all I think the book could have gone a bit lighter on the 'any who oppose this is wrong,' especially when the first chapters manage to get across so well the whys of humanism and the Pilgrimage for Prometheans. Painting the antagonists as awful is an understandable in-world angle for Prometheans, but when you're getting things across to players and storytellers it comes off a bit heavy-handed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:06:01-07:00","id":943854,"title":"","content":"While I don't have anything meaningful to add to debate on whether or not the Alchemist section spends enough time on the &quot;grey&quot; areas or not. I see both sides. The practicality of what belongs in a core books vs. compelling things that would be fun to explore doesn't have a good solution.<br /> <br /> I have to say though... as someone that's not neuro-typical... all the point complaining about &quot;ableism,&quot; here have made me feel far, far, worse about my mental status than anything in Beast or Promethean 2e has printed. Sanity is not a mental health diagnosis, it's a legal ruling, and conflating them doesn't help in any way. It doesn't help writers create more nuanced games. It doesn't help larger societal issues. Sanity is an issue of being able to appreciate the consequences of your actions; which my diagnosis doesn't impact at all. It intersects of neuro-atypical issues, but they aren't the same thing. &quot;Crazy&quot; and &quot;mad&quot; are similarly not diagnostic criteria, or mental health conditions. Sane, crazy, and mad, are not in the DSM or ICD, because they have nothing to do with psychology, psychiatry, or actually helping people that have real mental health conditions.<br /> <br /> I don't need defending against a game describing antagonists that have gone off the deep end in pursuit of an irrational path, with morally dubious methods, using terms that intersect with how poorly society discusses actual important issues. Nothing in the book has any relevance to things like the fact that every time I apply for a job, I need to decide if I want to opt to exercise my right to not disclose my mental health issues and possibly get the job but not have any assistance is (very simple) accommodations my employer could make to help me be a productive employee (and of course they're going to find out anyway, and living in a state where you can be fired very easily despite supposed protections &quot;lying&quot; isn't a great idea), or disclose and then risk not getting the job because I just gave them a subconscious reason to put me to the bottom of the pile regardless of my qualifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:14:17-07:00","id":943861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943837#post943837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but an Unfleshed 'bleeds' oil and might not scream or beg you to stop killing it so much as start throwing fireballs. Remember, while a Promethean feels pain, it doesn't debilitate them the way it does living creatures.<br /> <br /> We kill animals, too, that don't like it, to make sure people have food on the table. It's grisly, but it's not insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We recognize your species as a sentient one, and treat you more fairly than you do your livestock. We always make sure to get your assent and trade with you fairly&quot;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, that's <i>Kyubey</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:27:09-07:00","id":943876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943861#post943861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;We recognize your species as a sentient one, and treat you more fairly than you do your livestock. We always make sure to get your assent and trade with you fairly&quot;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, that's <i>Kyubey</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't get past the second episode. Relevance?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:35:52-07:00","id":943888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943546#post943546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it that Alchemists written as being crazed by lust for the Divine Fire is okay but it's not okay for <b>Beast</b>'s Heroes to be driven to murder by a Beast's Astral rampages?</div> </div> </div> </div>The word that separates them is sympathy. Heroes, as Beast goes out of its way to tell us, are supposed to be unsympathetic. Beyond being ridiculously bad writing advice, it is simply wrong, there's no such thing as an unsympathetic human. Hence the presentation of heroes is something I cannot stand. Alchemists, despite several instances where the book cuts very close towards the Hero approach, are deeply sympathetic character, driven by a common fear we all share, and acting in groups to justify themselves. That's a much more compelling, realistic take.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943675#post943675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I'm saying is, after reading the section, I feel like your impression is really selective. I don't mean to be insulting, but am I making sense? Should I provide quotes from the text explaining why I feel this way? Do you think I'm off my rocker, how so?</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense taken. I <b>am</b> being selective, because my issue comes from a very select portion of the text: sane alchemists. Notably the Great Works sidebar.<br /> <br /> I find it extremely artificial that somehow all 'sane' alchemists somehow &quot;know better&quot; (how?). It's unrealistic, since when has the threat of danger been a hard stop to knowledge seekers? Some, for sure, but <b>all of them</b>? Where are the Promethean run ins with wide eyed youths who believe they can brave the dangers and befriend the monsters? Where are the 'sane' organizations committed to protecting Prometheans (as they are &quot;wealths of alchemical wisdom&quot;), but being gradually undermined by disquiet and wasteland? Where are the Alchemists who are mid fall, slipping towards Insensate but not yet there? Where are the Alchemists pursuing transhumanism for altruistic goals?<br /> <br /> I'd have been totally willing to accept slight different explanations, such as: &quot;Prometheans are so rare that the only Alchemists who can routinely find them are also those who have been screwed hardest by Disquiet&quot;. Or: &quot;Divine Lightning does not strike the stable mind, an individual must be on the path to abandoning their humanity before Alchemy even becomes possible.&quot; Or even: &quot;Many of the worst Alchemical groups started off with good intentions, but were warped through by time, vitriol and disquiet into the grotesques they are today.&quot; Though I'd have best accepted: &quot;Alchemists are manifold individuals, not all are calloused skinners of the Created. What we are showcasing here are merely the worst offenders, to give readers some idea of just how bad an Alchemist can get.&quot;<br /> <br /> But instead we get the Great Work sidebar. Charliquin already did a great job of capturing the issue. Indeed his explanation is clearer than any I an think up at this time. So I'll stop here, but I hope you can at least see where I'm coming from now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-04-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:45:49-07:00","id":943895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943876#post943876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't get past the second episode. Relevance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Madoka Spoilers<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Kyubey basically ticks young girls into becoming magical girls so that they will become witches inevitably and release a greater amount of energy than went into changing them. At one point, Kyubey makes mention of how the relationship between humans and livestock works, with some grisly sacrifices actually ensuring the health, well being, and propogation of the rest of the species. Kyubey then goes on to say that line.<br /> <br /> Kyubey is a cold, purely rational creature who shows the cruelty inherent in such a being, exploiting girls and fighting a basically unsolvable position by throwing them into misery-but even it shows a better level of...decorum than alchemists. It's not justified when the devil rat has better manners/ethics, I suppose is my point.<br /> <br /> Now, that might be how alchemists view Prometheans, particularly given Disquiet-but that doesn't make it all right. It's very clearly wrong</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now, how that relates to the larger picture is...still not on the table, I'm still reading. If the argument is that alchemists are portrayed too harshly, then this frame of mind that surely happens with alchemists doesn't help that argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:47:36-07:00","id":943898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant#post943084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's a my way or the highway sort of vibe, that I can't help but feel is a deliberate shutdown of everyone who wanted to</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of fertile plot points in that middle ground, challenging stories about humanity, that go down the drain when you throw away the possibility of friendly (or at least non-murderous) Alchemists.<br /> <br /> Again though, let me make this clear, my beef is not with the many fucked up Alchemical societies presented in the book. Those are fine. It's exclusively with the book's often black-and-white presentation of the subsplat. Mind you, the book (thankfully) doesn't shoehorn in rules to prevent them, but the text irked me enough that I had to say something. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me it's a mixed bag. Prommie has always been to me a flawed diamond, with lots of squandered potential. Plus I hack the shit out of everything I run, so take what I say with a grain of salt.<ul><li>The Bestowments are cool, as are the different flavors of Torment. I'll be subbing out a DIY Lineage system for what I consider an excessively restrictive set of X-splats, but I don't like X-Splats in general so that's probably me.</li> <li>Transmutations are largely fine, a couple I feel need tweaking, but that's fairly high praise from my camp. They are a definitive step up from 1e, that's for sure, and give Prommies a nice powerset at a level that doesn't jeopardize their themes (Mage supremacists will no doubt be pleased to hear).</li> <li>There are a lot of subsystems built in to help players along in the game, from Roles to Milstones, to their Vice/Virtue analogs. Though the milage of that may vary I'm personally not fond of such clearly directed gameplay, but others may enjoy the sense of direction.</li> <li>I could do without Centimanus being presented as antagonists, a more nuanced approach (like the Seers received in Awakening 2e) would have been appreciated. But I knew better than to expect one.</li> <li>Firestorm rules are cool. They weren't something I had any idea what to do with, so the book provided great direction there.</li> <li>Can't comment on the storytelling or regional chapters too much.</li> <li>Weirdly I think the game perhaps puts too much emphasis on the New Dawn. It is so prevalent that I fear players (especially new ones) will prioritize hitting milestones and racing too humanity over digging into the story and giving real life to their character.</li> <li>All in all I'd give it maybe 3 of 5 stars. &quot;Good for what it is intended for, but too restrictive for much else.&quot; Mind you, this is all based off power skimming, and the joint reading of myself and a friend. Bottom line though, anyone who loved Prommie 1e will probably enjoy 2e, anyone who didn't will probably continue to dislike the game.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat is a great way to describe how I, and literally every player I know IRL, feel about P1E; and what <i>seems</i> to be the prevailing attitude on these forums is that*:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> If you like some/most of the rules for P:tC, but think that the downsides are too heavy handed to be much fun, then,<span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b> YOU ARE WRONG! YOU ARE A HORRIBLE PERSON, WHO SHOULD NOT BE ALLOWED TO REPRODUCE! YOUR IDEAS ARE BAD, AND YOU SHOULD FEEL BAD! DIE IN A FIRE! DIE,DIE,DIE,DIE!!!!!!!!!!</b></span> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *Spoilered, because I'm actually NOT trying to turn this thread into a flaming mess, but the hostility towards the very <i>NOTION</i> of wanting to have Created beings that can actually form meaningful, lasting relationships outside their own splat, or that perhaps <u>ALTERNATIVES</u> to becoming a non-supernatural in the World/Chronicles of Darkness would have been nice, has made me a bit...cranky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-15-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:51:17-07:00","id":943902,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying people don't do that, but I might suggest, that even with the hammering that happens, you have still managed to overblow the response.<br /> <br /> But whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:56:48-07:00","id":943908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943296#post943296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, a few years into you Pilgrimage; you understand some things about humanity, you know what sets you apart from it, and your days are spent striving towards becoming it. You come across a human being - a real human being, born into glorious normalcy with a genuine soul - who wants to kill you for the fire inside you. Somehow things reach a point where the two of you talk about things, and when you ask them why they want to steal your flame, they explain that they want to become more, become stronger and smarter and immortal and to surpass the circumstances of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would find that infuriating. Here's some jerk who has everything you've ever wanted by no virtue or effort of their own other than a luckier origin than you're own, and they're not happy with it. They want more. They want to leave being human (magnificently human!) for another state of being, and worse, they want to kill you to fuel it.<br /> <br /> You don't need &quot;Pyros drives them hopeless maaaaaaaad!&quot; for that to be an incredible point of ohilosophical contention in a game about the beauty of basic fundamental humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, baring the objective statement that humanity really is special and superior, the Promethean is expressing a very flaw reasoning. They are ignoring the point of view of the Alchemist and presuming to know the value of being human better than the human does. They would seem to be so blinded by their want and greed for the green grass of the other side that they are rejecting any potential points the would-be transhumanist has.<br /> <br /> It's only defensible in Promethean because the game itself makes that objective statement. But I'm not sure Prometheans know that. Making it so &quot;Pyros and Vitriol unbalance the mortal mind&quot; is far more easily justified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:57:27-07:00","id":943909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943902#post943902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying people don't do that, but I might suggest, that even with the hammering that happens, you have still managed to overblow the response.<br /> <br /> But whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not certain if this was aimed at me? Regardless I think I've said my peace, I'm headed to the hacking room to make playable Alchemists. Thanks to the book, this looks to be shockingly simple, yay!<br /> <br /> Before that, I would like to go a tad off topic to thank and commend everyone for managing to go this many posts, on a topic that is <b>clearly</b> divisive, and remain entirely cordial the whole way through. I was positive this thread would have been locked by page 2. I'll go out and say that no one managed to change my mind, but I appreciate the reasoned arguments offered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i>