09#post943909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not certain if this was aimed at me? Regardless I think I've said my peace, I'm headed to the hacking room to make playable Alchemists. Thanks to the book, this looks to be shockingly simple, yay!<br /> <br /> Before that, I would like to go a tad off topic to thank and commend everyone for managing to go this many posts, on a topic that is <b>clearly</b> divisive, and remain entirely cordial the whole way through. I was positive this thread would have been locked by page 2. I'll go out and say that no one managed to change my mind, but I appreciate the reasoned arguments offered.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was aimed at Mangle. Mangle was the one I had previously ranted at","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:06:02-07:00","id":943921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943909#post943909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not certain if this was aimed at me? Regardless I think I've said my peace, I'm headed to the hacking room to make playable Alchemists. Thanks to the book, this looks to be shockingly simple, yay!<br /> <br /> Before that, I would like to go a tad off topic to thank and commend everyone for managing to go this many posts, on a topic that is <b>clearly</b> divisive, and remain entirely cordial the whole way through. I was positive this thread would have been locked by page 2. I'll go out and say that no one managed to change my mind, but I appreciate the reasoned arguments offered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Civility is a virtue. I'm happy for this thread's existence even if I disagree with you on some points, and a reasonable discussion is a healthy thing to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:07:06-07:00","id":943922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943902#post943902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying people don't do that, but I might suggest, that even with the hammering that happens, you have still managed to overblow the response.<br /> <br /> But whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bHyperbole is the lifeblood of Internet discourse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:12:02-07:00","id":943925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943922#post943922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHyperbole is the lifeblood of Internet discourse.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the bloodclots of already heated discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:56:40-07:00","id":943957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943925#post943925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the bloodclots of already heated discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bTouch\u00e9'! Nonetheless, I think you can see my point; the RAW for this game makes it a hard sell, even for people who like the material that was it's inspiration. The reactions to houserule/homebrew topics is disproportionately hostile. If you <u>LOVE</u> the RAW, great! But not everyone does. I've been thinking about starting a new thread, to brainstorm my Diogenean concept, but I'm concerned at least 2 people(I won't name names) in this very thread will immediately show up and crap the whole thing, making a toxic mess that gets locked after about 3 posts. There really isn't any other place on these forums for those of us who find P:tC ALMOST playable to discus what we would change, so if someone doesn't like the idea of alternatives, it would be far more kind and courteous to simply stay out of such threads, instead of acting like they <b>OWN</b> these forums, and trying to discus transhumanist ideas in a positive way is somehow &quot;trespassing&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T17:04:09-07:00","id":944007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943771#post943771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thing) Ok, Your reading, whether its the sidebar or in general, seems to want a more nuanced take on the motivations of the Alchemists, Promethean killers or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a fair assessment of my stance. With the addendum that I understand and accept that there's not space to discuss non-Promethean-killing Alchemists (nuanced or otherwise). I don't think that means the discussion of the Promethean-killing Alchemists can't present a nuanced take on <i>their</i> motivations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943771#post943771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things here, first I would argue the example NPC is a good one of someone driven by their desperation to do terrible things. She's a deeply damaged cancer survivor, and fears both re-occurrence of the disease and now other signs of death so deeply that she is now willing to torture and kill beings that aren't human to stop it. I think that's a good mix of 'your evil as all get-out, but I can understand what drove you to this'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, she's a fantastic example of the nuanced antagonists I believe Alchemists have the potential to be. The thing is, I don't think she's consistent with the way Alchemists are presented in the rest of the section. She's motivated by fear and desperation, not by hunger for power and hatred of the human condition. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> that it reads like there are conflicting goals contributing to the writing, of trying to present Insensate Alchemists both as characters with believable motivations, and simultaneously trying to present them as irredeemable and unsympathetic monsters. I don't know if writer/developer conflict was the cause or not, but one way or another, it shows through that the text is simultaneously trying to present all Insensate Alchemists as humanity-hating madmen, and as tragic antagonists, and it doesn't come together in a coherent way for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943771#post943771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of how you think it sets up a dichotomy I again took it as dichotomy only so far as the focus of this sections goes. The writing makes it clear there <b>are</b><br /> <br /> *<br /> *bold and et. al mine<br /> <br /> They just aren't discussed here. That, I think, is where you and I primarily differ. You view that discussion, the one left out, as the one that's more compelling and interesting, and want to see it, and think the book would be better if it had that instead, or in addition to whats there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that it does make that clear. It says that rational, sane Alchemists aren't discussed here because Promethean characters aren't likely to run into them. That implies that the Alchemists Prometheans <i>are</i> likely to run into must all be irrational and insane. That's the dichotomy, either they're reasonable people who don't hunt Prometheans, or they do hunt Prometheans and they're Vitriol-crazed fiends. It doesn't even leave room for Alchemists who are mostly rational but are driven to hunt Prometheans out of desperation (despite there being an example character who does just that), or Alchemists who haven't gone off the deep end yet, but have started rationalizing the behavior and are on their way to becoming full-blown Insensate. I don't need an in-depth discussion of potential motivations, I just don't want the text to implicitly try to shut down the possibility of nuanced Alchemist antagonists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943771#post943771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily agree with this, and here's why, first I'll cover the 'instead' notion. I think it's important to cover villains seen as villains, so long as you caveat along the way that its not this black and white and simple. I think the book does that throughout, letting you know the somewhat simplistic picture they're painting isn't the whole thing, but it is an important and necessary part they need to cover. That leads to the natural response 'why not make the game better then and give us both? Tell us how they're villains but explore those grey areas, give that more nuanced view in addition to the villain-y picture we get wouldn't that make it better?<br /> <br /> In short, I do think that's right, it would, so why don't I have a problem with it not happening and in fact seem opposed to readings calling for just that? One main reason; practicality. At the end of the day this book had a limited word count the writer's had to work with, and including more on the Alchemists meant sacrificing elsewhere. Given that this is the Core Book for the new Promethean line I think the focus needed to be kept where its at, on the Prometheans and how they see and experience their Pilgrimage and their Great Work. A more nuanced view would have been better in presentation perhaps, but would have detracted, due to word count, on the villainous perspective that the Prometheans themselves experience, and as you yourself pointed out has so many rich variations to explore it likely wouldn't have done itself justice. Hence the approach the book took and one I agree with. Keep the focus tightened down on the Promethean experience, as simplistic as that might be for these complex villains, but let the players know there's a wealth of gray for them to explore. That exploration though, we'll need to leave up to them until some other books come out perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that leaving room for Promethean-killing Alchemists with more complex motivations would require more wordcount. All it would require is the text not undermining its own attempts to leave that room open. There's already a fantastic example character that shows Alchemists can be sympathetic and still be distinctly villainous. She just seems to be in direct contrast with the statements of &quot;Insensate Alchemists all despise their humanity and are obsessed with gaining personal power.&quot; There's already a section contrasting them with Pandorans in that they can be (more or less) rational beings, suggesting that they make good tragic antagonists, and pointing out that this theme is made stronger when they don't start out wanting to kill the throng. But then the example it gives of such a &quot;tragic antagonist&quot; totally did start out wanting to kill the throng, he just pretended not to. There's already a sidebar explaining why there's simply not room to discuss Alchemists who aren't likely to kill Prometheans. But then it associates those alchemists with sanity and rationality, and the ones it does discuss with madness and obsession. I don't need a detailed discussion of all the possible reasons an Alchemist could have for abandoning humanity and murdering Prometheans. I just want it to leave the motivations a little room to breathe, instead of quashing the potential of characters who are both rational and antagonistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943771#post943771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the wall of text, hope all that's clear. If you'd like to go into anything like the importance of the more simplistic villainous view as it is in the core book let me know, same if any of this is confusing or doesn't seem to add up, its a lot and I want to be clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem! I enjoy getting deep into these discussions. I actually agree with you that it's important to present villains in a straightforward manner at first, I just think it's equally important to leave the door open for more complex villains, and this section doesn't do that to my satisfaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T17:54:30-07:00","id":944025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943854#post943854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't have anything meaningful to add to debate on whether or not the Alchemist section spends enough time on the &quot;grey&quot; areas or not. I see both sides. The practicality of what belongs in a core books vs. compelling things that would be fun to explore doesn't have a good solution.<br /> <br /> I have to say though... as someone that's not neuro-typical... all the point complaining about &quot;ableism,&quot; here have made me feel far, far, worse about my mental status than anything in Beast or Promethean 2e has printed. Sanity is not a mental health diagnosis, it's a legal ruling, and conflating them doesn't help in any way. It doesn't help writers create more nuanced games. It doesn't help larger societal issues. Sanity is an issue of being able to appreciate the consequences of your actions; which my diagnosis doesn't impact at all. It intersects of neuro-atypical issues, but they aren't the same thing. &quot;Crazy&quot; and &quot;mad&quot; are similarly not diagnostic criteria, or mental health conditions. Sane, crazy, and mad, are not in the DSM or ICD, because they have nothing to do with psychology, psychiatry, or actually helping people that have real mental health conditions.<br /> <br /> I don't need defending against a game describing antagonists that have gone off the deep end in pursuit of an irrational path, with morally dubious methods, using terms that intersect with how poorly society discusses actual important issues. Nothing in the book has any relevance to things like the fact that every time I apply for a job, I need to decide if I want to opt to exercise my right to not disclose my mental health issues and possibly get the job but not have any assistance is (very simple) accommodations my employer could make to help me be a productive employee (and of course they're going to find out anyway, and living in a state where you can be fired very easily despite supposed protections &quot;lying&quot; isn't a great idea), or disclose and then risk not getting the job because I just gave them a subconscious reason to put me to the bottom of the pile regardless of my qualifications.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not an easy topic by any means, but it should be noted that this kind of argument isn't about, or even really <i>for</i> you individually. It's not even really about respecting the feelings of other people, although that plays a part. It's about how the prevailing representation of different groups in media can inform society's general attitudes towards that group. On its own Promethean's presentation of Alchemists isn't going to cause people to start conflating &quot;mental illness&quot; with &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;sane&quot; with &quot;good&quot;, but it is yet another example of media reinforcing exactly that representation, which plays into a long running history of similar portrayals. This has real world consequences when it comes to any attempt to reshape how we conceive of these terms, and helps to inform the very subconsciousness biases you mention.<br /> <br /> Alchemists as insane is also just boring, as reseru said in his excellent posts a few pages back. So there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T17:55:37-07:00","id":944026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943898#post943898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat is a great way to describe how I, and literally every player I know IRL, feel about P1E, and seems to be the prevailing attitude on these forums*:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> If you like some/most of the rules for P:tC, but think that the downsides are too heavy handed to be much fun, then,<span style=\"color:red\"><b> YOU ARE WRONG! YOU ARE A HORRIBLE PERSON, WHO SHOULD NOT BE ALLOWED TO REPRODUCE! YOUR IDEAS ARE BAD, AND YOU SHOULD FEEL BAD! DIE IN A FIRE! DIE,DIE,DIE,DIE!!!!!!!!!!</b></span> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *Spoilered, because I'm actually NOT trying to turn this thread into a flaming mess, but the hostility towards the very <i>NOTION</i> of wanting to have Created beings that can actually form meaningful, lasting relationships outside their own splat, or that perhaps <u>ALTERNATIVES</u> to becoming a non-supernatural in the World/Chronicles of Darkness would have been nice, has made me a bit...cranky.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">If you are worried that your comment could turn a thread into a flaming mess, don't spoiler it. Find a less inflammatory way to phrase it, or don't post it at all.</span><br /> <br /> Also, please don't use that shade of red in your posts - it's the color all of the mods use for our &quot;mod voices&quot;, and I wouldn't want it to cause a miscommunication. That's not a rule, just a personal request (hence the black text).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:03:33-07:00","id":944028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944025#post944025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not an easy topic by any means, but it should be noted that this kind of argument isn't about, or even really <i>for</i> you individually. It's not even really about respecting the feelings of other people, although that plays a part. It's about how the prevailing representation of different groups in media can inform society's general attitudes towards that group. On its own Promethean's presentation of Alchemists isn't going to cause people to start conflating &quot;mental illness&quot; with &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;sane&quot; with &quot;good&quot;, but it is yet another example of media reinforcing exactly that representation, which plays into a long running history of similar portrayals. This has real world consequences when it comes to any attempt to reshape how we conceive of these terms, and helps to inform the very subconsciousness biases you mention.<br /> <br /> Alchemists as insane is also just boring, as reseru said in his excellent posts a few pages back. So there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap Azahul, I've been spending the last 30 minutes or so trying to formulate a response to that line of discussion that I felt communicated my stance on the issue in an appropriate manner and you've just done a better job of it than I think I could have done, and certainly far more concisely than I would have been able to manage. Thank you for this post!<br /> <br /> With that out there, I just want to apologize to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> if anything I said was in any way hurtful to you. That was certainly not my intent, and Azahul has summed up very well where I'm coming from on this issue. I think I've said everything I have to say on that particular matter already, and it's really not even central to my argument regarding the portrayal of Alchemists in general, so I am more than willing to drop that line of discussion if it bothers you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:28:26-07:00","id":944079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944007#post944007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No problem! I enjoy getting deep into these discussions. I actually agree with you that it's important to present villains in a straightforward manner at first, I just think it's equally important to leave the door open for more complex villains, and this section doesn't do that to my satisfaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, so, I think this discussion with you is getting at something I've noticed in the forums a long time, but as of yet am still unsure how to articulate. Would you be willing to take this to PM or say Skype?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:00:35-07:00","id":944088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944079#post944079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, so, I think this discussion with you is getting at something I've noticed in the forums a long time, but as of yet am still unsure how to articulate. Would you be willing to take this to PM or say Skype?</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure, feel free to PM me any time. Skype is tough for me because I'm much more articulate in asynchronous communication than I am in real-time, but I'm not unwilling to do it that way if you prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:39:14-07:00","id":944122,"title":"","content":"My initial thoughts on alchemist rules:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cAlchemists do not store Pyros in their bodies the way Prometheans do, but in alchemical preparations that must be quickly mixed into other potions to activate them.\u201d</span> Great in theory. But in practice, storing Pyros externally leads to complications: you can set it down somewhere and walk away from them, and they can be stolen from you. Do they lose efficacy if you don't keep them on your person? And if not, what happens if you try to carry more than your Magnitude permits? Do the latest additions to your inventory suddenly lose their power? <br /> \u2022 As well, unlike a Promethean's automatic daily generation of Pyros, alchemical preparations that embody the alchemist's Pyros don't materialize out of nowhere. What do alchemists do to create them? <br /> \u2022 As for their Distillations: the fact that an alchemist's Distillations exist in the form of potions, powders, and the like implies that the effects are transferable \u2014 that is, if the alchemist hands a potion to someone else and they drink it, <i>that</i> person experiences the effects of the potion. As long as potions aren't extremely perishable, that's an extremely useful property.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-05-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:43:45-07:00","id":944124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943888#post943888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word that separates them is sympathy. Heroes, as Beast goes out of its way to tell us, are supposed to be unsympathetic. Beyond being ridiculously bad writing advice, it is simply wrong, there's no such thing as an unsympathetic human. Hence the presentation of heroes is something I cannot stand. Alchemists, despite several instances where the book cuts very close towards the Hero approach, are deeply sympathetic character, driven by a common fear we all share, and acting in groups to justify themselves. That's a much more compelling, realistic take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm weird, but I wish <b>Beast</b>'s presentation had been bolder. It's slightly hypocritical for me to say that I wish Heroes were more unsympathetic, but that's dependent on the fact that I wish <b>Beast</b> hadn't so (seemingly) catered to the internet's outcry towards its Kickstarter draft. It's like I said, though, unsympathetic characters have their place, even if they are mortals which are otherwise very rare, but I don't think that place lines up with what Alchemists should represent.<br /> <br /> Disquiet drives people to torches and pitchforks but as soon as Beasts drive Heroes to it everyone loses their minds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T02:19:30-07:00","id":944202,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to say here, since I haven't read Promethean 2ED yet.<br /> <br /> But I do want to throw my hat in as against the idea that the only Alchemists who should show up in a Promethian game are the Insensate Alchemists who want to cut you up for parts. I can think of obvious and unique milestones that you could fufill through friendly interactions with an Alchemist.<ul><li>Gold - Defeat an alchemist in a debate about humanism vs transhumanism.</li> <li>Gold - Learn why someone who has mortality would want to remove it.</li> <li>Lead - Learn why a human would see value in the Promethian condition.</li> <li>Quicksilver - Debate alchemical theory with a mortal.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Besides. A Created trying to learn about humanity from a mentor who's worldview is not humanist is something with precedent. I'm thinking of the awesome novel The Golem and the Djinn where Chava, a Golem, learns about humanity from Rabbi Meyer.<br /> <br /> Humanism is often contrasted to religion, and Rabbi Meyer is obviously a devout man. He can also be seen as &quot;transhumanist&quot; in the sense that he wants to overcome human nature. Not by magically or technologically replacing parts of the human body. But by replacing human culture with the laws of God.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a stretch, but I don't think it's a stretch to breaking point. Especially if you subscribe to one of the varients of Humanism that includes atheism as a core tennent. <br /> <br /> And if you haven't, read The Golem and the Djinn. It doesn't have a Wasteland or Disquiet, but aside from that it is the perfect Promethian novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-05-2016, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T02:57:26-07:00","id":944209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944202#post944202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do want to throw my hat in as against the idea that the only Alchemists who should show up in a Promethian game are the Insensate Alchemists who want to cut you up for parts. I can think of obvious and unique milestones that you could fufill through friendly interactions with an Alchemist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, the book doesn't say you can't have friendly interactions with Alchemists; actually the opposite. It merely points out that there's an inherent tension. A live promethean can give the alchemist more Pyros, but to actually learn much from them, the alchemist really needs to cut them up and examine their internal organs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T04:27:43-07:00","id":944237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944025#post944025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not an easy topic by any means, but it should be noted that this kind of argument isn't about, or even really <i>for</i> you individually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't assume it was however:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not even really about respecting the feelings of other people, although that plays a part. </div> </div> </div>This is a problem. If you can't discuss things without respecting the feelings of the people you're trying to empower, it isn't going to work. Even if you're 100% correct in the need to reevaluate a passage in a text given its relation to a social ill, if you can't present that case with respect to the feelings of the people that are maligned by that social ill, the larger case is lost, because the inertia of social norms don't change based on rational logical argumentation (or we'd have progressed at lot farther and a lot faster than we have as a society).<br /> <br /> And again, my issue with how this has been brought up is that there's really two intersecting social issues at hand.<br /> <br /> First, there's the social issue of how we discuss people that do things that don't seem rational, or at least are incredibly jarring to social norms. The feeling that there has to be something wrong with someone that does something sufficiently extreme, and our extremely poor discourse as a society on how to communicate about it. This is what Promethean runs afoul of because it's talking about people that are doing extreme enough things that the text is asserting something must be wrong with them.<br /> <br /> Second, there's the ableism issue of how a neuro-typical society discriminates on multiple levels against the neuro-atypical members of that society; aka the real life stuff I was talking about.<br /> <br /> While, again, these two things intersect plenty, they're not the same. It's upsetting when they get conflated, regardless of the context, because I don't like it when people react to me differently because they're conflating them, and it feels exactly the same when people say that some of the CofD games are having ableism issues because they push a bit hard on mental instability. The conflation is frustrating, regardless of the intent. If the intersection is actually validly there, that's one thing (like the 1e Morality mechanics hitting that intersection hard by having immoral behavior directly linked to developing Derangements), but everyone seems to be on the same page here that this isn't the case for this topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944028#post944028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that out there, I just want to apologize to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> if anything I said was in any way hurtful to you. That was certainly not my intent, and Azahul has summed up very well where I'm coming from on this issue. I think I've said everything I have to say on that particular matter already, and it's really not even central to my argument regarding the portrayal of Alchemists in general, so I am more than willing to drop that line of discussion if it bothers you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate it. As far as I'm concerned as I explained above, is keeping those two concepts separate. Diving into the issues around how society lacks good language, and subsequently loses nuance, around things like &quot;sanity&quot; when it comes to bad actors, and how the Alchemists section gets itself tripped up on that is fine. It's the conflation of that with other issues of ableism that's problematic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T05:49:09-07:00","id":944260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944237#post944237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest man, I'm not sure what the problem is. Whether you believe there is a correlation between the poor use of language in places like Promethean's Alchemist chapter and systemic discrimination in real life or not, encouraging writers to break free of stereotypes and do something more interesting is in everyone's best interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:22:14-07:00","id":944394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944122#post944122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial thoughts on alchemist rules:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cAlchemists do not store Pyros in their bodies the way Prometheans do, but in alchemical preparations that must be quickly mixed into other potions to activate them.\u201d</span> Great in theory. But in practice, storing Pyros externally leads to complications: you can set it down somewhere and walk away from them, and they can be stolen from you. Do they lose efficacy if you don't keep them on your person? And if not, what happens if you try to carry more than your Magnitude permits? Do the latest additions to your inventory suddenly lose their power? <br /> \u2022 As well, unlike a Promethean's automatic daily generation of Pyros, alchemical preparations that embody the alchemist's Pyros don't materialize out of nowhere. What do alchemists do to create them? <br /> \u2022 As for their Distillations: the fact that an alchemist's Distillations exist in the form of potions, powders, and the like implies that the effects are transferable \u2014 that is, if the alchemist hands a potion to someone else and they drink it, <i>that</i> person experiences the effects of the potion. As long as potions aren't extremely perishable, that's an extremely useful property.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the first point, it turns out that there's an official answer: try to carry too much Pyros on you, and you trigger a Firestorm. Ouch. Understandable, but ouch. <br /> <br /> <i>Also</i> on the first point, I'm thinking of saying that the Pyros-charged preparations that an alchemist makes to hold his Pyros tends to dissipate rather quickly if removed from his person. By \u201cquickly\u201d, I mean that it lasts for the rest of the scene; but if the materials are not in the possession of an alchemist for more than a scene, they become alchemically worthless. It doesn't have to be the <i>same</i> alchemist, mind you; logically, alchemists ought to be able to share Pyros by sharing the Pyros-laden reagents. I'm also thinking of adding a \u201cStorehouse\u201d Merit as an adjunct to Safe Place that lets you leave up to its rating of reagents without their efficacy fading or the concentration triggering a Firestorm. <br /> <br /> I'm also thinking that Prometheans should be able to retrieve the Pyros stored in a reagent, just as they can \u201cretrieve\u201d Vitriol stored in another Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:33:37-07:00","id":944502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944260#post944260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest man, I'm not sure what the problem is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how to phrase it better than I did...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...encouraging writers to break free of stereotypes and do something more interesting is in everyone's best interests. </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. A core book has limited space, and especially for antagonists, stereotypes for the ST to quickly jump into are a good thing for the text as a game. The important thing for the Alchemist section is to not cut off the ability for more nuanced approaches (which to me is pretty clear they did not do); either by ST creativity or in future books.<br /> <br /> If there's a 2e Alchemist book, or PtC 2e antagonist book with a major chapter on Alchemists, that doesn't go beyond those stereotypes? That's when everyone's interests are being poorly served.<br /> <br /> As things stand now, the people who are not best served by the current text are people that want Alchemists to play a major role in their games besides being Insatiate antagonists; which is not everybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:48:15-07:00","id":944509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944502#post944502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entirely. A core book has limited space, and especially for antagonists, stereotypes for the ST to quickly jump into are a good thing for the text as a game. The important thing for the Alchemist section is to not cut off the ability for more nuanced approaches (which to me is pretty clear they did not do); either by ST creativity or in future books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, though it's clear to me that that they <i>did</i> cut off the ability for more nuanced approaches. That's just the impression I got and individual interpretations are individual, but. That's where my problem lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944502#post944502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As things stand now, the people who are not best served by the current text are people that want Alchemists to play a major role in their games besides being Insatiate antagonists; which is not everybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. I am not looking to include non-Insensate alchemists in major rolls in my games and I still feel this writeup... Well, I guess it doesn't underserve me, since I know how to write nuanced antagonists. But it seems to me that it would go against what the text states about Alchemists to write them as such, and that's just kind of unsatisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:58:22-07:00","id":944541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944502#post944502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how to phrase it better than I did...</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't your words I had trouble understanding, rather your feelings on the matter. I get that your opinion is that the real life discrimination and the terminology used in media like Promethean intersect rather than being part of the same issue. I fail to understand why you might get upset at someone taking a different opinion. It ultimately has very little impact on you one way or the other, and they're naught more than opinions. But to a lot of us, language in any media <i>is</i> part of real life discrimination. Since, as far as I can tell, you don't disagree that the language used in Promethean is on the poor side, we're left in this weird position where you seem to just be taking issue with the &quot;why&quot; of some objections to the particular phrasing in Promethean, when the &quot;why&quot; is not even something with any direct bearing on you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=944502#post944502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entirely. A core book has limited space, and especially for antagonists, stereotypes for the ST to quickly jump into are a good thing for the text as a game. The important thing for the Alchemist section is to not cut off the ability for more nuanced approaches (which to me is pretty clear they did not do); either by ST creativity or in future books.<br /> <br /> If there's a 2e Alchemist book, or PtC 2e antagonist book with a major chapter on Alchemists, that doesn't go beyond those stereotypes? That's when everyone's interests are being poorly served.<br /> <br /> As things stand now, the people who are not best served by the current text are people that want Alchemists to play a major role in their games besides being Insatiate antagonists; which is not everybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're deep into value judgement territory at this point, so bear that in mind for the rest of this post. You may not think the Alchemist section cuts off the ability for more nuanced approaches, but the section does dedicate precious word count it could have otherwise have saved by explicitly ruling out specific types of Alchemists that, so far as I am concerned, would have made for excellent interpretations of Insatiate Alchemists. Rather than just use stereotypes as a shorthand to save on words, it uses stereotypes and then spends some of the saved word count removing options outside of those stereotypes.<br /> <br /> It's not the end of the world. Like Charlaquin I'm fairly confident in my ability to write antagonists with more interesting motivations without the book's help. But rather than purely going beyond the source material it means that I'm having to ignore it. Not the best feeling.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, there's the question of whether the stereotypes used are actually <i>interesting</i>. This is pure subjectivity, but the depiction of Insatiate alchemists as amoral, insane, power hungry monsters goes too far for me. They're pure black, which can be thematically strange in a world so full of (dark, dark) shades of grey as the Chronicles of Darkness. Those &quot;pure evil&quot; villains who do show up in other game lines are usually alien, inhuman creatures. So on a thematic level I find it a bit jarring, and as a concept I find it lacking. This is humanist game that is in a large part about the human condition, there is so much meat to dig into there in having a villain <i>who is human</i>. After all, if being a human is better than being a Promethean, and if a Promethean knows that and seeks to become human, how do they then resolve the question of whether their life, a Promethean life, is worth more than that of a human? What if it would be morally correct to allow the Alchemist to do what they want? Good writing can often create depth near as easily as make use of a stereotype, but the Alchemist section has an entire sidebar that seems to be apart reinforcing the stereotype and closing off the potential for depth and nuance.<br /> <br /> And finally, there's the real life issues we've already discussed. As useful a tool as stereotypes are, it is important to understand where they come from and the kind of attitudes they entrench through their use. You may feel that &quot;mad=evil&quot; is harmless, just a symbol of our poor ability to discuss issues we find horrifying, but others hold stereotypes of that nature responsible for creating the unconscious biases that lead to everyday discrimination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T21:02:15-07:00","id":944682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943296#post943296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine you're a Promethean, a few years into you Pilgrimage; you understand some things about humanity, you know what sets you apart from it, and your days are spent striving towards becoming it. You come across a human being - a real human being, born into glorious normalcy with a genuine soul - who wants to kill you for the fire inside you. Somehow things reach a point where the two of you talk about things, and when you ask them why they want to steal your flame, they explain that they want to become more, become stronger and smarter and immortal and to surpass the circumstances of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I would find that infuriating. Here's some jerk who has everything you've ever wanted by no virtue or effort of their own other than a luckier origin than you're own, and they're not happy with it. They want more. They want to leave being human (magnificently human!) for another state of being, and worse, they want to kill you to fuel it.<br /> <br /> You don't need &quot;Pyros drives them hopeless maaaaaaaad!&quot; for that to be an incredible point of ohilosophical contention in a game about the beauty of basic fundamental humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It -is- an excellent point of philosophical contention. Even so, I'd be inclined to say the Promethean has blinded themselves to the Alchemist's viewpoint.<br /> <br /> The Promethean sees Humanity as this exalted state, meanwhile the Alchemist knows all of the flaws and downsides to Humanity. Despite this, they both want the same thing; to surpass the circumstances of their birth. Sure, the Alchemist's means are reprehensible, but their ends are no less noble than the New Dawn; not that this justifies their attempts to steal Pyros, of course.<br /> <br /> Hm, this is an interesting line of thought. I haven't actually got Promethean 2e yet, but this makes me want to.<br /> There was a thread here that I lurked through where someone pointed out that Promethean isn't actually anti-Transhuman, on the grounds that in order to transcend Humanity one must first -be- Human. Alchemists seem to kind of represent this, with the potential for both positive and negative views; albeit with the latter emphasised in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:21:39-07:00","id":945025,"title":"","content":"Okay, wow! I feel like it must have been weeks since this book dropped to read the back-and-forth of this thread, but's been DAYS! Some of us take this seriously... And I wholeheartedly approve! Not on to the points at hand, I have some thoughts that will <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013 </span>no doubt <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013 feel positively dated in this context, but onward I go!</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943331#post943331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Healthy Minds do not seek the Divine Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the crux \u2013 and the truth \u2013 of the matter. The Divine Fire is NOT for mortals. Every demiurge who managed to create a Promethean was, to one degree or another (and sorry-but-not-really for the less-than-clinical-term) bonkers. That touch of madness is what made the process <i>POSSIBLE</i>, and it is part and parcel to the experience of the Divine Fire in all its forms. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Yeah, yeah, yeah, the terms for 'sane' and otherwise ARE all kinds of problematic, and while I won't go into that specifically in this post, please do know that I think all of you have done a brilliant job of unpacking, repacking, pack-packing and everything else around this. The point I would make is that the OP got it right when saying that this notion 'broke me'. THAT is what the Divine Fire does to a mortal, does it mind, body, and soul. The means of that damage is via alchemy.</span><br /> <br /> Alchemy, in this case and for this game, is the exact same alchemy of the Promethean Transmutations, the slippy processes that are driven and fuelled by the Divine Fire. The same forces that cause Disquiet and Wasteland come with mortals attempting to harness the Divine fire, no matter if it be to wield the alchemical forms that come 'naturally' to the Created or to act as a demiurge. That is \u2013 in case it's not clear enough \u2013 ALL mortals who try to use this form of magic (by whatever name you wish to call it) are broken by the Divine Fire that is incompatible with a human soul. Prometheans, on the other hand, are NOT hurt because their Azothic sparks ARE as close as they come to possessing souls. <br /> <br /> Alchemists <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013 </span>the ones we're discussing from the game <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2013 </span>use the EXACT same Transmutations as Prometheans do, but these mortals use the various almebics and whatnot to make potions and elixirs as \u2018external alchemy\u2019 mentioned on <b>p 117</b>. The write-up could offer more info for clarity\u2019s sake, sure, but it's all the same alchemy. The biggest difference, however, is that '<i>Pyros is not for mortals</i>' (<b>p 262</b>). What's this mean? The book says they'll suffer persistent Conditions and Derangements (something that CofD does not have as a basic rule, by the way), but I would have liked to see more. The notion that a mortal imbibing or otherwise 'taking' concoctions of distilled Pyros for some benefit ought to come with some consequence, especially for THESE Insatiate monsters who take a devil-may-care attitude to what their pursuit may cause. Stains on the soul, physical changes, <i>SOME</i> sort of stigmata should come with such reckless use of forces that mortals are ill suited to manipulate. The fact that the mortals who DO use these methods become jaded, horrid, and less-than-sane (however one chooses to define or conceptualise that state) is what makes these alchemists different from the 'sane' ones who know better, and those changes might have been spelled out a little better in the book.<br /> <br /> ...Of course, all of the above are MY thoughts, none of which are binding even in MY own games. I'm NOT saying anyone who disagrees is wrong so much as, you know, just not agreeing with me? Yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:31:27-07:00","id":945831,"title":"","content":"One of the things that's going to be in the rules/fluff/setting hack of Promethean I'm working on is an appendix that makes alchemists fully playable not mustache-twirlers. I'm even making some advice on mixed parties- making alchemist to promethean as ghoul is to vampire or sleepwalker is to mage. <br /> <br /> I have to say the comment about &quot;murderers and normal people&quot; is kind of funny to me since the vast majority of Chronicles of Darkness characters have committed at least one murder. <br /> <br /> Also, &quot;transhumanists and alchemists have to be eeeeeevil because it's a horror game&quot; would be more acceptable if Promethean was more horror-y and less of a &quot;humans are great and wonderful and special&quot; morality tale. <br /> <br /> Also also, A+ point about how Alchemists, even the ones who steal Pyros and Vitriol, aren't any worse than some groups that are playable. Hell, the average eeeeeeeevil transhumanist alchemist who REJECTS HIS HUMANITY, JOJO, is probably responsible for less damage than the average vampire, werewolf, or mage. <br /> <br /> Also also also, I actually really like Matt as a person and I think he's a good writer and designer overall, but I really really massively disagree with his aversion to making antagonist groups playable. Ascension really came into its own when the Technocracy became playable, and the playability of Fetches was one of my absolute favorite things about Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:51:07-07:00","id":945849,"title":"","content":"Oh! Also! ChroD has literally already presented morally ambiguous alchemists who do some pretty shady things to try to transcend the limits of their condition as sympathetic and playable. Remember the Ordo Dracul? They're a perfect guide for how Alchemists should have been handled. There's not really a fundamental difference between an Ordo Dracul member who wants to be able to walk in the sun and a human who wants to be immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T21:06:49-07:00","id":945918,"title":"","content":":\\<br /> <br /> Man, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>, the sheer amount of hyperbole in your posts really does not help your case. Like, I'm pretty firmly on the &quot;alchemists are presented too unsympathetically for my taste&quot; side, and reading your post actually made me <i>less</i> sure about that stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T21:45:39-07:00","id":945942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945849#post945849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not really a fundamental difference between an Ordo Dracul member who wants to be able to walk in the sun and a human who wants to be immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer to think &quot;There's not really a fundamental difference between an Promethean who wants to be human, and a human who wants to be free of a horrible disease.&quot; (especially if that disease is contagious). Of course the alchemist is trying to fix a &quot;natural&quot; fault in themselves rather than the promethean's &quot;supernatural&quot; fault in themselves, but I don't think that really affects the ethics of the situation. But both are simply trying to improve themselves, until the promethean or the alchemist start to hurt others in order to reach their new state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T22:41:45-07:00","id":945959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945942#post945942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer to think &amp;quot;There's not really a fundamental difference between an Promethean who wants to be human, and a human who wants to be free of a horrible disease.&amp;quot; (especially if that disease is contagious). Of course the alchemist is trying to fix a &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; fault in themselves rather than the promethean's &amp;quot;supernatural&amp;quot; fault in themselves, but I don't think that really affects the ethics of the situation. But both are simply trying to improve themselves, until the promethean or the alchemist start to hurt others in order to reach their new state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I'm not sure how that's any different than my examples. A vampire wanting to transcend the limitations of vampirism and a promethean wanting to transcend the limitations of prometheanism are pretty much the same, and I consider aging and diseases to both be flaws of the human condition, the way Disquiet is a flaw of the Promethean condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:18:49-07:00","id":945972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945849#post945849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not really a fundamental difference between an Ordo Dracul member who wants to be able to walk in the sun and a human who wants to be immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is. The Dragons are protagonists in a game that reinforces their themes. Alchemists are antagonists in a game that contrasts with their themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the playability of Fetches was one of my absolute favorite things about Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, the depiction of Fetches <i>in the Changeling core book</i> wasn't dissimilar to the depiction of Alchemists in the Promethean core book. Fetches were expanded and made playable in <i>Autumn Nightmares</i>, if I'm not mistaken. Alchemists may see something similar in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:29:12-07:00","id":945978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945972#post945972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, the depiction of Fetches <i>in the Changeling core book</i> wasn't dissimilar to the depiction of Alchemists in the Promethean core book. Fetches were expanded and made playable in <i>Autumn Nightmares</i>, if I'm not mistaken. Alchemists may see something similar in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 2e playtest material, however, they are nuanced, potentially sympathetic, and like a baby step away from playable as PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:32:20-07:00","id":945980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945849#post945849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Also! ChroD has literally already presented morally ambiguous alchemists who do some pretty shady things to try to transcend the limits of their condition as sympathetic and playable. Remember the Ordo Dracul? They're a perfect guide for how Alchemists should have been handled. There's not really a fundamental difference between an Ordo Dracul member who wants to be able to walk in the sun and a human who wants to be immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Have you seen some of the scales? They're right up crimes against humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:44:01-07:00","id":945982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945959#post945959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but I'm not sure how that's any different than my examples. A vampire wanting to transcend the limitations of vampirism and a promethean wanting to transcend the limitations of prometheanism are pretty much the same, and I consider aging and diseases to both be flaws of the human condition, the way Disquiet is a flaw of the Promethean condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one, Ordo are pretty messed up. Secondly, because &quot;comparing two monsters and saying this human is the same&quot; gives a different feel to &quot;the designated villain in this case is doing the exact same thing as the protagonists&quot;. Third, immortality has a stigma of being &quot;innately wrong&quot; and thus less sympathetic than someone trying to cure a disease without necessarily trying to become truly immortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:48:40-07:00","id":945984,"title":"","content":"I guess my overarching problem, the problem I have with the themes of Promethean is that &quot;humans are special and wonderful and the best thing ever&quot; does not fit with a personal horror setting or the actual themes of Frankenstein. In fact, the closest thing to a central lesson that Frankenstein has is basically &quot;humans are incompetent, lazy assholes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:00:58-07:00","id":946007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945984#post945984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my overarching problem, the problem I have with the themes of Promethean is that &quot;humans are special and wonderful and the best thing ever&quot; does not fit with a personal horror setting or the actual themes of Frankenstein.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read 2e yet, but unless it makes some major changes isn't it more &quot;being a human is better than being rejected by all existence including the land itself&quot;...? And I say that as someone who hates how Promethean handles transhumanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:05:45-07:00","id":946010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946007#post946007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read 2e yet, but unless it makes some major changes isn't it more &amp;quot;being a human is better than being rejected by all existence including the land itself&amp;quot;...? And I say that as someone who hates how Promethean handles transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why Promethean has the &quot;the land rejects you&quot; is specifically because the devs want to push the &quot;humanity is super special and awesome&quot; theme. Note that in Frankenstein, the land or reality or whatever doesn't reject the Creature. Only humans do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:42:51-07:00","id":946018,"title":"","content":"Good thing the game isn't meant to be a game version of Frankenstein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:54:52-07:00","id":946020,"title":"","content":"Which sucks for people who love the novel and hate how so many adaptations bastardize it. <br /> <br /> The Creature is my favorite &quot;classic monster&quot;. That's why Promethean bugs me so much. I want to love it, because I love the source material and subject matter, but there's the huge barrier of misinterpretation and pilgrimage railroading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T02:45:21-07:00","id":946038,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear though that you don't want to love it... you want to love a different thing that's in your head that occupies as similar enough space OPP isn't going to make that game instead.<br /> <br /> Promethean, despite the influence and inspiration from Frankenstein, isn't actually about the same things as the novel. The novel is far more closely related to Mage (as Victor is the main character and the story is all about his hubris running unchecked), with the Creature's side-plot of discovering humanity in itself being what Promethean draws on.<br /> <br /> Besides... a game of playing the Creature more true to the novel would be... kind of painfully boring. The Creature doesn't actually do a whole lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:27:46-07:00","id":946055,"title":"","content":"What does the Creature find when he discovers humanity, though? Not that humanity is a wonderful exalted state, certainly. <br /> <br /> Anyway, this thread was originally about alchemists, so let's get back to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:59:35-07:00","id":946202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945849#post945849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Remember the Ordo Dracul? They're a perfect guide for how Alchemists should have been handled. There's not really a fundamental difference between an Ordo Dracul member who wants to be able to walk in the sun and a human who wants to be immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Both are terrible monsters who are super keen to throw their humanity out of the window so they can become an even more terrible monster.<br /> <br /> Man, that was easy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:32:41-07:00","id":946223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946202#post946202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. Both are terrible monsters who are super keen to throw their humanity out of the window so they can become an even more terrible monster.<br /> <br /> Man, that was easy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! And this is a horror game, so I'm completely fine with the pursuit of power and immortality turning you into a horrible monster. <br /> <br /> It's just that this is a game about being monsters, and as horrible as the Ordo Dracul they're not just fully playable but incredibly sympathetic. In fact, you could make a case that they're the &quot;most lesser evil&quot; among the Covenants, in that their end goal would be the most beneficial to humanity. That doesn't make them not monsters, but it makes them twisted vampire mad scientists that someone could look at and think, &quot;this is a shitty situation and these guys are making the best of it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because that's the other side of &quot;it's a horror setting&quot;. Things kind of suck. You could die or be hollowed out by magic rats at any moment through no fault of your own. You're a weak, squishy, ignorant nobody. &quot;Evening the odds&quot; has been brought up before, but it bears repeating. ChroD is a dark, scary setting, and the games hammer home that you often have to do things you'll regret to survive. It isn't just the monsters- Hunters can do horrific things, break law after law, and modify themselves into something inhuman, but the alternative is to just lie down and be complacent cattle for the monsters. <br /> <br /> That, to me, is the best way to look at alchemists sympathetically while also keeping them twisted and monstrous. <br /> <br /> They are the ones who didn't lie down. <br /> <br /> Hunters are the people who saw monsters preying on humanity, and didn't lie down. Alchemists saw diseases, aging, and death preying on humanity, and didn't lie down. Both of them work with powers they don't understand and do things that are hard to justify, but the alternative is, well, death. The Hunter says she refuses to let some Draugr drink her or her friends dry. The alchemist says she refuses to let cancer or aging or an accident bring her or her friends down. Both light a candle. They may burn out. Their fire may burn out of control. In fact, those things are probably likely. But without them, darkness is all there would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:47:08-07:00","id":946238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946202#post946202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. Both are terrible monsters who are super keen to throw their humanity out of the window so they can become an even more terrible monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in first edition, the Ordo Dracul kept Humanity in relatively high esteem, there's even a coil that requires one to be Humanity 8 to take. They want to throw away their vampiric weaknesses out the window. Overcoming one's weaknesses is something humanity's been trying to do, and often pulling off, since the use of tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-08-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:09:22-07:00","id":946253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943117#post943117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no, no. I get all that. As I said, I understand the writers don't want to dedicate book space to subsplats (even though Vampire, Werewolf, Mage &amp; Demon all do so to their betterment, but I digress.) My gripe is exclusively with the degree to which the book seems to go out of its way to make is excessively clear that Prometheans should not be running into 'sane' Alchemists...ever. Which to me feels artificial and a tad cloying.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> You don't digress at all, in fact you've touched another point I was struggling with but hadn't put to thought.<br /> <br /> Weirdly the sample Alchemist is a sincerely relatable and indeed pitiable figure. A young woman, marred by cancer and afraid for her life. Which really makes me think the entire divide between White Alchemists and Black Alchemists is...well...pointless. Let them all be deeply flawed people, relatable and repulsive in their own ways, and dispense with breaking them down into wise and &quot;Insensate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It says they MIGHT at some point usualy after seeking them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:09:30-07:00","id":946254,"title":"","content":"Also, if we're going to do the ableism perspective, I should point out that I have two conditions that could be considered either disabilities or mental illnesses and one chronic injury. I want to cure the chronic injury and one of the mental illnesses, but not the other. In fact, that condition is one of the reasons why I identified so strongly with the Creature, and Promethean let me down by presenting a scenario where the only road to happiness and self-acceptance is magically getting rid of it, which A. Isn't possible in real life and B. Isn't something I would do if it were. I know there are other ways people see it, but that's how I see it. <br /> <br /> With the other illness and the chronic injury, that's where I get the Alchemist perspective. The human body is faulty, fragile, and poorly designed in many ways. Back injuries, diseases, and aging are all things that don't make me who I am in the way that other things do, and they're things I have no attachment to and wish to get rid of. <br /> <br /> I fully accept that, in a tabletop roleplaying game about personal horror, the result of that will probably be monstrous, but, from an in and out of universe perspective, I don't think that makes it not worth doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:45:10-07:00","id":946277,"title":"","content":"So, snark aside, I finished the section on Alchemists on Saturday, and this thread seems lively enough to warrant response.<br /> <br /> So, I'm gonna break my opinion down on two points, being a) Are they portrayed as too unsympathetic?, and b) are they unplayable as PC's? I'm gonna start on that second one.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Are Alchemists Unplayable as PC's?</u></b><br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Like seriously, if you want to play an Alchemist, the only mechanic you're missing is how exactly the make their potions and such, and that doesn't take much in the way of houseruling-extended action, hour per roll, Intelligence,Resolve, or Composure+Science, Occult, Expression Or Other+Magnitude depending on the Alchemical Tradition you're trying to evoke, 5 successes per level of the Alembic you're trying to take a distillation from(persistent level as 5, 1 Pyros level as 10, 2 pyros level as 15, 3 pyros level as 20). I thought that up just now. Everything else is available, except EXP costs. Go play your happy asses off. I wouldn't be opposed to fleshing that out in a future book.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Are Alchemists too unsympathetic?</b></u><br /> <br /> Eh? Ish.<br /> <br /> Let me get two biases out of the way before I expand on that The first is, having been here during the entire development cycle, I have a shit ton of spite for the Alchemist bias. Being frank, the road to this point has been filled with a lot of people who were obnoxious and rude about the entire thing, and that pisses me off more than anything else. I was really soured on the entire idea of alchemists before they got announced, and when people threw an even bigger bag of shit when the blog came out, I probably would have been well satisfied if they had been cut all together. That I am impressed with the Alchemist delivery in spite of the hateful vocal minority really inclining me to hate it anyways speaks to fact that Matt and his team know how to juxtapose elements in really evocative ways.<br /> <br /> The second bias is that we've had a pretty direct address of the sympathetic alchemist in the sidebar. It's short and can't cover the dichotomies super well, but it's not like it's not addressed, and its' sense is fairly well grounded-as a general rule, players have enough common sense to figure out how to run more sympathetic alchemists based on everything in here. There's enough material for players to figure out how to make the spectrum work. My grand point is that it's not like it's absolutely ignored, so to complain at length like it is strikes me as useless.<br /> <br /> Now that out of the way, let's me give my more level opinion. Because it is a little too unsympathetic, but not to any point I actually care about.<br /> <br /> As Gecko blew out of proportion, this game is about taking a step outside of our assumptions to look at humanity and discover things about, to try and slip into a place where we can understand our condition from a detached position. For me, this is a positive, as that invites me to gain wisdom on flaws and strengths and understand more deeply things that can be done as well as appreciating my life more as it is. So for the purposes of the game, it pays to have an antithesis, people who are convinced that humanity has nothing worth examining and nothing to appreciate, people desperate to escape. And it just so happens, Insatiate alchemists neatly fit that slot. The problem, of course, is that by having the Insatiate(by the way, Insatiate, not Insensate, various people who are getting it wrong) as our main focus, it does miss out on the alchemists who create story hooks without being antagonist-the alchemist who thinks the only answer is a Promethean's Vitriol and begs them to help is not an indecent example.<br /> <br /> There's some issue in terms of the matter of space and word count and intent, but for now I'm going to ignore that. I think a few story hooks before going into the Insatiate might have been good, because there is some room for the discussions that come up with people who know of Prometheans and advanced alchemy and have needs they might try to negotiate for-hell, the book <i>outside of the sidebar</i> mentions that. It is fairly heavy on the one side of the argument, and I can see some bother to be had over that.<br /> <br /> Not a lot though.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Why I'm Okay with the Insatiate barring Metaphysics.</u></b><br /> <br /> For starters, as the mention of <i>outside the sidebar</i> implies, I actually found that even with the heavy-handed presentation, there were still lots of concessions(and that's without applying any outside &quot;usuallys&quot;). There's enough mentioned to keep it, for me at least, from weighing too heavily to one side.<br /> <br /> On top of that, I also find that a lot of those particular hooks don't necessarily need alchemists to make them happen, it just speeds the setup for Prometheans more if you have people outside of the characters push it. For example, the &quot;My daughter needs help, and only your Vitriol can do the trick&quot; scenario posits that an alchemist needs to present for that, but does it? Could a Promethean, whose been working on building a relationship with this family, not find out about the condition, try the transmutations they know, and then reach the hypothesis that maybe they're own Vitriol is what's needed? An Alchemist confirms those theories, or finds the flaws with them-they do great as sounding boards for the ideas, but you don't really need them to push the matter. And honestly, when an alchemist is there to push the matter, odds are it's because there's more on their own plate than simply being a good Humanitarian.<br /> <br /> Like mages, alchemists are defined by what they do, and in relationship to the Prometheans, it's what they do with their alchemy in relationship to the Promethean's existence and goals that shape their place in the narrative. In many ways, the more antagonistic options are actually wider and offer better questions than the sympathetic ones, because these are realms that they are best allowed to guide Prometheans through, places they alone can show the way of. In a fit of irony, a lot of the people here who want more sympathetic alchemists are also the ones who harp on more about the &quot;Humanity is the best&quot; idea, often mangled into stupid configurations as it is. If humanity is not really a thing worth aspiring to, then it makes sense that the more powerful a human is, the more anti-aspirational they become, because their options for demonstrating those anti-aspirational attributes of humanity are that much more increased. In this way, the Insatiate form a definite anti-honeymoon collective of humanity, a very solid bunch that show that being human isn't sunshine and roses, but a collection of flaws, biologically, sociologogically, etc. If you want to prove that humanity is not &quot;Hur-Dur, the <i>best&quot;, </i>Insatiate alchemists go a long way in revealing just that. If humanity not being great is a point you're going to make, you have to accept it of alchemists too.<br /> <br /> I think, though, that even in the negativity of the alchemists there's something great for both Prometheans and players to pick up from. When I first joined the forums ages ago, I joined under the username of Being, with my signature being &quot;All strive to be something else.&quot; It was sort of sardonic, but it had a great measure of truth. For Prometheans, it's easy to think that it'll all be worth it when they reach their destination of humanity, but having even someone, even or perhaps especially someone who's cruel, reinforces that there's always something bitter that needs fixing. It shows for the Promethean that regardless of form, life is a journey, that flaws so far are a part of life, and that we all share in the suffering, even when it's different. The destination is not about finally achieving happiness-happiness is not the whole of life. What the Insatiate lack is equanimity, serenity, the inner stillness that comes from being <i>in</i>.<br /> <br /> And this leads to the other reason why, despite the heaviness, I don't mind so much-the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Why I'm okay with the Insatiate including Metaphysics.</u></b><br /> <br /> Now, honestly, I'm glad they didn't lean too much on this. Humans can be ugly without having to warp it and justify it with the Divine Fire. It'd be so easy to write off alchemists as antagonists under the premise of &quot;Even the more sane and kindly alchemists will eventually do harm to a Promethean because of Disquiet.&quot; Instead, they got to the point and let it do the talking. And likewise, it's not ignored-they make it pretty clear that the Divine Fire, which is change incarnate, fucks these guys up with all the Conditions they get. But it cannot be overstated-too much exposure to the Divine Fire means you lack equanimity. It's possible to be a force of change while also maintaining a personal state of harmony, but the Divine Fire doesn't tolerate it-it pushes and shoves and demands change, fuck your comfort and place. As such, I have no problem believing that the more you do alchemy with the Divine Fire, the more everything is not enough. Going, again, to the example of &quot;My daughter needs help, and only your Vitriol can do the trick&quot;, I don't personally believe for a second that a man who has a theory on the subject is going to accept No as an answer, because at that point, odds are that the alchemist has had enough exposure to Pyros to basically be in the kinetic state-this must move forward.<br /> <br /> And it's a danger. While madness might be overselling it, the Divine Fire is change, and it relies on the strong conduits of obsession and desperation. The better you are at working with it, the more you are those things. I think that sets the stage for eventualities, that most of the people you see working with the Divine Fire <i>are</i> going to be Insatiate. Those who aren't probably make a sure point of saying &quot;DON'T <i>TEMPT ME</i>, FRODO&quot; to themselves when they get involved with it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Conclusion</u></b><br /> <br /> Still, I get the frustrations. It's not like that window doesn't exist, that there isn't room to ask &quot;But what if?&quot; Given the matter of space, it's not surprising, but it would have been nice to see some more exploration of the middle ground before doing the deep dive.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, though, I think the deep dive is more important for the game, that the Insatiate make points that Promethean need to hear more than what the moderates can tell them. So, are they too unsympathetic? Ish. Enough to note, not enough to care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-08-2016, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts"