 monsters- Hunters can do horrific things, break law after law, and modify themselves into something inhuman, but the alternative is to just lie down and be complacent cattle for the monsters. <br /> <br /> That, to me, is the best way to look at alchemists sympathetically while also keeping them twisted and monstrous. <br /> <br /> They are the ones who didn't lie down. <br /> <br /> Hunters are the people who saw monsters preying on humanity, and didn't lie down. Alchemists saw diseases, aging, and death preying on humanity, and didn't lie down. Both of them work with powers they don't understand and do things that are hard to justify, but the alternative is, well, death. The Hunter says she refuses to let some Draugr drink her or her friends dry. The alchemist says she refuses to let cancer or aging or an accident bring her or her friends down. Both light a candle. They may burn out. Their fire may burn out of control. In fact, those things are probably likely. But without them, darkness is all there would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps (from the Alchemist's perspective) that their preys are walking blights who can turn a normal city into Fallout Las Vegas given enough time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:48:02-07:00","id":946279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946223#post946223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep! And this is a horror game, so I'm completely fine with the pursuit of power and immortality turning you into a horrible monster.<br /> <br /> It's just that this is a game about being monsters, and as horrible as the Ordo Dracul they're not just fully playable but incredibly sympathetic. *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>Methinks you missed the sarcasm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:25:54-07:00","id":946310,"title":"","content":"Excellent points, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. I think we're more or less in the same boat, my issues just lie in a few specific instances where it seems like an attempt to give breathing room for the &quot;my daughter needs your Vitriol and I won't take no for an answer&quot; Alchemists was made, and then self-sabotaged.<br /> <br /> The sidebar almost opens the door for a broader spectrum of Alchemists, but instead of saying &quot;there's a lot of Alchemists out there, but the ones best suited to a Promethean game are the really fucked up ones, so that's what we're going to focus on here,&quot; it says &quot;there are sane alchemists and there are fucked up alchemists. This section is about the latter because they're the ones best suited to a Promethean game.&quot; It's a subtle difference, but the former implies that there is a spectrum that's not being fully explored while the latter implies that there is only one option that isn't being explored. It sets out to expand options and ends up restricting them.<br /> <br /> The Alchemists and their Prey section almost explored the possibility of Alchemists who start out saying &quot;DON'T TEMPT ME, FRODO&quot; but over the course of the game get to the point where they're saying &quot;IT COULD'VE BEEN MINE. IT SHOULD'VE BEEN MINE!&quot; But what it presents as a good example of that is an Alchemest who has been saying &quot;If I could but borrow the ring...&quot; all along. It sets out to point out that the road to insatiety (thank you for pointing that out, by the way) is paved with good intentions, and instead says that even Alchemists who look like they might have good intentions are actually just lying.<br /> <br /> It's like... So close to presenting great, on-theme antagonists while leaving the door open for a different take down the road that the places where it falls short of that and undermines itself are all the more frustrating. Where you see &quot;unsympathetic enough to make note of, but not enough to care about&quot;, I see &quot;close enough to sympathetic to care that it's falling short of its potential.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-08-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:32:44-07:00","id":946318,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I can see the issue. And honestly, if it's a sticking point for someone, okay. I think others might be making too much of a thing of it, but barring the overblowing, even if I don't care in the end, I do get why it's a sore point for some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:21:27-07:00","id":946405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=945984#post945984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my overarching problem, the problem I have with the themes of Promethean is that &amp;quot;humans are special and wonderful and the best thing ever&amp;quot; does not fit with a personal horror setting or the actual themes of Frankenstein. In fact, the closest thing to a central lesson that Frankenstein has is basically &amp;quot;humans are incompetent, lazy assholes&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Humanity is fantastic and you are decidedly not human&quot; doesn't sound like personal horror to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:50:17-07:00","id":946427,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I wish I could fully appreciate that comprehensive dissertation on your opinions of Alchemists, but alas, I do not yet have the material to peruse.<br /> <br /> I don't quite know why it turns out surprising or objectionable to some people that, in a game with the core thesis of striving for humanity despite all its failings, the meat in presentation of the antagonists is on those who stand clearly for anti-humanism or transhumanism and are easily condemnable. From what Charlaquin is saying, I suppose there's more of a problem with how the alternatives and the little explicit room given to those are addressed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-08-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:50:44-07:00","id":946429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946279#post946279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Methinks you missed the sarcasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inigo Montoya says: &quot;If the post I was responding to was sarcastic, that would mean you were saying that the Ordo Dracul and alchemists aren't actually monsters. Also, I was agreeing with you that they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> And no, it doesn't. Because it railroads you into only having the choice to either become human or Be A Bad Point-Misser Who Is Playing Wrong. And in a horror setting, &quot;humans are special&quot; just doesn't work for me. Especially since every other Chronicles of Darkness book emphasizes how awful humans can be. <br /> <br /> Back to alchemists, I would advise everyone (in general and on this thread) to read/watch Baccano for a sympathetic portrayal of immortal alchemists. As a bonus, there's a character who could easily be a Promethean, and she ends up in a happy relationship with an alchemically-immortal human without having to become human herself. It even has Slashers and an Unchained (although that particular character was revealed in a sidestory to be more like an incredibly ancient and powerful Promethean). <br /> <br /> EDIT: Searched it on the forums, and ironically enough some of the most vocal deathists here are fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-08-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:06:37-07:00","id":946440,"title":"","content":"The monster wanted to belong in a world that could not accept him-that simply was not ready for him...or was it?<br /> <br /> I wonder, sometimes, how the monster might have faired in today's world. The book frames his problems as primarily being grotesque, and it makes me wonder what kind of a scientist would harbor revulsion long for their creation before the joy of the impossible came back in, before the exultation came flowing. Certainly, in today's world, with our X-Mens and Inuyashas and our civil rights movements and scientific progress against deformity and social progress for deformity and wiser humanitarian acts in desperate countries and many other features, I wonder if Frankenstein would have had the insight, if not of a scientist, then of dweller in today's culture to better control his response, to at least continue his work to try and make the monster presentable at least. Having fled, wouldn't there be punks and goths who would take one look at the monster and exclaim how fucking radical it was-in fact, would it be impossible for the monster to have become a king of goth culture, a decorated writer and oft-invited guest to talk shows? Would there be twitter feeds and tumblr posts labeled #giveadamabride, or perhaps #giveadamahusband, if he was shown in the right lens? Are these things impossible, or would they be inevitable?<br /> <br /> And then I wonder: does he need a modern era? Maybe all he had was bad luck, missing the person with the right Unless. Do we really believe that there was ever no one in the world without a heart for a monster, in a myriad of cultures that have always gladly bent their knee to that altar? We envy our monsters, secretly aspire to be them, in ways. The monster was more human than most we have wanted to be over the generations-surely, it was not impossible.<br /> <br /> The monster almost assuredly knew, and felt cursed from early in his life, that his was an uphill battle. His creator rejected him, so how could anyone else. And yet, despite that, in his heart-he wanted what all humans want. We're a social species, we want to-have to-be with someone, sometime-to be part of something. We do not want to be alone. Are we surprised, then, that the creature, as well as all other monsters that we create, so also desire to be part of something-to be in the great human family, somehow?<br /> <br /> One thing strikes me as certain, in relation to the wider thread:<br /> <br /> You cannot mourn that alchemists are treated unsympathetically without having sympathy for humanity. To say there is nothing in humanity worth becoming for the Prometheans is to say that there is nothing worthy of becoming as an alchemist.<br /> <br /> They are, after all, still human. If the desire to escape the human condition is anything, it is, perhaps in some ways, the most human thing of all.<br /> <br /> All things strive to become something else. Begrudge not those who seek their inclusion.<br /> <br /> That is the terrible theme of Frankenstein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-14-2016, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:11:35-07:00","id":946445,"title":"","content":"Personal theory(well, humor, really): Frankenstein treated his creature like shit when he realized that, despite creating life, he still wasn't allowed into God's club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:22:58-07:00","id":946456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946429#post946429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Searched it on the forums, and ironically enough some of the most vocal deathists here are fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's a deathist? Someone who does or doesn't believe people should strive for longer lives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:26:47-07:00","id":946457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946456#post946456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's a deathist? Someone who does or doesn't believe people should strive for longer lives?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's people who are okay with the idea of dying.<br /> <br /> Urban Dictionary says it's <a href=\"http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=deathism\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-08-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:17:03-07:00","id":946501,"title":"","content":"Gotcha.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of people coming at this for a lot of different reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:24:28-07:00","id":946507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946427#post946427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what Charlaquin is saying, I suppose there's more of a problem with how the alternatives and the little explicit room given to those are addressed?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few different problems that different people have. It seems <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> and others who don't care for the humanist themes in Promethean are seeing the generally unsympathetic presentation of Alchemists as one more item on the laundry list of issues they take with the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> Others, such as myself, are fine with the generally unsympathetic portrayal of Alchemists in the core book, but would like to see a more nuanced take on them in the future. Unfortunately, the places where it seems like the book was trying to leave room for that ended up coming off to some of us as shutting down that potential rather than opening it up.<br /> <br /> In particular, one of the primary reasons <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> started this thread in the first place was a sidebar that appears to be an attempt to explain that the reason this section is so down on Alchemists is that it's focused on the alchemists that Prometheans are most likely to encounter - the ones who are so obsessed with transcending humanity that they are willing to hunt down, maim, and kill Prometheans for their Pyros and Vitriol. After all, if they weren't so obsessed, they'd probably be avoiding Prometheans, because the divine fire in them is dangerous, and a wise Alchemist would want to stay away from it.<br /> <br /> That's all well and good, the problem is it talks in very polarizing terms of &quot;rational, sane Alchemists&quot; and &quot;Insatiate&quot; Alchemists, which is what the &quot;sane&quot; ones call the ones that kill Prometheans. It makes it sound like there are exactly two kinds of alchemists: the perfectly reasonable, decent human beings who Prometheans will never run into, and the power-hungry, insane Vitriol addicts who will tear a Promethean open as soon as look at zir. No room is left for a spectrum of Alchemists, who might be driven by desperation, or curiosity, or otherwise justifying Promethean slaughter to themselves &quot;just this once&quot;. It reads like Insatiety is an on/off switch rather than a road paved with good intentions. For such a humanist game, it's ironically reluctant to play up the deeply human qualities that might drive an Alchemist from rational to Insatiate.<br /> <br /> I also have a problem with a particular passage that talks about what sort of antagonistic role Alchemists fill in the game. It explains that they are often a physical threat, posing the danger of violence and bodily harm against the protagonists, but if that were all they had to offer, that role could be filled by pandorans. What sets them apart is that they are intelligent, rational(ish), and most importantly, tragic. They mirror Prometheans as humans on a sort of Pilgrimage to leave humanity behind, which can call a lot of a Promethean's values into question. &quot;This human was born with the thing I want so badly, and they're willing to butcher and mutilate me just to get rid of it. Maybe being human isn't so much better than being a monster after all, if this human so desprate not to be one.&quot; It even says that this theme is strengthened when a reoccurring Alchemist antagonist doesn't start out wanting to murder the Throng and suck the Vitriolic marrow from their bones, but gets to that point more gradually.<br /> <br /> Again, all well and good, but then the examples it gives of possible motivations for such characters are:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe she claims that she is trying to escape the world of alchemy but needs some Pyros to pull off one last preparation. Maybe she wants to learn something from the Prometheans before she guts them, so she pretends to have a different motivation. Black alchemists are obsessives, addicts, users, and abusers; chances are good that any who try to talk to Prometheans are deluding themselves, the throng, or even both. </div> </div> </div>That's not a character who doesn't start out wanting to kill the Throng. That's a character who starts out wanting to kill the throng but lies about it to give himself a better shot at it. Which is a perfectly valid way to run an Alchemist antagonist, but it's not the nuanced take the rest of the paragraph seemed like it was trying to discuss. It really reads like it's trying to make Alchemists into complex characters, but is afraid to do so in a way that might make you empathize with them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-08-2016, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:04:07-07:00","id":946527,"title":"","content":"I can't tell exactly how much these tendencies in the presentation would bother me since I don't have the actual text, but I can see why people would be unsatisfied when you put it like that. It sounds as if the book may have some difficulty exploring the Alchemists as sympathetic without running counter to its themes up to that point or offering exploration that makes them clear enemies for the titular characters. If that's the case, well. It's a complex subject that may be difficult to parse entirely well in a limited space, even if it is otherwise adequate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-08-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:55:26-07:00","id":946548,"title":"","content":"I'm with ArcaneArts on their first point, it's pretty easy to turn these guys playable or make them sympathetic.<br /> <br /> For sympathetic causes, the Emerald Crucible seems like the 'nicest' of the groups, providing you're not a Promethean. The others use some of the usual ways to paint them badly, one being religious zealots, another being racist and sexist 1%ers, Amalgama is an evil corporation run by sociopaths, the last are ghouls throwing themselves into 'monstrous transhumanism.'<br /> <br /> But you still have to get past a lot of the wording and portrayal. From the start, alchemists don't seem like particularly scary antagonists. They seem repulsive, but it's a repulsive to general reader sensibilities, not necessarily the Promethean, for whom they're just a different shade of asshole trying to steal their Vitriol. If alchemists are not too busy killing each other, they want you, but even then they're so pathetic the game actually has to warn you you can make them too pathetic.<br /> <br /> 'The Storyteller should be as sadistic as possible without crippling the alchemist to the point that she is no longer a threat to the Prometheans she hunts. Alchemists are foils for Prometheans because of how they ruin and degrade their bodies and minds for the sake of power.'<br /> <br /> Is this something that happened in playtesting?<br /> <br /> I'm aware that Promethean and Werewolf are different games, even if they are pronounced the same. But looking at the antagonist sections for werewolf, the enemies are more intimidating for their aspirations, their methods. Some might be right, some are fulfilling ancient purpose, some are justifiably angry against werewolves. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, 'black' alchemists are wretched on so many levels and just plain wrong. 'The fact is that insatiate alchemy is a dead end.'<br /> <br /> We get it, they're bad. But some of the paragraphs spent talking about how evil they are could be spent making them interesting. The rich ones or corporation could use their resources to tag Prometheans out in the field, watching for when they meet up with others and harvesting Vitriol only to let them go again until they may have replenished it. The Lodowick Society could be trying to dig up all evidence of the Prophets lineage. They could be more than Vitriol-thieves and you could encounter them in more situations than them trying to steal your Vitriol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-08-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:09:59-07:00","id":946554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946429#post946429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inigo Montoya says: &quot;If the post I was responding to was sarcastic, that would mean you were saying that the Ordo Dracul and alchemists aren't actually monsters. Also, I was agreeing with you that they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> And no, it doesn't. Because it railroads you into only having the choice to either become human or Be A Bad Point-Misser Who Is Playing Wrong. And in a horror setting, &quot;humans are special&quot; just doesn't work for me. Especially since every other Chronicles of Darkness book emphasizes how awful humans can be.<br /> <br /> Back to alchemists, I would advise everyone (in general and on this thread) to read/watch Baccano for a sympathetic portrayal of immortal alchemists. As a bonus, there's a character who could easily be a Promethean, and she ends up in a happy relationship with an alchemically-immortal human without having to become human herself. It even has Slashers and an Unchained (although that particular character was revealed in a sidestory to be more like an incredibly ancient and powerful Promethean).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Searched it on the forums, and ironically enough some of the most vocal deathists here are fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't pretty much the only real alchemist in the show the bad guy, while other immortals are pretty much people who accidentally drank the potion? I don't know much about Promethean (reading these threads to wage if it's worth trying out 2nd ed), but I feel that citing Baccano here is counter productive to your cause - like, characters are alchemically-immortal, but aside of people on the ship (and they are ...problematic), Szilard (who is THE evil alchemist) and Maiza (who is basically &quot;repentant Alchemist who saw error of his ways&quot;), who do you consider a capital A Alchemist in the show? <br /> Being alchemically modified doesn't make you an Alchemist. Witcher Geralt dabbles in elixirs made from monsters he kills, and yet he is not an Alchemist. This game seems to have very specific definition of what it means as Alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:13:02-07:00","id":946556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946554#post946554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know much about Promethean (reading these threads to wage if it's worth trying out 2nd ed)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a heads-up about this, the alchemist section and their relevance in the game is a small part of the book, about seven and a half pages out of more than three hundred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:21:38-07:00","id":946559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=943151#post943151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then don't reply to them? The topic is &quot;I am dissatisfied with the presentation of alchemists and wanted to share my thoughts on the matter, and invite others to share their own thoughts on it.&quot; If you don't have anything to say on the subject, you don't have to say anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> dont those who are content with things as they stand get to add their 2 cents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:25:56-07:00","id":946562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946559#post946559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dont those who are content with things as they stand get to add their 2 cents?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Yes? That would constitute having something to say on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:46:36-07:00","id":946582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946554#post946554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being alchemically modified doesn't make you an Alchemist. Witcher Geralt dabbles in elixirs made from monsters he kills, and yet he is not an Alchemist. This game seems to have very specific definition of what it means as Alchemist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version is that a Capitol-A Alchemist is a human who can steal Pyros from the Principle. It's not entirely clear what allows some humans to do this, but it seems to be related to their obsession with transcending humanity, much like a Demiurge's obsession with creating new life allows them to steal enough of the Divine Fire to create a Promethean. In mechanical terms, an Alchemist is someone with Magnitude, a sort of mini-power stat that goes from 1 to 5 and determines how much Pyros they can generate per week, how much of it they can store at a time (in the form of alchemical preparations), how much they can spend in a turn, and how many Distillations they can know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:26:52-07:00","id":946607,"title":"","content":"Well, Baccano isn't so much about the alchemists being great, I admit, but it's heavily into immortality and not being human as both being states that it's possible to find peace and belonging in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:27:19-07:00","id":946608,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not reading through this thread because a) it's a rant and those stress me out and b) I don't really agree with the premise (which seems to be that I should have devoted precious word count to making secondary antagonist characters playable), but I do want to say this: I don't have any problem with people wanting to play alchemists. I don't think it necessarily steps on the themes of the game in the same way that, say, playing Heroes in <b>Beast</b> does, and if you want to add an XP chart and do it, you definitely have my completely unnecessary blessing. Hell, if I get to do a PG, I might even include playable-alchemist rules. <i>Maybe</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:31:42-07:00","id":946614,"title":"","content":"That's good to know, but I don't really think that's what the issue was. PD and others have acknowledged that Alchemists are more or less playable, and we're not even asking for more content about them- we're just objecting to an aspect of the content there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:09:39-07:00","id":946721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946608#post946608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm not reading through this thread because a) it's a rant and those stress me out</div> </div> </div> </div>I Don't blame you, that seems like it would be pretty stressful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946608#post946608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and b) I don't really agree with the premise (which seems to be that I should have devoted precious word count to making secondary antagonist characters playable),</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is the premise. It's certainly not what I was trying to say, and I don't thing it was what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> was either. They're already pretty close to playable for those who want that, and the critique I and some others had wasn't about wordcount not being spent on making Alchemists sympathetic, but about wordcount having been used on quashing the potential for more nuanced portrayals of alchemists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946608#post946608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I do want to say this: I don't have any problem with people wanting to play alchemists. I don't think it necessarily steps on the themes of the game in the same way that, say, playing Heroes in <b>Beast</b> does, and if you want to add an XP chart and do it, you definitely have my completely unnecessary blessing. Hell, if I get to do a PG, I might even include playable-alchemist rules. <i>Maybe</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:43:29-07:00","id":946915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946429#post946429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inigo Montoya says: &quot;If the post I was responding to was sarcastic, that would mean you were saying that the Ordo Dracul and alchemists aren't actually monsters. Also, I was agreeing with you that they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> And no, it doesn't. Because it railroads you into only having the choice to either become human or Be A Bad Point-Misser Who Is Playing Wrong. And in a horror setting, &quot;humans are special&quot; just doesn't work for me. Especially since every other Chronicles of Darkness book emphasizes how awful humans can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still is a horrible journey. Take the universal milestone to achieve the new dawn: to beget another of your kind. Even binary choices contain nuance. Consider falling to flux because you refuse to inflict your fate on another?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946429#post946429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to alchemists, I would advise everyone (in general and on this thread) to read/watch Baccano for a sympathetic portrayal of immortal alchemists. As a bonus, there's a character who could easily be a Promethean, and she ends up in a happy relationship with an alchemically-immortal human without having to become human herself. It even has Slashers and an Unchained (although that particular character was revealed in a sidestory to be more like an incredibly ancient and powerful Promethean).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Searched it on the forums, and ironically enough some of the most vocal deathists here are fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant. Not the media, or the themes we're trying to explore with the game as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:48:30-07:00","id":946969,"title":"","content":"Gonna be honest, I'm not entirely sure what you're saying here. And &quot;irrelevant&quot; is a funny word to throw around when you're talking about media inspiration. You probably don't consider Breaking Bad to be close to the themes of Promethean, but it's something I would recommend to anyone playing an alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:49:26-07:00","id":946970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946223#post946223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep! And this is a horror game, so I'm completely fine with the pursuit of power and immortality turning you into a horrible monster.<br /> <br /> It's just that this is a game about being monsters, and as horrible as the Ordo Dracul they're not just fully playable but incredibly sympathetic. In fact, you could make a case that they're the &quot;most lesser evil&quot; among the Covenants, in that their end goal would be the most beneficial to humanity. That doesn't make them not monsters, but it makes them twisted vampire mad scientists that someone could look at and think, &quot;this is a shitty situation and these guys are making the best of it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because that's the other side of &quot;it's a horror setting&quot;. Things kind of suck. You could die or be hollowed out by magic rats at any moment through no fault of your own. You're a weak, squishy, ignorant nobody. &quot;Evening the odds&quot; has been brought up before, but it bears repeating. ChroD is a dark, scary setting, and the games hammer home that you often have to do things you'll regret to survive. It isn't just the monsters- Hunters can do horrific things, break law after law, and modify themselves into something inhuman, but the alternative is to just lie down and be complacent cattle for the monsters.<br /> <br /> That, to me, is the best way to look at alchemists sympathetically while also keeping them twisted and monstrous.<br /> <br /> They are the ones who didn't lie down.<br /> <br /> Hunters are the people who saw monsters preying on humanity, and didn't lie down. Alchemists saw diseases, aging, and death preying on humanity, and didn't lie down. Both of them work with powers they don't understand and do things that are hard to justify, but the alternative is, well, death. The Hunter says she refuses to let some Draugr drink her or her friends dry. The alchemist says she refuses to let cancer or aging or an accident bring her or her friends down. Both light a candle. They may burn out. Their fire may burn out of control. In fact, those things are probably likely. But without them, darkness is all there would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>But death aging and diseases are not supposed to be avoided. Death is also part of of life,trying to rise above it is wrong. That's the alchemists mistake,they don't want to accept death and disease as part of nature,part of life. They think they are too special and awesome to suck it up and accept things as they are. They are not refusing to lie down like a hunter would.n they're refusing being content","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:55:54-07:00","id":946976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946970#post946970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But death aging and diseases are not supposed to be avoided. Death is also part of of life,trying to rise above it is wrong. That's the alchemists mistake,they don't want to accept death and disease as part of nature,part of life. They think they are too special and awesome to suck it up and accept things as they are. They are not refusing to lie down like a hunter would.n they're refusing being content</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation needed. If you're going to be a deathist, at least try to come up with something more creative. <br /> <br /> By the way, if diseases are a part of life we should accept, does that mean that vaccines and disinfectant are bad? Are all doctors twisted mad scientists because they defy the natural order by saving people who should have died?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:58:16-07:00","id":946977,"title":"","content":"If diseases weren't supposed to be fought and death should be accepted, I literally wouldn't be born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:02:40-07:00","id":946982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946976#post946976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Citation needed. If you're going to be a deathist, at least try to come up with something more creative.<br /> <br /> By the way, if diseases are a part of life we should accept, does that mean that vaccines and disinfectant are bad? Are all doctors twisted mad scientists because they defy the natural order by saving people who should have died?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I offended,not my intention. What I meant,is that ,maybe an Alchemist would be happier just accepting things as they are instead of hurting others and himself trying to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:06:01-07:00","id":946984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946982#post946982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I offended,not my intention. What I meant,is that ,maybe an Alchemist would be happier just accepting things as they are instead of hurting others and himself trying to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside the ethical concerns of the situation, you can't really have a story if your character just accepts everything and doesn't try to change it. To go back to Breaking Bad, there's no story if Walter just decides he's fine with dying and leaving his family in poverty. <br /> <br /> &quot;My character's motivation to become an alchemist was to cure her cancer.&quot;<br /> &quot;Sounds good, there's a lot of potential for conflict and development there.&quot;<br /> &quot;But then she decided to just accept her slow and agonizing depth and decided that she shouldn't risk trying to fight it.&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay, uh, that's not really going to work.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:08:07-07:00","id":946985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946984#post946984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting aside the ethical concerns of the situation, you can't really have a story if your character just accepts everything and doesn't try to change it. To go back to Breaking Bad, there's no story if Walter just decides he's fine with dying and leaving his family in poverty.<br /> <br /> &quot;My character's motivation to become an alchemist was to cure her cancer.&quot;<br /> &quot;Sounds good, there's a lot of potential for conflict and development there.&quot;<br /> &quot;But then she decided to just accept her slow and agonizing depth and decided that she shouldn't risk trying to fight it.&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay, uh, that's not really going to work.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man,you're right. Damn,I think i was being close minded here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:17:10-07:00","id":946988,"title":"","content":"We have to remember, we're not talking about real people. We aren't talking about whether actions and qualities are morally good in real life, we're talking about whether they would create a compelling character to roleplay.<br /> <br /> I personally think that pursuing immortality and human enhancement in real life is a worthwhile and noble goal, but that belief isn't central to this topic because real life isn't a supernatural horror setting. Human immortality and transhumanism in real life do not involve hunting frankenstoids and alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:19:26-07:00","id":946990,"title":"","content":"I feel something's been overlooked here. Non-supernal magic.<br /> <br /> You can buy youth at a Goblin Market. It's not risk free, but Mages should have a fair chance of pulling it off. There's a Contract in 1E Changeling that trades 7 years younger for a Willpower dot, that's a very good exchange rate even when you account for the Goblin Merchant who you're paying to use it on you adds a markup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:23:36-07:00","id":946995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946990#post946990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel something's been overlooked here. Non-supernal magic.<br /> <br /> You can buy youth at a Goblin Market. It's not risk free, but Mages should have a fair chance of pulling it off. There's a Contract in 1E Changeling that trades 7 years younger for a Willpower dot, that's a very good exchange rate even when you account for the Goblin Merchant who you're paying to use it on you adds a markup.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's assuming that setting elements from first edition Changeling even exist in your game of second edition Promethean. <br /> <br /> Also, if you're a chemist or an alchemist and you want to live forever, your first impulse isn't going to be &quot;I'm going to find out if goblins are real and buy youth from them because they could probably totally do that&quot;, it's to try to use mad science to give yourself eternal life. <br /> <br /> This isn't a &quot;best way to become immortal in ChroD&quot; thread, it's an &quot;alchemists got a bad break in Promethean 2e&quot; thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-09-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:28:38-07:00","id":947004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946995#post946995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's assuming that setting elements from first edition Changeling even exist in your game of second edition Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> Also, I posted this in the wrong thread. It's supposed to be in the Mage immortality thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T16:10:47-07:00","id":947300,"title":"","content":"I guess one of my main problems with &quot;humanism&quot; the way Promethean uses it is that I've never felt much of a connection to humanity or a feeling that it's a particularly wonderful state. The way defenders of the game describe what it's like to be a Promethean sounds like the way I feel a lot of the time. They talk about how wonderful it is that humans have stability and belonging, but somehow despite being human I never really wound up with anything like that. <br /> <br /> One of the reasons why I push the &quot;ChroD should be about being a monster and coming to terms with it&quot; rule so hard is because I identify much more with monsters than with heroes. I can't relate to enlightened superbeings, I can't relate to people who think humanity is just the greatest thing ever, and so on. That's why the massive focus on the Pilgrimage is such a letdown for me. Because it obliterates the reason why I loved Frankenstein so much, and why I related so strongly to the Creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:47:09-07:00","id":947352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947300#post947300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess one of my main problems with &quot;humanism&quot; the way Promethean uses it is that I've never felt much of a connection to humanity or a feeling that it's a particularly wonderful state. The way defenders of the game describe what it's like to be a Promethean sounds like the way I feel a lot of the time. They talk about how wonderful it is that humans have stability and belonging, but somehow despite being human I never really wound up with anything like that. One of the reasons why I push the &quot;ChroD should be about being a monster and coming to terms with it&quot; rule so hard is because I identify much more with monsters than with heroes. I can't relate to enlightened superbeings, I can't relate to people who think humanity is just the greatest thing ever, and so on. That's why the massive focus on the Pilgrimage is such a letdown for me. Because it obliterates the reason why I loved Frankenstein so much, and why I related so strongly to the Creature.</div> </div> </div> </div> Stick to the refinement of Flux, then. That's literally embracing the monster. That's literally treated with the same respect as any other refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:00:05-07:00","id":947360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947352#post947352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Stick to the refinement of Flux, then. That's literally embracing the monster. That's literally treated with the same respect as any other refinement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Centimani are called &quot;Freak&quot; and consort with wild beasts that subsist by eating Prometheans, I get the feeling other Created don't really put them on even footing with the other Refinements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:06:49-07:00","id":947368,"title":"","content":"Or just... move on and play games that suit you more? I mean, the CofD have a ton of game lines. The list is almost ridiculously massive (like, I'm constantly surprised that they announce new game lines since it seems so hard to find new narrative space). Promethean's take on humanism doesn't strike your fancy? OK. There are lots of games that don't do that. Just because Promethean is related to Frankenstein doesn't mean it has some sole claim on Frankenstein inspired characters.<br /> <br /> I get being disappointed when expectations and reality don't mesh, but that should always be put in perspective. Promethean has always been about the Pilgrimage. Why expect 2e to change it? It seems, in context, that it isn't a very reasonable expectation. Which means you just set yourself up for disappointment.<br /> <br /> Also,the idea that the CofD games all need to be about, &quot;being a monster and coming to terms with it,&quot; doesn't really hold any water. There's always been a scale of focus on this. Some games have this as a central theme, most of the games tend to gloss over the &quot;coming to terms with it,&quot; part as something that PCs have generally already done, and some games don't actually have you play a monster as the default in the first place.<br /> <br /> If what you like about the CofD/when you feel it is at its strongest for you is when it's pushing that theme, that's awesome. Just respect that it doesn't need to be that for everyone to be that for you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:07:36-07:00","id":947369,"title":"","content":"If you want a game about embracing your otherness in a rejection of the world, play Beast. If you want a game about discovering how your otherness can actually bring you into an embrace of the world, and to be embraced in return, play Promethean.<br /> <br /> The world was a lonelier place when I hated people. That's all I'll say.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:20:19-07:00","id":947375,"title":"","content":"The problem is, Beast isn't anything like what I'm looking for. And it lacks the atmosphere and style and rich vein of source material that Promethean has. I guess I'm a bit overly possessive of the Creature, since he's my all-time favorite monster.<br /> <br /> At least all of this is giving me the motivation to finally get The Lightning Chronicle done, since then I can fix all of this and make the game of my dreams. And Promethean straight up tells you that you can only find a place in the world by removing your &quot;otherness&quot;, which doesn't appeal to me in the slightest. And I maintain that all ChroD lines should be about being a monster in some way. And I wouldn't say I hate people so much as I don't think humanity is overall that great. There's a difference. There are plenty of people I like, I just wish they weren't stuck in perpetually oozing, reeking, decaying hunks of meat. <br /> <br /> But we're off topic. How about some inspiration for playing alchemists? Quite honestly, I can't think of anything that does that quite as well as Breaking Bad. I will forever maintain that BB is the single best modern exploration of the mad scientist archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:24:38-07:00","id":947378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947300#post947300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess one of my main problems with &quot;humanism&quot; the way Promethean uses it is that I've never felt much of a connection to humanity or a feeling that it's a particularly wonderful state. The way defenders of the game describe what it's like to be a Promethean sounds like the way I feel a lot of the time. They talk about how wonderful it is that humans have stability and belonging, but somehow despite being human I never really wound up with anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the thing to look out for here is that Promethean is both exploring that place of being the other who doesn't have that sense of stability and belonging, and it seems to be about (which it sounds like is something you identify with) and its about finding that among people. It doesn't necessarily mean hunting city to city until you find the loving family that accepts you for who you are. It seems that Promethean is more interested in you learning about yourself and accepting who <i>you </i>are, the good, bad and ugly. That's the sense I get from the way the Pilgrimage is laid out. Learning about humans, acting like them and becoming one of them is more a process of self-knowledge mediated through experiencing the myriad of situations life offers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947300#post947300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons why I push the &quot;ChroD should be about being a monster and coming to terms with it&quot; rule so hard is because I identify much more with monsters than with heroes. I can't relate to enlightened superbeings, I can't relate to people who think humanity is just the greatest thing ever, and so on. That's why the massive focus on the Pilgrimage is such a letdown for me. Because it obliterates the reason why I loved Frankenstein so much, and why I related so strongly to the Creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Promethean's interest in humanity is as cognizant of the flaws as it is the things which are genuinely aspirational. Perhaps a better way to think of Promethean is to not understand it as a game about escaping monstrousness, or if you want to change it, into a game about accepting the fact that you're a monster. It's a game about accepting and coming to terms with humanity, and oneself. So while the metaphor of the monstrousness is present, it's moreso about personality identity than the state of being a monster.<br /> <br /> It's not about becoming an enlightened superhero or even some platonic ideal of a person. It's about self-knowledge in the context of humanity, and that's reflected by the transformation from Promethean to mortal.<br /> <br /> There's a particular thing you're doing here that I think happens a lot with fiction and monstrousness, others and self-knowledge. I'll try to think about how to articulate it, but I think the short of it is that there's baggage you're bringing to the language of the book that makes it harder to parse and consequently harder to enjoy.<br /> <br /> I think it's a thing we all do, especially with the sorts of large metaphors and thematic spaces the Chronicles of Darkness explore. I don't know if it's possible to approach these concepts <i>without </i>the baggage we bring, so maybe a better way to do it might be to give it some time and come back to it? Obviously that's your prerogative, I just think it might be worth thinking about what biases you're bringing to the text, and considering how to work with/around those.<br /> <br /> Like, as a queer person of color, there was a way I reacted to <i>Beast </i>that I think was really unfounded upon thinking about it, and I think a lot of people did similar, and because it touches a lot of sensitive buttons on the baggage we carry, it made it a bit harder to appreciate. I still see some things that I think are weaknesses, but looking at it again I think there are a lot of problems with the way people engage with <i>Beast</i>.<br /> <br /> I think the same thing happens with some of the words used to describe Alchemists, where there's a knee-jerk reaction that makes it harder to appreciate, and I think it's worth considering that if one considers this a &quot;failure&quot; then it might be one that both we as readers and the text can both take responsibility for. Incidentally, this also goes for <i>Beast</i> since I mentioned it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 08-09-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:28:40-07:00","id":947380,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about something: a person earlier in the thread described the whole journey and theme of Promethean The Created as ultimately - orthogonal to the matter of humanism vs transhumanism - being easily read as the desire to surpass the circumstances of your birth.<br /> <br /> Which strikes a cord, because when you think about it, transhumanism and by inclusion the want to improve ourselves and make our lives better, are very human things. But just because we define the first humanocentrically, doesn't mean we're the only intelligent beings the idea ought to resonate with. If the book was written with that interpretation in mind, we would likely have a different (less divisive) focus which wouldn't see a need to single out some Alchemists as obvious villains. In the end, I see many of them looking for the same thing as Prometheans; the latter have reason to idolize and pursue mankind, while the former have reasons and drive to surpass it as it is. But, as already commented on, it's very much a &quot;the grass is greener on the other side of the fence&quot; thing, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Too bad the most reliable way for Alchemists to chase that goal is to grind up Prometheans. Which should be enough to promote conflict! There doesn't really need to be a fundamental clash of philosophy between them or an integral difference in the inherent value of what they respectively seek. The differing perspectives and incompatible priorities in what they're willing to do to achieve their goals ought to suffice to establish the Alchemists as complex but clear antagonists for the titular characters.<br /> <br /> (Bear in mind, I'm sharing these thoughts having not read the book, which is why I haven't added anything to the discussion of what what the definition of antagonistic alchemists implies about people with mental illness; the criticisms that the wording is insensitive or insulting seem valid to me, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-09-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:44:34-07:00","id":947386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947360#post947360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Centimani are called &quot;Freak&quot; and consort with wild beasts that subsist by eating Prometheans, I get the feeling other Created don't really put them on even footing with the other Refinements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking in terms of narrative. I'm talking editorially.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947375#post947375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're off topic. How about some inspiration for playing alchemists? Quite honestly, I can't think of anything that does that quite as well as Breaking Bad. I will forever maintain that BB is the single best modern exploration of the mad scientist archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing mad about the exploits of Walter White. He's extremely sapient, deliberate and rational. Even when he tries to appear otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-09-2016, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:49:40-07:00","id":947392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947386#post947386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing mad about the exploits of Walter White. He's extremely sapient, deliberate and rational. Even when he tries to appear otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know how much Walter White speaks to the mad scientist beyond a surface level of chemical/scientific affectation. His story seems more like the broadly archetypal quest for power, corruption and all that yadda yadda which has more to do with people than with the science that may or may not have been involved in the show. You can see how it became such a hit with people since it's a story about that rather than one about mad science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:07:51-07:00","id":947406,"title":"","content":"Nah. Walter White is a total mad scientist. His motivation is ultimately born out of resentment, the feeling that his genius was never recognized. The way the mad part comes in is that Walter's insecurities and thirst for power end up sabotaging his logical side. He could have the sinecure from Grey Matter and solved all of his problems. But he didn't, because he can never forgive Elliot, because he blames Elliot for never getting the recognition he thought he deserved. Walter repeatedly sabotages himself because he doesn't just want money, he wants to be recognized as the genius he thinks he is. <br /> <br /> Example: Telling Hank that he doesn't think Gale was Heisenberg is an incredibly illogical and risky move, but he does it because his own burning thirst to be recognized won't let him allow someone else to be given credit for his accomplishments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:28:22-07:00","id":947422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947406#post947406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. Walter White is a total mad scientist. His motivation is ultimately born out of resentment, the feeling that his genius was never recognized. The way the mad part comes in is that Walter's insecurities and thirst for power end up sabotaging his logical side. He could have the sinecure from Grey Matter and solved all of his problems. But he didn't, because he can never forgive Elliot, because he blames Elliot for never getting the recognition he thought he deserved. Walter repeatedly sabotages himself because he doesn't just want money, he wants to be recognized as the genius he thinks he is.<br /> <br /> Example: Telling Hank that he doesn't think Gale was Heisenberg is an incredibly illogical and risky move, but he does it because his own burning thirst to be recognized won't let him allow someone else to be given credit for his accomplishments.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those examples characterize madness. Psychological issues best addressed to a therapist? Sure. Madness? Not at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:56:08-07:00","id":947437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947422#post947422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of those examples characterize madness. Psychological issues best addressed to a therapist? Sure. Madness? Not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mad scientist&quot; does not literally mean &quot;a scientist who is mentally ill&quot;. It implies a pattern of behavior and a character arc that Walter White fits perfectly. Walter's obsession with getting the recognition he believes he is owed isn't fundamentally different than, say, Lex Luthor or Rusty Venture's motivations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:19:59-07:00","id":947449,"title":"","content":"Has anyone ever explored the idea of a <i>Redeemed</i> becoming an Alchemist? I'm working on a character for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency\">this thread</a> of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s that's based on that concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:36:50-07:00","id":947456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947449#post947449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever explored the idea of a <i>Redeemed</i> becoming an Alchemist? I'm working on a character for <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency&amp;quot;]this</a> thread[/URL] of <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s that's based on that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it. &quot;Shit, turns out being human kind of sucks. Right, time for Pilgrimage 2.0.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:09:54-07:00","id":947465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947449#post947449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever explored the idea of a <i>Redeemed</i> becoming an Alchemist? I'm working on a character for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency\">this thread</a> of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s that's based on that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty straightforward; there's nothing mutually exclusive about the two options. Though I do think that Redeemed who chose to forget their prior existence would arguably be a little more likely to choose this route, as they wouldn't have the memories of the Pilgrimage to remind them of just how much better off they are now \u2014 and conversely, they'd be more prone to thinking of Prometheans as things that can be destroyed and ground up to serve their purpose when they don't remember <i>being</i> a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:41:59-07:00","id":947482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947465#post947465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty straightforward; there's nothing mutually exclusive about the two options. Though I do think that Redeemed who chose to forget their prior existence would arguably be a little more likely to choose this route, as they wouldn't have the memories of the Pilgrimage to remind them of just how much better off they are now \u2014 and conversely, they'd be more prone to thinking of Prometheans as things that can be destroyed and ground up to serve their purpose when they don't remember <i>being</i> a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, a Redeemed Alchemist who does remember his past life would make for an interesting character, whether or not they're antagonistic towards Created. One could act as a guide for Prometheans in their Pilgrimages, inspiring them as a sort of <i>bodhisattva</i>. Another tries to reclaim some of the power he had to defend himself against an old supernatural adversary, and he ultimately damns himself with each Created he victimizes to get what he needs.<br /> <br /> Also, those rare Redeemed who retain use of an Alembic also have a unique advantage at their disposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:44:20-07:00","id":947485,"title":"","content":"Remember, there's no reason why a Redeemed alchemist wouldn't find himself preferring his old &quot;life&quot;. Going back to unusual sources of inspiration, the New Dawn has always made me think of the ending of Goodfellas. &quot;Now I get to live the rest of my life like a schnook.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:37:13-07:00","id":947530,"title":"","content":"Yeah; you basically said that in your last post, and I get that you don't like Promethean's central theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:56:31-07:00","id":947673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947530#post947530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; you basically said that in your last post, and I get that you don't like Promethean's central theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you can have a theme and still have a compelling character who rejects the central theme of a game. In-game you can have characters who are wrong. You can even have characters who reject the game's central theme and not even portray them as explicitly wrong <i>or</i> even villainous and still have them work. You just need to trust that your theme is compelling enough in its own right to not fall off the rails at a single false flag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:42:13-07:00","id":947866,"title":"","content":"Isn't that the sort of thing the Centimani do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:16:58-07:00","id":947893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947866#post947866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that the sort of thing the Centimani do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is literally their editorial purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:16:31-07:00","id":947944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947866#post947866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that the sort of thing the Centimani do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Centimani are Prometheans rejecting Humanity. Alchemists are Humans rejecting Humanity (to varying degrees, maybe), so there is that difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:38:46-07:00","id":947958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=947482#post947482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, a Redeemed Alchemist who does remember his past life would make for an interesting character, whether or not they're antagonistic towards Created. One could act as a guide for Prometheans in their Pilgrimages, inspiring them as a sort of <i>bodhisattva</i>. Another tries to reclaim some of the power he had to defend himself against an old supernatural adversary, and he ultimately damns himself with each Created he victimizes to get what he needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were examples of that in 1e. The previously mentioned redemmed alchemist from Waters of Life (think that was the name). But more darkly, the original demo had a redemmed who was using her patchy memory of being a Promethean to drain vitriol from captured Prometheans in order to make clones or something like that. Not sure if that counts as Alchemy as such, but it's a really interesting dynamic. Come to think of it, wasn't she being blackmailed by a centimani into doing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:33:19-07:00","id":948192,"title":"","content":"On alchemists and insanity. I find it rather interesting (at least to me) that the Conditions that the alchemists suffer from are Addiction and Obsession. They're like miniture mages here, just powered by Pyros instead of the Supernal. Its like... mages are obsessive, mad creators who give metaphorical birth to flawed creations. Meanwhile, Prometheans ARE the flawed creations that have issues with their obsessed creators. A rather interesting dichotomy, akin to vampires and werewolves, a cycle that is eternally destined to butt heads against each other because they're really flip sides of the same coin. <br /> <br /> <br /> From my personal perspective, the difference between the so-called &quot;nice&quot; and &quot;bad&quot; alchemists are like the divide between the Pentacle and Seers - in short, Wisdom to know when to not exploit living creatures for your own profit and benefit. Both mages and alchemists are basically trans-humanists that magically enhance their bodies into something more than humans. Both push themselves into grand magical conspiracies. Honestly, the only real difference to me is one relies on pyros, and the other on mana. By the same token, if you made pyros and mana the same thing, then you could run the game with mages replacing the alchemists!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:06:51-07:00","id":948259,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 Supernal mages are a heck of a lot more powerful than Pyros alchemists. But thematically? You might be on to something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:32:40-07:00","id":948442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=948192#post948192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the only real difference to me is one relies on pyros, and the other on mana. By the same token, if you made pyros and mana the same thing, then you could run the game with mages replacing the alchemists!</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fullmetal Alchemist</b> made this already in 2003 year! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Dsa8j_usqI\" data-code=\"2Dsa8j_usqI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2Dsa8j_usqI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> ( P.S. It's also basis of my <b>Promethean</b> subplot in alchemical <b>Mage</b> game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:11:28-07:00","id":948476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=948259#post948259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well\u2026 Supernal mages are a heck of a lot more powerful than Pyros alchemists. But thematically? You might be on to something.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, Supernal magic is pretty much disasterously more powerful than pretty much everyone else in the CofD, save other mages and high ranking spirits. That's always been a giant issue when it comes to crossovers - how many times have people said that mages are inappriopriate? Even Mr. Brookshaw has stated that mages are inappropriate for <i>antagonists in a hunter game</i>. And the whole point of the Vigil is to hunt down other supernaturals. You have to make watered down versions for it to be playable. And that's exactly what we have in alchemists - watered down mages that fit nicer into other games.<br /> <br /> But that's another matter for another day. I'm absolutely looking forwards to the Crossover Chronicle book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-11-2016, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:32:11-07:00","id":948478,"title":"","content":"duplicate, please ignore<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:39:27-07:00","id":949281,"title":"","content":"Semi-relevant to this thread. I'm working on some small rule hacks for Alchemists in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uLuP3_Bu8ROO2181eGJMtOGt1Z_Ok7Yz4lzdEDlVnFo/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">this doc</a>. There's also a separate thread for discussing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 08-12-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:23:28-07:00","id":949384,"title":"","content":"Ah, that looks good. I wish you'd done something about the smug fluff, though. That's the main problem- the mechanics are pretty good and pretty much PC-playable, but they need a much less odious narrative wrapped around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:31:28-07:00","id":949394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949384#post949384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, that looks good. I wish you'd done something about the smug fluff, though. That's the main problem- the mechanics are pretty good and pretty much PC-playable, but they need a much less odious narrative wrapped around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff is pretty much a work-in-progress. And I'm hoping that I can improve upon it with whatever suggestions can be sent my way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T14:20:11-07:00","id":949528,"title":"","content":"While I don't have the book yet, while looking over the Open Dev I noticed one of the types of Athanors was the Vitriol Fount, which produces Vitriol. While it also notes that it can take decades to refill once used, I can easily see an Alchemist attempting to capture as many as they can to ensure a sustainable stream of mutagen, possibly trading what little they could spare for favors from the Created (like making more Fonts, perhaps?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:55:22-07:00","id":949742,"title":"","content":"If I were going to critique the game's take on alchemists, it would probably be by saying that the game is really big on alchemy and wants you to think that using it to perfect the self is a really cool and froody thing to do... but basically only if Prometheans are doing it. The game is pretty bland at best about humans using it for any reason, which is kind of odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","user":"Rand Brittain","date":". 08-12-2016, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:07:46-07:00","id":949753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949742#post949742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were going to critique the game's take on alchemists, it would probably be by saying that the game is really big on alchemy and wants you to think that using it to perfect the self is a really cool and froody thing to do... but basically only if Prometheans are doing it. The game is pretty bland at best about humans using it for any reason, which is kind of odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm one of those people with a tendency to associate people with their avatars, so my initial thought was &quot;thank god Jake is here, he's going to show us the way.&quot; Anyway, 100% agree with you. The wider problem is, Promethean has a love affair with the surface trappings and aesthetics of alchemy but not the actual philosophy, so it ends up being pretty janky if you've actually studied perspectives on alchemy. They get some stuff right, but the OP's devs irrational dislike of transhumanism and immortality get in the way. Historical alchemists were very much in favor of immortality. They were basically transhumanist utopians- they believed they could fix society by helping people live forever and curing all diseases. Saint-Germain, perhaps the archetypal alchemist, was famed for his supposed immortality, and was seen as a highly moral, principled, and altruistic man who used his extended life to help others. <br /> <br /> Promethean and Mage toy with gnostic themes, but they're afraid of taking them too far. For example, notice how Dave comes down like a sack of bricks on anyone who suggests that mortality might be part of the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:29:50-07:00","id":949773,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I'd call it an &quot;irrational&quot; dislike of transhumanism, but it does lead to a possibly unintended place where the game approves of transhumanism if you're transforming yourself from something it doesn't like to something it does like, but not vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:39:43-07:00","id":949779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949753#post949753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wider problem is, Promethean has a love affair with the surface trappings and aesthetics of alchemy but not the actual philosophy, so it ends up being pretty janky if you've actually studied perspectives on alchemy. They get some stuff right, but the OP's devs irrational dislike of transhumanism and immortality get in the way. Historical alchemists were very much in favor of immortality. They were basically transhumanist utopians- they believed they could fix society by helping people live forever and curing all diseases. Saint-Germain, perhaps the archetypal alchemist, was famed for his supposed immortality, and was seen as a highly moral, principled, and altruistic man who used his extended life to help others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... That's <i>exactly</i> what mortal alchemists do in Promethean, which is <i>why</i> they're presented as antagonists in a humanist game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:46:06-07:00","id":949783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949779#post949779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... That's <i>exactly</i> what mortal alchemists do in Promethean, which is <i>why</i> they're presented as antagonists in a humanist game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point. Historical alchemical texts and &quot;alchemical culture&quot; mostly presented immortality and transhumanism in an overwhelmingly positive way. Presenting those as negatives isn't true to the spirit of that vein of source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-13-2016, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:07:21-07:00","id":949795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949783#post949783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the point. Historical alchemical texts and &quot;alchemical culture&quot; mostly presented immortality and transhumanism in an overwhelmingly positive way. Presenting those as negatives isn't true to the spirit of alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemy being the tendrils of a self-annihilating zoetrope-sentience dwelling in the fundamental forces of change is also not true to &quot;the spirit of alchemy,&quot; and yet there's the Divine Fire chumming around on the same approximate metaphysical level as the Wyrd and the God-Machine and the aggregate magical-political constituents of the Shadow and the Underworld and all the myriad convergent strains of vampirism re: Monstrous Portfolios of Miraculous Nonsense.<br /> <br /> It is <i>just possible</i> total fidelity to historic alchemical practices is not the primary aim of this game where alchemy is a product of the force that your character has literally in their bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:19:59-07:00","id":949801,"title":"","content":"Realism and verisimilitude are not the same thing. Realism is often tiring and pointless in fiction, while verisimilitude is, if not the Holy Grail of fiction, then a very clear milestone on the way to it.<br /> <br /> But hey, changing the perspective on a subject has never yielded greater enjoyment, enlightenment, wisdom, empathy, understanding or anything worthwhile before in the history of man, am I right? It's all about that fidelity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:27:26-07:00","id":949804,"title":"","content":"What I was mostly getting at was basically what Rand's point was. Even if you don't care about historical alchemy or alchemical philosophy at all, it seems rather silly that alchemy is presented as being only useful in that it allows Prometheans to become human, and that going from Promethean to human is the only state change that is presented as desirable. Going from human to another sort of being is consistently presented as bad (with the possible and inconsistent exception of Mage), and the end result is that alchemy and self-transformation seem like they're only useful if you happen to a Promethean, and also that being a baseline human is the only acceptable type of existence.<br /> <br /> And I'd say that in this case changing the perspective has not provided any empathy or understanding, since the change produces a dominant atmosphere of &quot;neener neener those silly alchemists don't understand how wonderful being human is&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:50:46-07:00","id":949823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949804#post949804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;neener neener&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not now a useful means by which to present a viewpoint that you don't like, nor has it ever been, nor will it ever be, whether for supporting the legitimacy of a claim to have actually considered the position or for any other constructive purpose.<br /> <br /> Losing your humanity in the Chronicles of Darkness means losing some of your claim on your self and gambling more of it away as you accrue more power. Gradually turning into a sockpuppet for Cthugha because you made poor life decisions in the haste of desperation is what folks in the business call a suboptimal investment of resources, in any context, regardless of what grand philosophical pedigree the choice was framed as being a part of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:56:44-07:00","id":949827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949823#post949823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not now a useful means by which to present a viewpoint that you don't like, nor has it ever been, nor will it ever be, whether for supporting the legitimacy of a claim to have actually considered the position or for any other constructive purpose.<br /> <br /> Losing your humanity in the Chronicles of Darkness means losing some of your claim on your self and gambling more of it away as you accrue more power. Gradually turning into a sockpuppet for Cthugha because you made poor life decisions in the haste of desperation is what folks in the business call a suboptimal investment of resources, in any context, regardless of what grand philosophical pedigree the choice was framed as being a part of.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm totally fine with that. It's just that Promethean's all-devouring emphasis on becoming human means that alchemists who trade away their humanity end up being given a lot less sympathy than all the other people in ChroD who do that. Hell, even the possessed in Inferno didn't receive the naked scorn that alchemists get, and they're people who are literally possessed by creatures that exist solely to sin. <br /> <br /> A wider problem is that the &quot;optimism&quot; that people say they like about Promethean doesn't really fit with the horror nature of the setting, and I admit, does not really resonate with me personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:58:08-07:00","id":949829,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is all forgetting that we're playing in the Chronicles of Darkness, which as a default is a bad world.<br /> <br /> One of the unifying themes in all the games is that the pursuit of power - regardless of the justification - has a cost. This cost is generally framed in ethical or moral terms to retain meaning instead of just simple transactions.<br /> <br /> That's where the Promethean/Alchemist ethical divide comes in beyond any claims about the author's &quot;bias.&quot; Prometheans are walking a path that results in sacrificing power, which is why they're allowed a &quot;good,&quot; ending in at least getting to be a spiritually natural human. Alchemists are pursuing power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:01:09-07:00","id":949832,"title":"","content":"I guess I just don't think that in the setting, being a &quot;spiritually natural human&quot; is necessarily that great. Plus, again, I wish the Pilgrimage wasn't so omnipresent. None of the other splats can become human, too, so I'm not sure why Prometheans can. Becoming human isn't a plot element in Frankenstein, so I'm not quite sure where the devs got it, why they made it so central, and why they doubled down on it for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:13:14-07:00","id":949838,"title":"","content":"There are at least three kinds of beings in the ChroD that can legitimately be called \u201cangels\u201d, at least four that can be called \u201cdemons\u201d, and at least two that can be called \u201cfae\u201d. In a similar sense, I don't get why the assumption seems to be that <b>Promethean</b>'s alchemists <i>must</i> span the full range of alchemist concepts. Why can't there be multiple kinds of alchemists in the ChroD, each with its own role and themes? Put another way, Pyros and its assorted phenomena are not the be-all/end-all of alchemy; they're merely the forms best suited to <b>Promethean</b>'s themes. <br /> <br /> That said, Matt <i>has</i> acknowledged that playable (and, by implication, relatable) alchemists are something that's at least <i>compatible with</i> PtC2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:15:04-07:00","id":949842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949783#post949783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the point. Historical alchemical texts and &quot;alchemical culture&quot; mostly presented immortality and transhumanism in an overwhelmingly positive way. Presenting those as negatives isn't true to the spirit of alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called deconstruction, it's a narrative technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:16:58-07:00","id":949843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949838#post949838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are at least three kinds of beings in the ChroD that can legitimately be called \u201cangels\u201d, at least four that can be called \u201cdemons\u201d, and at least two that can be called \u201cfae\u201d. In a similar sense, I don't get why the assumption seems to be that <b>Promethean</b>'s alchemists <i>must</i> span the full range of alchemist concepts. Why can't there be multiple kinds of alchemists in the ChroD, each with its own role and themes? Put another way, Pyros and its assorted phenomena are not the be-all/end-all of alchemy; they're merely the forms best suited to <b>Promethean</b>'s themes.<br /> <br /> That said, Matt <i>has</i> acknowledged that playable (and, by implication, relatable) alchemists are something that's at least <i>compatible with</i> PtC2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only <i>can</i> there be multiple kinds of alchemists, there <i>are</i> multiple kinds of alchemists. From Mage and Mummy to the Purified, the Ascending Ones, the Thaumaturges of Second Sight, and scores more throughout the books, anyone who wants to be an alchemist has <i>options</i>.<br /> <br /> That is why this has always been a stupid hill to die on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:21:59-07:00","id":949848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949832#post949832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just don't think that in the setting, being a &amp;quot;spiritually natural human&amp;quot; is necessarily that great. Plus, again, I wish the Pilgrimage wasn't so omnipresent. None of the other splats can become human, too, so I'm not sure why Prometheans can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every gameline gets to have its own break with the overall ChroD \u201cgame model\u201d. Humanity as a verifiable goal is Promethean's. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949832#post949832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming human isn't a plot element in Frankenstein, so I'm not quite sure where the devs got it, why they made it so central, and why they doubled down on it for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>spirits aren't a plot element in the Wolf Man, nor is techgnosticism a plot element in stories featuring demons. ChroD isn't about faithfully reproducing the legends and stories that inspired a given gameline; it's about using them as inspiration and putting a unique twist on the result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:25:50-07:00","id":949851,"title":"","content":"Well, putting aside whether or not it's a good element to begin with, I was wondering why the Frankenstein-inspired line was the one they decided to add it to, since, as I mentioned, it's not a feature of any of the others. Maybe they were worried that otherwise the game would lack direction? <br /> <br /> And the reason why I spend so much time on Promethean alchemists is because, as I've mentioned, Frankenstein, the Creature, and the archetype of the mad scientist resonate with me in ways deeper than any other monster that ChroD has covered, so I want them to be present in a way I can enjoy.<br /> <br /> And no, Promethean does not in any way &quot;deconstruct&quot; the concept of alchemy. That's not what deconstruction means. To give an example, deconstructing the conventions of alchemy would mean something like pointing out that figuring out how to turn lead into gold would make gold worthless. Just saying &quot;alchemy and immorality are bad actually&quot; isn't deconstruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-13-2016, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:31:29-07:00","id":949856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949832#post949832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just don't think that in the setting, being a &amp;quot;spiritually natural human&amp;quot; is necessarily that great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>'s signature when you need it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949832#post949832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, again, I wish the Pilgrimage wasn't so omnipresent. None of the other splats can become human, too, so I'm not sure why Prometheans can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's the premise of the game. It's not the premise of Vampire, or Werewolf, or Mage, or any other game line. Though it could have easily been - the search for a cure to one's curse is a big theme in media featuring monsters as protagonists, particularly werewolf stuff. But, Promethean is the game they decided to use to tackle that theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949832#post949832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming human isn't a plot element in Frankenstein, so I'm not quite sure where the devs got it, why they made it so central, and why they doubled down on it for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean isn't the Frankenstein game, any more than Vampire is the Dracula game, or werewolf is the Lon Cheney game. CofD has always presented unique takes on its monsters, perhaps drawing inspiration from classic source material, but always with a twist, and often featuring deconstruction of themes found in the source material.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry that Promethean isn't the Created Being game you want to play. But railing against the game's central premises isn't going to get you very far. 2e was never not going to be centered around the Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:39:50-07:00","id":949860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949851#post949851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, putting aside whether or not it's a good element to begin with, I was wondering why the Frankenstein-inspired line was the one they decided to add it to, since, as I mentioned, it's not a feature of any of the others. Maybe they were worried that otherwise the game would lack direction? <br /> <br /> And the reason why I spend so much time on Promethean alchemists is because, as I've mentioned, Frankenstein, the Creature, and the archetype of the mad scientist resonate with me in ways deeper than any other monster that ChroD has covered, so I want them to be present in a way I can enjoy.<br /> <br /> And no, Promethean does not in any way &amp;quot;deconstruct&amp;quot; the concept of alchemy. That's not what deconstruction means. To give an example, deconstructing the conventions of alchemy would mean something like pointing out that figuring out how to turn lead into gold would make gold worthless. Just saying &amp;quot;alchemy and immorality are bad actually&amp;quot; isn't deconstruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the game about werewolves one where you play those keeping the balance between reality and animist spirits? Why is the game about faeries a metaphor for rebuilding your life after surviving abuse? Why is the game about fallen angels couched in gnostic terms and portrayed with a cyberpunk coat of paint?<br /> <br /> Because that's the premise the authors went with. <br /> <br /> I listen to an excellent podcast called Roleplaying Public Radio, run by a handful of RPG nerds and writers. One of them has chronicled his misadventures in game design and recounted how, when playtesting a game about students and school staff who are driven to supervillainy by demons, had feedback like &quot;I don't like the school setting&quot; or &quot;why do we have to have superpowers?&quot; There's a point where not liking the core idea of game passes into an endless crusade of explaining just how much you hate what it is on a base level and it doesn't lead to a productive conversation after the first dozen times. <br /> <br /> Gecko, you'll catch a lot less flack if you focus on clever setting hacks and writing your own fangames rather than talking about how much you hate the central concept or Promethean or how unfair you think Mage's anti-immortality stance is; hell, I agree with you on the immortality thing! But channel that difference of opinion into creative endeavors into endless circular discussions about not liking things, because it's rapidly approaching the point where people think you're deliberately baiting for replies and fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:41:41-07:00","id":949862,"title":"","content":"Actually, vampires and sin-eaters and changelings and anything aided by the holy hunters of God can become human. So, you know. Wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, one does not have sorrow and furor over being unable to connect with humanity without some desire to be apart of it, which is basically one step away from being becoming human. it also doesn't take a genius to see how Frankenstein, in connection to other similar stories that, you know, just might be handily list as sources and inspirations in either edition can yield a story of created beings becoming human, and how that lens deepens and strengthens Frankenstein.<br /> <br /> Much like one doesn't have to be a genius to easily see a problem with trying to say &quot;Doctor Frankenstein is a symbol for how humanity sucks&quot; and then say &quot;Gosh, I'm mad I can't be Doctor Frankenstein.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:50:30-07:00","id":949866,"title":"","content":"Even if it possible for them, it doesn't totally dominate their games. And even though Promethean isn't &quot;the Frankenstein game&quot;, it's far more influenced by that one work than any other line is influenced by a single work. <br /> <br /> And I have to say, as someone who identified with the Creature for the reasons I articulated, you saying, essentially, that the story would be better if the Creature had become human, just reminds me of why I keep ending up in these arguments with Promethean apologists. <br /> <br /> I understand that trying to convince Onyx Path that they goofed and should change something isn't productive (coughBeastcough), but sometimes you just need to vent. And if I can make just one person so much as question Promethean or Mage, I'll be happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:01:27-07:00","id":949870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949866#post949866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it possible for them, it doesn't totally dominate their games. And even though Promethean isn't &amp;quot;the Frankenstein game&amp;quot;, it's far more influenced by that one work than any other line is influenced by a single work. <br /> <br /> And I have to say, as someone who identified with the Creature for the reasons I articulated, you saying, essentially, that the story would be better if the Creature had become human, just reminds me of why I keep ending up in these arguments with Promethean apologists. <br /> <br /> I understand that trying to convince Onyx Path that they goofed and should change something isn't productive (coughBeastcough), but sometimes you just need to vent. And if I can make just one person so much as question Promethean or Mage, I'll be happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I disagree with the central concept of this game&quot; is not the same Onyx Path making a mistake. Forsaken doesn't really scratch the itch for what I'm looking for in a Werewolf game, and I've gone on the record saying that I generally prefer Unknown Armies to Awakening, but that doesn't mean I endlessly wade into spaces full of fans of those two games and loudly talk about how they're bad because I wish they were done differently. Trying to make fans &quot;question&quot; the games they like is kind of inane unless those games are outwardly harmful, rather than just taking philosophical stances you disagree with or taking an interpretation of the source you dislike.<br /> <br /> If you hate Promethean, then by all means throw yourself into setting hacks or fangames. Just please stop trying to convince people that they're wrong for liking it just because you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:01:57-07:00","id":949871,"title":"","content":"And speaking as someone who also identified with The Creature growing up, I am reminded why I'm very, <i>very </i>tired of Promethean theme hackers.<br /> <br /> Frankenstein is not your book. Promethean is not your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:04:15-07:00","id":949872,"title":"","content":"Putting aside the issue of how you can sympathize with the Creature and not see a problem with Promethean, &quot;theme hacker&quot; actually sounds pretty awesome. <br /> <br /> And I wouldn't have ended up in this argument if the Promethean Defenders' League hadn't shown up in a thread that they knew would make them angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:06:11-07:00","id":949875,"title":"","content":"Pen wanted a response. We gave them.<br /> <br /> Pen and I actually get along fairly well, even if we disagree about games and the nature of hacking. There's a problem here, but it's not that people are having a conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:09:05-07:00","id":949879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949872#post949872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting aside the issue of how you can sympathize with the Creature and not see a problem with Promethean, &amp;quot;theme hacker&amp;quot; actually sounds pretty awesome. <br /> <br /> And I wouldn't have ended up in this argument if the Promethean Defenders' League hadn't shown up in a thread that they knew would make them angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go back to the early pages and see the difference between OP and those who disagree with them and our current conversation. Look at the part where the OP and myself both thank each other for a civil discussion and agree to disagree after making our points.<br /> <br /> Compare that to you saying the writers &quot;goofed&quot; for writing a game you don't like, making up a funny name for people you disagree with, and hijacking someone else's thread to (yet again!!!!) rant about how you hate Promethean. <br /> <br /> You've made your point a few dozen times. Every time you get a volative responce because you're incendiary about it whenever you post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:11:21-07:00","id":949881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949879#post949879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've made your point a few dozen times. Every time you get a volative responce because you're incendiary about it whenever you post.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be that problem I was alluding to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:20:45-07:00","id":949886,"title":"","content":"Man I wish people wouldn't just decry people that disagree with them as &quot;(thing) Apologists&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:23:36-07:00","id":949888,"title":"","content":"Easy labels make for easy garbage tosses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:25:23-07:00","id":949889,"title":"","content":"Apologist apologists and use-apologist-as-an-insult apologists are destined to clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:30:40-07:00","id":949890,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>, knock it off with the name-calling. I don't care if it's &quot;Promethean apologist&quot; or &quot;deathist&quot; or &quot;doodoo head&quot;, that shit doesn't fly in kindergarten and it doesn't fly here just because you use more sophisticated language to denigrate people you don't agree with. Find a way to express your disagreement that doesn't disrespect those you disagree with, or keep your disagreements to yourself, but if you don't stop disrespecting other people, you're going to get a suspension.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:28:56-07:00","id":950198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=946429#post946429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And in a horror setting, &quot;humans are special&quot; just doesn't work for me. Especially since every other Chronicles of Darkness book emphasizes how awful humans can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I admit I haven't read Promethean 2e yet, but unless it's changed from 1e at an incredibly fundamental level -- such that it's not really even the same game -- Promethean <b>does</b> emphasize how awful humans can be. There are entire schools of Promethean thought dedicated to understanding humanity's flaws and weaknesses and hatreds since being human isn't shiny and magical perfection. Centimani frequently come out of dealing with the hatred and weakness and awfulness of humanity and saying &quot;Y'know what? Forget that. If it's either be that or be a monster, I'm gonna be a monster.&quot; The message absolutely isn't &quot;humans are special&quot;, but &quot;being human is better than being a Promethean.&quot; And, unless you remove or alter the downsides, it's extremely hard to argue against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:06:45-07:00","id":950213,"title":"","content":"If you have to choose between being shot in the leg, and being shot in the face, you'd probably avoid the face. Being Promethean is the &quot;getting shot in the face&quot; option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:12:57-07:00","id":950217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949832#post949832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming human isn't a plot element in Frankenstein, so I'm not quite sure where the devs got it, why they made it so central, and why they doubled down on it for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you not read <i>Frankenstein</i>? <br /> <br /> Becoming human in the way that we present in PtC isn't a theme, sure. Humanity and what that means absolutely is. Besides which (as I'm sure other folks have pointed out), <i>Frankenstein</i> isn't the only inspiration for PtC. <br /> <br /> Gecko, it really seems like you don't like this game. I didn't &quot;goof&quot; because you don't like it. You are not the yardstick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:38:19-07:00","id":950227,"title":"","content":"Although i've not had the chance to read prometheans 2e yet (i'm keeping my funds to kickstart scion ). From what i remember of 1e i've always felt that pinocchio was a bigger inspiration. (not saying that frankenstein isnt, just saying i got a bigger pinocchio feel than a frankenstein feel. But then i understand that its entirely subjective)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:29:01-07:00","id":950299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950227#post950227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although i've not had the chance to read prometheans 2e yet (i'm keeping my funds to kickstart scion ). From what i remember of 1e i've always felt that pinocchio was a bigger inspiration. (not saying that frankenstein isnt, just saying i got a bigger pinocchio feel than a frankenstein feel. But then i understand that its entirely subjective)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pinocchio, a classic supernatural horror story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:32:28-07:00","id":950301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950217#post950217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you not read <i>Frankenstein</i>? <br /> <br /> Becoming human in the way that we present in PtC isn't a theme, sure. Humanity and what that means absolutely is. Besides which (as I'm sure other folks have pointed out), <i>Frankenstein</i> isn't the only inspiration for PtC. <br /> <br /> Gecko, it really seems like you don't like this game. I didn't &amp;quot;goof&amp;quot; because you don't like it. You are not the yardstick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I'm going to have to disagree completely. <br /> <br /> I don't hate Promethean. <br /> <br /> I love Promethean. <br /> <br /> I love the Lineages, I love the Refinements, I love the Centimani, I love Pandorans, I love the aesthetics, I love Transmutations, and I've established how much I love Frankenstein and robots. I love stories about being a monster. I love exploring what it means to be human. I love playing the role of an artificial being in a hostile world. I love all those things with a passion, and to me, those are the &quot;buy-in&quot; of Promethean. I do this because I love Promethean. Or rather, I love what it could be. But there's plenty there already that I love. <br /> <br /> So no, let's not say I hate Promethean. It just isn't true. You can say I hate Awakening, I guess (I don't actually hate it, I just don't think it fits in ChroD. I would probably love it as its own thing). But do not say I hate Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:00:46-07:00","id":950340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950301#post950301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Promethean. <br /> <br /> I love the Lineages, I love the Refinements, I love the Centimani, I love Pandorans, I love the aesthetics, I love Transmutations, and I've established how much I love Frankenstein and robots. I love stories about being a monster. I love exploring what it means to be human. I love playing the role of an artificial being in a hostile world. I love all those things with a passion, and to me, those are the &quot;buy-in&quot; of Promethean. I do this because I love Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/hellsing/images/d/d4/The_major_in_the_sparks.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20160610131405\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Very well. Then we shall have Promethean!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-13-2016, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:02:54-07:00","id":950341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950340#post950340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/hellsing/images/d/d4/The_major_in_the_sparks.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-w