er_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:06:34-07:00","id":950986,"title":"","content":"Boy, these last few pages sure were an interesting ride...<br /> I don't really understand the hate for alchemists. That whole section kind of feels like Matt didn't want to rehash the backlash for the first draft version of Heroes, so he decided to preempt it by putting in several #NotAllAlchemist bits himself. Almost every subsection has a bit about how not all alchemists are driven to madness and hatred, and that they can even do good. And yet apparently people keep telling me that the whole section is filled with how all alchemists are evil and you can never have a sympathetic one.<br /> <br /> Then again, people also think that Centimani are great and shouldn't be considered bad guys, mostly because they forget that to be <i>trans</i>human, you first have to be <i>human</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T07:28:37-07:00","id":951099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950986#post950986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy, these last few pages sure were an interesting ride...<br /> I don't really understand the hate for alchemists. That whole section kind of feels like Matt didn't want to rehash the backlash for the first draft version of Heroes, so he decided to preempt it by putting in several #NotAllAlchemist bits himself. Almost every subsection has a bit about how not all alchemists are driven to madness and hatred, and that they can even do good. And yet apparently people keep telling me that the whole section is filled with how all alchemists are evil and you can never have a sympathetic one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that the text is inconclusive - parts are #NotAllAlchemists and parts are &quot;Only bad/insane Alchemists use Pyros/Vitriol&quot;. There seems to be two messages being sent, which disagree on whether you can actually be a sympathetic Alchemist who actually does anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:27:03-07:00","id":951123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950982#post950982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. Not that shaky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Promethean and Alchemist shaky, no, but they're not exactly thick as thieves, at least not in the previewed draft. Outsiders are uncomfortable with how flippantly Changelings enter into Oaths and promises and avoid Freeholds. Those Who Do Not Know are wary of Changelings and see them as just one more type of creature from the hedge. Key Smiths are willing to take Changelings and/or their loved ones hostage if they think they can use that leverage to open a door to the hedge. The Loyal... Well... Are Fae-Touched Loyalists. That's 4 of the 7 sections of example Fae Touched groups that have less-than-positive relationships with Changeling society. It's said early in the draft, &quot;The relationships between the fae-touched and changelings are as complex and varied as the people composing them.&quot; which to me means they can be positive or negative, but they're usually complicated. In other words, shaky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:31:44-07:00","id":951126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950986#post950986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy, these last few pages sure were an interesting ride...<br /> I don't really understand the hate for alchemists. That whole section kind of feels like Matt didn't want to rehash the backlash for the first draft version of Heroes, so he decided to preempt it by putting in several #NotAllAlchemist bits himself. Almost every subsection has a bit about how not all alchemists are driven to madness and hatred, and that they can even do good. And yet apparently people keep telling me that the whole section is filled with how all alchemists are evil and you can never have a sympathetic one.<br /> <br /> Then again, people also think that Centimani are great and shouldn't be considered bad guys, mostly because they forget that to be <i>trans</i>human, you first have to be <i>human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have helped if the #NotAllAlchemists parts weren't also all tagged with #JustInsatiateAlchemists #IfYouTalkToPrometheansYou'reInsatiate #VitriolNotEvenOnce","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:50:27-07:00","id":951256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951126#post951126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would have helped if the #NotAllAlchemists parts weren't also all tagged with #JustInsatiateAlchemists #IfYouTalkToPrometheansYou'reInsatiate #VitriolNotEvenOnce</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that torture is inhumane and monstrous, and that the extraction of both Pyros and specially Vitriol is basically this, yes. You have to be insane to pursue torturing such an engine of destruction as a promethean with any assumption that you can handle what karmic comeuppance will come your way.<br /> <br /> The other way to gather Pyros? Braving firestorms? That's even more insane than being a storm-chaser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:10:37-07:00","id":951337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951256#post951256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that torture is inhumane and monstrous, and that the extraction of both Pyros and specially Vitriol is basically this, yes. You have to be insane to pursue torturing such an engine of destruction as a promethean with any assumption that you can handle what karmic comeuppance will come your way.<br /> <br /> The other way to gather Pyros? Braving firestorms? That's even more insane than being a storm-chaser.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't want to get into the issue I take with using the word &quot;insane&quot; as a synonym for &quot;inhumane and monstrous&quot;, as other members have expressed discomfort with that line of discussion, and I don't want to go back down that road if it's going to upset people. Needless to say, I don't think it's a helpful thing to do.<br /> <br /> Also note that I said Insatiate, not insane - I was using the books own terminology. Also note that the point I was making with the tag #IfYouTalkToPrometheansYou'reInsatiate was that I take issue with the dichotomy the book draws when trying to say not all Alchemists are Insatiate, by implying that non-Insatiate alchemists are all rational, sane people. That kind of binary is really unappealing to me. There should be a spectrum of Alchemists, ranging from sane, rational people to Vitriol-crazed monsters, instead of those two extremes being the only options the book acknowledges the existance of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:47:11-07:00","id":951351,"title":"","content":"I still feel it's a bit of an unfair reading of the text. It feels far more like, &quot;I want Alchemists that aren't want the books did,&quot; is being allowed to bias the reading more than what the text actually says; esp. with the caveat the book makes in the beginning to not treat any absolute statements are anything more than, &quot;usually.&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, I think where the text is trying to make things binary, is different from the kind of spectrum people actually want to see.<br /> <br /> When I read it (and I've reread it a few times because of this thread), I get the impression that Alchemists are more like drug-users, and the Insatiate are addicts (I'm aware I'm vastly oversimplifying the factors that go into addiction in this). You're either addicted to something or you aren't. There's plenty of room for a spectrum of how that addiction impacts you life, but being one or not is binary. Alchemists that avoid the addiction of the Insatiate do so by having to avoid using Pyros too much, and pretty much avoid Vitriol completely. A non-Insatiate Alchemist hanging out with Prometheans is like a sober alcoholic going to bars all the time. It's a rare few might find power in the challenge and successful resistance, but most are just going to find it painful to be constantly tempted and seek to avoid such situations instead.<br /> <br /> You can't really make that a spectrum, and that's where the division between the two seems to be intended to lie. Where you can put in a spectrum is really on all the different ways the Insatiate mentally cope with the fact that they're addicts to Vitriol. Do they try to justify it as serving some cause? Do they just not care? Etc. And I think the book does provide plenty of examples on that spectrum to illustrate that it should be highly varied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:05:18-07:00","id":951478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949870#post949870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>hate</b></i></u></span> Promethean, then by all means throw yourself into setting hacks or fangames. Just please stop trying to convince people that they're wrong for liking it just because you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949879#post949879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare that to you saying the writers &quot;goofed&quot; for writing a game you don't like, making up a funny name for people you disagree with, and hijacking someone else's thread to (yet again!!!!) rant about how you <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><i><b>hate</b></i></u></span> Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950301#post950301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I'm going to have to disagree completely.<br /> <br /> I don't hate Promethean.<br /> <br /> I love Promethean.<br /> <br /> I love the Lineages, I love the Refinements, I love the Centimani, I love Pandorans, I love the aesthetics, I love Transmutations, and I've established how much I love Frankenstein and robots. I love stories about being a monster. I love exploring what it means to be human. I love playing the role of an artificial being in a hostile world. I love all those things with a passion, and to me, those are the &quot;buy-in&quot; of Promethean. I do this because I love Promethean. Or rather, I love what it could be. But there's plenty there already that I love.<br /> <br /> So no, let's not say I hate Promethean. It just isn't true. You can say I hate Awakening, I guess (I don't actually hate it, I just don't think it fits in ChroD. I would probably love it as its own thing). But do not say I hate Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it falls on me to take up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\">@Geckopirateship</a>'s flag for a bit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949871#post949871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankenstein is not your book. Promethean is not your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not &quot;yours&quot; either, nor do these forums belong to you. That goes for all of the&quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!&quot; crowd.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=949870#post949870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I disagree with the central concept of this game&quot; is not the same Onyx Path making a mistake. Forsaken doesn't really scratch the itch for what I'm looking for in a Werewolf game, and I've gone on the record saying that I generally prefer Unknown Armies to Awakening, but that doesn't mean I endlessly wade into spaces full of fans of those two games and <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>loudly</b></i></u></span> talk about how they're bad because I wish they were done differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>NO ONE is &quot;louder&quot; on the Promethean Forums than the people who want to shut us &quot;Theme Hackers&quot; down. There's a reason why I once compared them to &quot;Angry Villagers&quot;; It's an irrational, disproportionate response to other players having a difference of opinion about whether or not Onyx Path should have included OPTIONS for players who don't find much appeal in playing a splat build around trying not to play that anymore. While I respect the Devs creative integrity, I can't really agree with their vision, and it's pretty well established I'm not alone. The fact of the matter is, Pinocchio is just about the only story listed as inspiration in which the protagonist can/wants to become a normal human. A Shard, or some other form of alternative, <i>MIGHT</i> go a <u>LONG</u> way toward making the game more popular. Playing a person returned from the dead in an...imperfectly repaired body and fractured memories, instead of a <i>Tabula Rasa. </i>A being brought to life by Divine Fire, walking a path toward Divinity of their own. An Automaton gaining independence from it's creator, but not becoming a &quot;meatbag&quot; it's self. These are all things that COULD be part of Promethean, but first the devs need to be willing to listen to feedback, and the players who LOVE the game as-is need to stop attacking the players who want something different.<br /> <br /> TLDR: For a game about Alchemy, it's most loyal fans are weirdly resistant to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-16-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:20:42-07:00","id":951482,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6138_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6138\" data-vbnamecard=\"6138\">Mangle77</a> Promethean is a game with a tight focus, certainly the tightest focus of any CofD lines; it's more kin to weird little art games like A Place To Fuck Each Other or the delightfully strange Noumenon in that way. The Promethean are created by others in a world that rejects them, and find themselves on a long journey to understand humanity and build an identity for themselves in the name of finally finding some peace. That's the elevator pitch of the game, that's why the people that love it love it, and trying to change that so radically is bizarre to me. I don't complain that a Spider-Man movie isn't about Wolverine, and I certainly don't act like a victim when I tell Spider-Man fans that they're wrong and so are the writers and we'd all be so much happier if we were talking about Wolverine.<br /> <br /> Promethean isn't the game some people want it to be. Why not let that be the end of the discussion, and move on to something else <i>like literally any other game?</i> Why keep beating a dead horse that has plagued this forum for years, and why do it in a thread about Alchemists? If half the time, energy, and vitriol (ha!) spent complaining about Promethean and the people that like it as intended went into making a transhuman fangame, it would be finished and playable by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:34:32-07:00","id":951489,"title":"","content":"I've found in similar situations the problem can be the opening remark.<br /> <br /> When you make a post in the game's board that goes ahead and warns you, 'This is not a positive post,' you're already asking for fans of the game to come and defend it as much as possible. PenDragon seemed to want their input, as well, or have them explain the causes for certain sections.<br /> <br /> It would have been better, after PenDragon got their answer, to simply make a new thread calling people who didn't like aspects of the game to come together and figure out alternatives to fix them, not to for people to have to defend their opinions, which is going to get them all up in arms.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm imagining it but it seems there's a lot of antagonism on the boards lately, perhaps it just spikes when a new game is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:41:20-07:00","id":951490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951478#post951478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not &quot;yours&quot; either, nor do these forums belong to you. That goes for all of the&quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!&quot; crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have chosen a poor flag.<br /> <br /> It's not my place to discuss Gecko's forum etiquette or it's failings, or even it's successes if they are present. If you wish to hear an opinion of that, seek a moderator. However, in terms of these forums not being mine, I agree, and that's why I try very hard to abide by the terms of use. I assume I have succeeded on some front, because I am still here. Now, I have been banned before for being an absolute asshole to people, and I quite frankly deserved it. If, in future, I am a such a raging asshole I get permanently banned, I will deserve that too. But for the moment, I am here.<br /> <br /> Not only am I here, but I am here in spite of what feels to me like a very large presence of spiteful presences. I have found my method of dealing with problems here. I have a system that involves levels of response, levels of ignoring, and final lines for just flat out blocking people. At no point have I determined that just because people feel I'm wrong and get very angry at me about it have I decided that I need to so securely sever my relationship with these forums that I need to be banned. If it becomes too much, I can take a break. If it stops feeling worth it, I can just leave. I do not demand that everyone shut up and listen to what I say, because I know very well that these are not my forums and that I do not have infinite power here. I try to live in some form of acceptable harmony with the people around me. Sometimes, that means speaking passionately about my viewpoints. Othertimes, that means listening and learning.<br /> <br /> At all times, it means hedging my bets on whether I am going to become a better person through the conversation who not only learns something about the game, but about other people and the world, or if the conversation, due to my involvement or others is just going to ruin my day or someone else's. Because these are not my forums, but it is my communication, and my communication is how I break the barriers between people and actually connect.<br /> <br /> As for Promethean not being mine, you are also correct. Promethean belongs to Promethean, and therefore deserves attempts at understanding and respect just as much as any person here. It is it's own thing first and foremost, both as a product and as a compilation of the efforts and experiences of the writers and developers of it, all of whom had a vision to communicate. Promethean's existence, in all honesty, has more value in it than any post here, because the creative process has time and money and sleepless hours and headaches and coffee and wine runs and more put into it-more than any one person. Even if you do not like what it is, it must be accorded a certain amount of respect first, by the sheer miracle of it's existence. Any finished product is worth more for that reasons. Even Genius, which I am currently reading and raving to high fucking hell about, deserves the respect of what it is, the culmination of dreams.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm going to ignore my usual philosophy and continue that train. The biggest problem with the theme hackers of Promethean has often not been the fact that they want to change the game utterly and completely-it has been that they have wanted to do so with no respect for the people who enjoy it or the effort that went into it in the first place. These topics have not merely been a desire for a different vision-they have been a platform for people to express hatred for the game, it's makers, and it's fans, who have <i>zero</i> respect for how this game, as it is, might have affected the lives of those who have read it. As a counter example, WyrdHamster, for all his problems with it, has always been very thoughtful of the fact that other people enjoy Promethean as it is. While he has been insistent upon his own treatment, he has been very willing to openly and honestly accept that people do not agree with him. It's a reason why his thread on the subject is actually moderately successful. But the majority are often nothing but engines of spite and malice. As we have stated before, small wonder it's a topic that raises hackles.<br /> <br /> So, no, Promethean's not mine. But it sure as fuck doesn't belong to anyone who's got an axe to grind, whose primary purpose is to hurt and to exclude, to persecute those who do not share in the message. No game belongs to a person like that.<br /> <br /> Finally, the deepest problem, the one that seems to get missed over and over again, is that the the whole synthesis of the game revolves around a theme you all don't like. It's not enough to merely change surface elements, or even craft elements, but deep structural and idiomatic pieces. To change a game like this into what you all want is to honestly just create another game. This is why general discussion on the subject leans towards finding another game. It's genuinely, deeply, too much. Promethean will fight anyone trying to do this at every turn, and the game you have at the end is not it's own distinct thing. You might as well slice up a person's brain and put them into a robot suit, regardless of whether they wanted to or not. It's crass-vulgar. Useless, really. Better to just find a different game. When we say that, we're thinking of the people asking as much as we are thinking about the game.<br /> <br /> Kindly take your attitude and burn it in a fire. We're not your fucking enemies here, however much you might want us to be.<br /> <br /> I am so very, very tired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-16-2016, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:44:46-07:00","id":951492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951489#post951489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found in similar situations the problem can be the opening remark.<br /> <br /> When you make a post in the game's board that goes ahead and warns you, 'This is not a positive post,' you're already asking for fans of the game to come and defend it as much as possible. PenDragon seemed to want their input, as well, or have them explain the causes for certain sections.<br /> <br /> It would have been better, after PenDragon got their answer, to simply make a new thread calling people who didn't like aspects of the game to come together and figure out alternatives to fix them, not to for people to have to defend their opinions, which is going to get them all up in arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like you're describing RPG.net's + and - threads. It's an interesting strategy for sure. I'm not sure it would be the right one for these forums. But something to consider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951489#post951489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm imagining it but it seems there's a lot of antagonism on the boards lately, perhaps it just spikes when a new game is out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this strikes me as normal post-release tension. Passions are high, and people are naturally going to clash a bit. This <i>particular</i> release is bringing out even higher passions because, as observed, Promethean has an extremely tight focus, which means the people who like it are <i>really</i> going to like it, and the people who don't are <i>really</i> not going to. That's before we get into the humanism vs. transhumanism thing, which is super blown out of proportion in the CofD fanbase, and at this point the New Dawn and the price of immortality in Mage have acquired so much baggage over the years that the arguments are really only tangentially related to the actual games by this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:50:30-07:00","id":951494,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">I'm also going to have to ask that we stop calling people &quot;theme hackers.&quot; The proscription against name-calling cuts both ways.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:52:11-07:00","id":951495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951494#post951494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">I'm also going to have to ask that we stop calling people &quot;theme hackers.&quot; The proscription against name-calling cuts both ways.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Understood. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:52:48-07:00","id":951496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951478#post951478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NO ONE is &quot;louder&quot; on the Promethean Forums than the people who want to shut us &quot;Theme Hackers&quot; down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I direct your attention to the state of the Demon forums circa 2014 and invite you to examine the comparative initial behavior of the people who were mad that that game had an aesthetic that they interpreted as thematically counter to their vision of its monster-type.<br /> <br /> Not only did it become as rapidly tiresome then as this has been for the responding parties here as detractors seemed increasingly incapable of framing their dissatisfaction in terms more concrete than &quot;I don't want this game to be the way that it is&quot; and more civil than &quot;this game not adhering to my vision of X means it is bad at being a game about X,&quot; but one of the most vocal detractors in that vein significantly mellowed their tune when they finally <i>actually actively read the material they were decrying, acknowledged that it was just not specifically about the things they were looking for, and started putting more time into casting about for a more appropriate gameline for what they wanted/building their homebrew.</i><br /> <br /> The old forums had a recurring problem member who vocally decried a grossly-exaggerated strawman of &quot;personal horror&quot; and seemed unable to post a homebrew setting without enumerating all the Published Peripheral/Supplementary Elements That Were Not Canon There and holding forth on all the ways their own inventions (several of them callbacks to the storied age of Katanas and Trenchcoats) kicked the posteriors of between one and three direct stand-ins for their least favorite themes. Nobody cared for this behavior and the poster was told so multiple times in multiple different ways, many of them extremely civil.<br /> <br /> At last check, they still hold roughly the same views. This is, in the grand scheme of things, fine.<br /> <br /> If you're wondering why it's fine, it's because the core problem was always the attitude they approached engaging with the forums on their topic of contention over, <i>and they've largely fixed that</i>.<br /> <br /> If you want help with shifting the existing material toward a thematic end more in line with your desired setup, many of the people on these forums will be happy to help you in that endeavor.<br /> <br /> If you just want to holler about how much you hate the base game, though, you will only find yourself in the same place any series of polarizing statements puts you, which you have handily grasped in the propagandic terms of Persecuted Homebrewers and Torch-Wielding Angry Villagers, in stark refusal of the premise that you have been passing out sticks and oily rags and playing the firebrand.<br /> <br /> You are standing in a hell of your own making and asking why it is so damn hot.<br /> <br /> I trust that you don't need to be told the reason by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":"though nothing was meant by it, the terminology has been edited accordingly. 08-16-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:44:35-07:00","id":951509,"title":"","content":"I find the presentation of Alchemists kind of sad, metatextually. It's like, Matt knew he did heroes wrong and knew that alchemists also had a similar problem, and tried to fix it. But then he fixed the wrong bit. He acknowledged that there are good Alchemists, but again he didn't give any reason for them to interact with the pcs, because alchemists, like heroes, are meant to be unsympathetic. I think Matt just doesn't get how to do antagonists beyond 'these guys want to kill you' and that's just kind of sad to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:44:48-07:00","id":951510,"title":"","content":"Could we also put \u201cthe \u2018You are on Fire!\u2019 crowd\u201d on the growing list of politically incorrect terms here, along with \u201ctheme hackers\u201d, \u201cdeathists\u201d, and \u201cPromethean apologists\u201d? Better yet, <i>could we please stop throwing labels around</i> and using prejudicial stereotypes to engage in <i>ad hominem</i> attacks? Lookat my sig: I'm a big fan of hacking the system to get what you want out of it. I started a thread a while back to discuss the tenson between respecting a gameline's themes and hacking the system to feature your own themes. I try to be respectful of everyone in the debate. And yet, when I use an analogy involving fire in a discussion about <b>Promethean</b>, I immediately get jumped on for promoting \u201cthe \u2018You Are On Fire!\u2019 analogy\u201d. I get lumped together with several other posters here and summarily dismissed as an aspect of a group-think clique that's trying to shut down debate. <br /> <br /> Arc has the right of it: the problem here isn't \u201ctheme hacking\u201d per se (sorry, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>, but I disagree about it being a pejorative term; just like Gecko, I would be <i>proud</i> to be called a theme hacker); the problem is the disrespectful attitude that <i>some</i> of the theme hackers have displayed \u2014 namely, the attitude that the game is broken and/or that the developers screwed up because its themes don't align with one's own preferences. <br /> <br /> I \u201ctheme hacked\u201d Werewolf a while back, before 2e came out. I developed a series of posts that carefully and meticulously excised spirits from their central role in the game, with the intent of making it possible to play WtF without ever once encountering a spirit or visiting the Hisil. And I didn't get \u201ctorch-wielding mobs\u201d of \u201cWerewolf purists\u201d trying to shut down my threads and/or drive me out of the forums \u2014 or even bogging down my threads with a lot of \u201cbut that's not WtF!\u201d rants. Was it because WtF's fanbase is so much more mature than PtC's fanbase? Hardly. It's because I was respectful of their views. I did not claim that WtF was broken because spirits are so integral to it, and I didn't try to proselytize. I clearly identified my threads for what they were so that no one would go in under false pretenses. And I made an effort to be additive in my hacks whenever possible, building on the existing material instead of ripping it out and replacing it with something different. <br /> <br /> That's not what's been going on here, for the most part.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: \u201cX is dumb, and I'm here to show you the <i>right</i> way to do it\u201d is very different from \u201cX is not my cup of tea, and I'm going to tweak it to be more to my liking\u201d. Both are theme hacking; the former is bad theme hacking; the latter is good theme hacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-16-2016, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T23:33:36-07:00","id":951520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951510#post951510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we also put \u201cthe \u2018You are on Fire!\u2019 crowd\u201d on the growing list of politically incorrect terms here, along with \u201ctheme hackers\u201d, \u201cdeathists\u201d, and \u201cPromethean apologists\u201d? Better yet, <i>could we please stop throwing labels around</i> and using prejudicial stereotypes to engage in <i>ad hominem</i> attacks? Lookat my sig: I'm a big fan of hacking the system to get what you want out of it. I started a thread a while back to discuss the tenson between respecting a gameline's themes and hacking the system to feature your own themes. I try to be respectful of everyone in the debate. And yet, when I use an analogy involving fire in a discussion about <b>Promethean</b>, I immediately get jumped on for promoting \u201cthe \u2018You Are On Fire!\u2019 analogy\u201d. I get lumped together with several other posters here and summarily dismissed as an aspect of a group-think clique that's trying to shut down debate.<br /> <br /> Arc has the right of it: the problem here isn't \u201ctheme hacking\u201d per se (sorry, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>, but I disagree about it being a pejorative term; just like Gecko, I would be <i>proud</i> to be called a theme hacker); the problem is the disrespectful attitude that <i>some</i> of the theme hackers have displayed \u2014 namely, the attitude that the game is broken and/or that the developers screwed up because its themes don't align with one's own preferences.<br /> <br /> I \u201ctheme hacked\u201d Werewolf a while back, before 2e came out. I developed a series of posts that carefully and meticulously excised spirits from their central role in the game, with the intent of making it possible to play WtF without ever once encountering a spirit or visiting the Hisil. And I didn't get \u201ctorch-wielding mobs\u201d of \u201cWerewolf purists\u201d trying to shut down my threads and/or drive me out of the forums \u2014 or even bogging down my threads with a lot of \u201cbut that's not WtF!\u201d rants. Was it because WtF's fanbase is so much more mature than PtC's fanbase? Hardly. It's because I was respectful of their views. I did not claim that WtF was broken because spirits are so integral to it, and I didn't try to proselytize. I clearly identified my threads for what they were so that no one would go in under false pretenses. And I made an effort to be additive in my hacks whenever possible, building on the existing material instead of ripping it out and replacing it with something different.<br /> <br /> That's not what's been going on here, for the most part.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: \u201cX is dumb, and I'm here to show you the <i>right</i> way to do it\u201d is very different from \u201cX is not my cup of tea, and I'm going to tweak it to be more to my liking\u201d. Both are theme hacking; the former is bad theme hacking; the latter is good theme hacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise excellent points here. I'll go ahead and ease up on the label policing, as long as we can all agree to use them productively, and not to reduce or marginalize those we disagree with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, on second thought, I might be too close to this discussion to be moderating it. I'm going to take a step back from that in general. If something particularly egregious like a direct personal or group attack comes up, I'll step in to address it, but otherwise I'm going to take off of my mod hat for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-16-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:18:48-07:00","id":951526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951509#post951509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He acknowledged that there are good Alchemists, but again he didn't give any reason for them to interact with the pcs, because alchemists, like heroes, are meant to be unsympathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>No... the text is actually fairly explicit that it's because the Alchemists getting the focus are supposed to be <i>antagonists</i>. Even with the various details on specific Insatiate Alchemists in the write up there are characters you can sympathize with (even some of the more monstrous ones).<br /> <br /> &quot;Good&quot; Alchemists aren't given a reason to interact with the PCs (and are actually given reasons to largely avoid the PCs) because that doesn't serve any narrative niche for the stories Promethean is aimed at creating. Having these Alchemists successfully seek out Prometheans to for working relations with them runs counter to a lot of the thematic elements of the game, so that's not something the base-line game encourages. Having them as antagonists doesn't really work if they're not actually antagonizing the PCs.<br /> <br /> The Insatiate Alchemists have a niche to fill as antagonists. So that's the focus the text takes.<br /> <br /> Why, exactly, is that a problem? After all this I still don't see why that choice, beyond personal preference, is <i>bad</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Matt just doesn't get how to do antagonists beyond 'these guys want to kill you' and that's just kind of sad to me. </div> </div> </div>His rather large body of work (including a number of writing credits on CofD books dedicated to antagonists) would suggest this isn't the case. So it seems more appropriate to give him a bit more charity in the reading about how the editorial choice to make the antagonists in PtC 2e the way they are was for a design reason rather than some deficiency in his skills.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, for example, the focus is on things that want to kill Prometheans (and it isn't just the Alchemists, who don't really want to kill Prometheans as much as killing them is a side effect of what they really want) is because part of the core themes of the game are how the Created are outsiders that are supernaturally rejected by the world around them. That isolation and alienation is a large part of their drive to seek out the Great Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:21:52-07:00","id":951528,"title":"","content":"As a note on the entire &quot;Matt can't write antagonists beyond 'these guys want to kill you' front&quot;, you are talking about the man who is responsible for every bit of information we have on fetches in Changeling the Lost.<br /> <br /> You might want to reconsider your position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:33:11-07:00","id":951532,"title":"","content":"New proposal: Either talk about the game and leave the developer and writers out of the conversation, or actually research and know a thing or two about the people you're talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:48:48-07:00","id":951539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951496#post951496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just want to holler about how much you hate the base game, though, you will only find yourself in the same place any series of polarizing statements puts you, which you have handily grasped in the propagandic terms of Persecuted Homebrewers and Torch-Wielding Angry Villagers, in stark refusal of the premise that you have been passing out sticks and oily rags and playing the firebrand..</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's how many times I've witnessed any thread that even suggests trying to build a &quot;better&quot; (I.E. broader appeal) version of Promethean get bogged down with the exact same 5 or 6 posters ranting about how the game is perfect the way it is, and how trying to hack is some form of blasphemy. That response makes no sense. It literally makes me think about how Disquiet works, causing otherwise rational people to become aggressive, belligerent, and ready to drive any &quot;Outsider&quot; away with extreme prejudice.(&quot;Torches &amp; Pitchforks&quot;) I LIKE the game as is, but there's no point in having a game I can't play, and NONE of my friends is interested in the game as is. I can't really play it by myself. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950301#post950301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the Lineages, I love the Refinements, I love the Centimani, I love Pandorans, I love the aesthetics, I love Transmutations, and I've established how much I love Frankenstein and robots. I love stories about being a monster. I love exploring what it means to be human. I love playing the role of an artificial being in a hostile world. I love all those things with a passion, and to me, those are the &quot;buy-in&quot; of Promethean. I do this because I love Promethean. Or rather, I love what it could be. But there's plenty there already that I love.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the parts of the game that work for me. Think like Victor Frankenstein for a moment: When building your monster, you take the pieces of a cadaver you can make use of, and discard the parts you can't. For us &quot;Theme Hackers&quot;, there are aspects of P:tC that simply DO NOT WORK. But I'm done arguing about that in this thread. It's been suggested that if the same amount of time and energy was spent working on a new game as we spend arguing about why we want one, we'd already have one, so I made a thread for that, outside the P:tC Forums:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951524-building-a-new-monster\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-a-new-monster</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-16-2016, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:51:03-07:00","id":951540,"title":"","content":"In all fairness, those of us outside the process do not have access to solid sources of information on how many of the books were broken down between the different writers; or how much the lead developers adjusting those sections. I have no idea what Matt wrote for the various antagonist books he's credited for, and I have no idea where I would even go to look to find out since that's not really included in the public material. In only a few open dev documents where early outlines were shared that included writer assignments do we ever get a solid glimpse into that.<br /> <br /> I can easily point to Matt having worked on Autumn Nightmares, three of the Night Horrors books, Banishers, Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss, Reign of the Exarchs, WOD: Inferno, WOD: Slashers, the Horror Recognition Guide, The Pure, and see he's work on a ton of purely antagonist focused books (so no question he was writing about something else in a more general book) that are generally well regarded to show he can write really good antagonist material. But I honestly can't point to specific examples in any of those books because I have no idea what he did specifically in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T01:00:08-07:00","id":951545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951539#post951539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, it's how many times I've witnessed any thread that even suggests trying to build a &quot;better&quot; (I.E. broader appeal) version of Promethean get bogged down with the exact same 5 or 6 posters ranting about how the game is perfect the way it is, and how trying to hack is some form of blasphemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i>again</i>, I exhort you to examine the way those &quot;suggestions&quot; are almost invariably phrased. This is by no means a problem whose roots are difficult to see.<br /> <br /> Best of luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T02:59:47-07:00","id":951572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951539#post951539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, it's how many times I've witnessed any thread that even suggests trying to build a &quot;better&quot; (I.E. broader appeal) version of Promethean get bogged down with the exact same 5 or 6 posters ranting about how the game is perfect the way it is, and how trying to hack is some form of blasphemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly didn't even bothered reading Arcane's post, did you? You aren't doing anything better. Different, perhaps. Better? Hardly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951539#post951539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That response makes no sense. It literally makes me think about how Disquiet works, causing otherwise rational people to become aggressive, belligerent, and ready to drive any &quot;Outsider&quot; away with extreme prejudice.(&quot;Torches &amp; Pitchforks&quot;) I LIKE the game as is, but there's no point in having a game I can't play, and NONE of my friends is interested in the game as is. I can't really play it by myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep tossing labels, please. No, really. I'm just counting how many it takes for moderation to act.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951539#post951539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the parts of the game that work for me. Think like Victor Frankenstein for a moment: When building your monster, you take the pieces of a cadaver you can make use of, and discard the parts you can't. For us &quot;Theme Hackers&quot;, there are aspects of P:tC that simply DO NOT WORK. But I'm done arguing about that in this thread. It's been suggested that if the same amount of time and energy was spent working on a new game as we spend arguing about why we want one, we'd already have one, so I made a thread for that, outside the P:tC Forums:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951524-building-a-new-monster\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-a-new-monster</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And whatever your sentiments towards the game may be, those shouldn't be expressed in a forum specifically meant to address it's antagonist. Not once have you said anything about Alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:12:07-07:00","id":951592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951509#post951509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the presentation of Alchemists kind of sad, metatextually. It's like, Matt knew he did heroes wrong and knew that alchemists also had a similar problem, and tried to fix it. But then he fixed the wrong bit. He acknowledged that there are good Alchemists, but again he didn't give any reason for them to interact with the pcs, because alchemists, like heroes, are meant to be unsympathetic. I think Matt just doesn't get how to do antagonists beyond 'these guys want to kill you' and that's just kind of sad to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Regardless of whether or not I know how to write antagonists (YMMV), alchemists were written <i>before</i> Heroes, and I didn't get either of them &quot;wrong.&quot; You just don't like them. <br /> <br /> (But, as others point out, shockingly the alchemists in the antagonists section are meant to be antagonists. I can't remember, when <b>VtR</b> first came out, were there big threads complaining about how the book didn't support playing VII?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:19:40-07:00","id":951595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951532#post951532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New proposal: Either talk about the game and leave the developer and writers out of the conversation, or actually research and know a thing or two about the people you're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding on this: leave <i>posters</i> out of the conversation, too; stick to the content of the game. Or, if you're going to talk about others, first consider whether or not <i>you</i> have anything to do with the current climate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:27:06-07:00","id":951600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951592#post951592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of whether or not I know how to write antagonists (YMMV), alchemists were written <i>before</i> Heroes, and I didn't get either of them \u201cwrong.\u201d You just don't like them. <br /> <br /> (But, as others point out, shockingly the alchemists in the antagonists section are meant to be antagonists. I can't remember, when <b>VtR</b> first came out, were there big threads complaining about how the book didn't support playing VII?)</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, my main gripe with the alchemists section as written is that it doesn't really address the \u201cgood intentions, bad results\u201d possibility, where the requisite desperation that's necessarily at the heart of all Pyros-based alchemists gradually overwhelms his ethics and ends up with him cutting up a Promethean to further his goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:51:41-07:00","id":951604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951592#post951592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(But, as others point out, shockingly the alchemists in the antagonists section are meant to be antagonists. I can't remember, when <b>VtR</b> first came out, were there big threads complaining about how the book didn't support playing VII?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, it was the Brood that got the attention when VtR came out, and did eventually get their own splat book for playing. When Werewolf hit, people wanted to jump onto Pure as PCs. To this day, we have &quot;lets make the Seers something other than two-dimensional black hat villains&quot; threads. No one's really jumped on the Loyalist bandwagon, persay, but there's been plenty of &quot;my character didn't have an abusive Keeper and is fond of them&quot; ones. Slashers and Decieved are antagonist-material that have PC-able rules. Demon and Geist seems to be the only games to escape the &quot;play antagonist faction&quot; type situation, and that's because the former's antagonists are ephemeral creatures, while the latter's antagonist factions were PC material from the start (*cough*Reapers*cough*). Even then, there have been lots of complaints about not having God-Machine level abilities in demons, and wanting to have Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Sorry, Matt, but this is just something doomed to happen with every game. The only way to avoid it is to not make antagonists. Combine with the fact we're dealing with something kinda new, its going to be picked on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-16-2016, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:31:40-07:00","id":951620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951509#post951509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the presentation of Alchemists kind of sad, metatextually. It's like, Matt knew he did heroes wrong and knew that alchemists also had a similar problem, and tried to fix it. But then he fixed the wrong bit. He acknowledged that there are good Alchemists, but again he didn't give any reason for them to interact with the pcs, because alchemists, like heroes, are meant to be unsympathetic.<b> I think Matt just doesn't get how to do antagonists beyond 'these guys want to kill you' and that's just kind of sad to me</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">.\u200bAnd that seems like a personal attack. Don't do it again, this is your official warning. Take the advice offered by other forum users about talking specifically about the subject being discussed rather than taking tangentially related shots at the Developers.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:03:18-07:00","id":951633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951604#post951604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, Matt, but this is just something doomed to happen with every game. The only way to avoid it is to not make antagonists. Combine with the fact we're dealing with something kinda new, its going to be picked on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wasn't being sarcastic - I literally couldn't remember whether people wanted to jump on playing VII, but now that you say that I certainly remember them being fascinated by the Brood. And of course during OWoD there was the &quot;ooh, Sabbat! Ooh, BSDs! Ooh, Technocracy!&quot; <br /> <br /> And like, I'm not even opposed to (some of) that. As I think I've said, I think making an alchemist character might be kind of fun...but don't ask me to hack out word count in an already squeezed book so that folks can play the antagonists for the actual focus characters. Gotta have something in reserve in case I get to do a PG. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:16:57-07:00","id":951638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951592#post951592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Regardless of whether or not I know how to write antagonists (YMMV), alchemists were written <i>before</i> Heroes, and I didn't get either of them &quot;wrong.&quot; You just don't like them.<br /> <br /> (But, as others point out, shockingly the alchemists in the antagonists section are meant to be antagonists. I can't remember, when <b>VtR</b> first came out, were there big threads complaining about how the book didn't support playing VII?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> VII is an interesting case, I think. I don't know if there were threads about making them playable (wasn't here back then), but they are handled in a interesting way. I think someone with better Vampire acumen than me *and* with actual Alchemist write up available to compare it could do some interesting analysis on the case. If I remember correctly, the thing with VII - at least in 2nd ED core - was that there weren't many &quot;facts&quot; stated about them, judgemental or not - they were portrayed more like a *occurence* than anything normal; like a occult mystery. Their section is literally a string of contradictory, mysterious possible origins that give hints and ideas to use in your own games. <br /> Basically, they aren't really even a concrete thing; they are a *conceptual space* to be filled on your own. And thus, I can imagine that there wasn't much complaining about them, because everyone could just delve into ideas-soup of imagination stimulation (because that's what basically VII chapter is) and come out with whatever they are pleased with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:21:38-07:00","id":951643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951592#post951592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(But, as others point out, shockingly the alchemists in the antagonists section are meant to be antagonists. I can't remember, when <b>VtR</b> first came out, were there big threads complaining about how the book didn't support playing VII?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't around when VtR came out, so I can't speak much about that. But regarding Alchemists, I haven't seen anyone complaining that they're not playable. Most people who dislike their presentation dislike it because they don't see their motivations as antagonists being believable enough. Others (such as myself) are merely opposed to the suggestion that the divide is as dichotomous as &quot;playable Alchemists&quot; and &quot;Insatiate Alchemists&quot;. Them being antagonists is fine, but must all antagonist Alchemests be unsympathetic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:25:47-07:00","id":951644,"title":"","content":"&quot;Power&quot; Isnt motivation enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:27:03-07:00","id":951647,"title":"","content":"To add onto what WHW said.... yes, they were pretty vague in the core book, but there were lots of Aasimite remake threads (which many people discussed as the inspiration behind VII).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:31:33-07:00","id":951653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951644#post951644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Power&quot; Isnt motivation enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Power is a super boring motivation to me. Like, it's fine, but it is kinda the lowest hanging fruit of reasons for characters to evil things. &quot;I want power and I don't care who I have to hurt to get it&quot; is pretty one-dimensional, and I like my antagonists more complex than that. Ideally, they should even be relatable from a certain point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-16-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:35:58-07:00","id":951658,"title":"","content":"Power is fine, but it's most interesting when power is a goal to attain other goal. Power...to do what? Power...because of why? Power...due to their lack of what? <br /> Or, in different way - power is an interesting motivation, because it usually comes attached to pursuing *other* motivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:42:35-07:00","id":951666,"title":"","content":"You've tapped into the Divine Fire. For a <i>human</i> to tap into the Divine Fire, there must be desperation. Desperation for power is certainly a possibility; but to me, it's one of many \u2014 and even when it <i>is</i> what the alchemist pursues, there's generally more to it than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:46:28-07:00","id":951668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951666#post951666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've tapped into the Divine Fire. For a <i>human</i> to tap into the Divine Fire, there must be desperation. Desperation for power is certainly a possibility; but to me, it's one of many \u2014 and even when it <i>is</i> what the alchemist pursues, there's generally more to it than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as fear (of death, of monsters, of his high cholesterol), desperation (to save someone, to fix themselves) or simply a very very powerful desire to turn into a ChroD version of Ursula from the little mermaid because you lost both your legs in an incident involving killer squirrels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:03:51-07:00","id":951715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951572#post951572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You clearly didn't even bothered reading Arcane's post, did you? You aren't doing anything better. Different, perhaps. Better? Hardly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I put the word better in quotation marks; I am aware such things are subjective. Also, can we stop saying that using a word or phrase to describe a fairly clear philosophical divide is &quot;Labeling&quot;? That word is a trigger for me.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And whatever your sentiments towards the game may be, those shouldn't be expressed in a forum specifically meant to address it's antagonist. Not once have you said anything about Alchemists. </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou are correct. I have not said anything about the material that I have not read, and might never read, because $20 is more than I'm willing to pay for a non-refundable PDF of the second edition for a game I can NEVER play the first edition of. I can say that I agree that if you want readers to see a group/splat/faction as something other than mustache twirling cartoon villains, you need to show that they can(and will, at least sometimes) do something good. I absolutely can see potential in the Alchemist concept, but as multiple people have already pointed out, if the only Alchemist who actually DO Alchemy are deranged butchers, it really defeats the idea of them as protagonists or allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:31:36-07:00","id":951731,"title":"","content":"No, &quot;not all alchemists who do alchemy are deranged butchers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Non-insensate alchemists certainly use less alchemy, since they don't use vitriol to give themselves powers or merits, or harvest outside sources for refueling, but being able to store up to 9 points and regenerate without actually doing anything 3 points a week is certainly better than some minor templates have gotten, which is the niche alchemist fills beyond antagonist.<br /> <br /> I imagine there would be plenty of ghouls who would gladly murder someone for the ability to replenish automatically 3 points of vitae a week. <br /> <br /> Although for the life of me I cannot imagine why a mage would choose to become an alchemist,what with the automatically gaining conditions, I would imagine most mage alchemists were alchemists first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:57:51-07:00","id":951755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951490#post951490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have chosen a poor flag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that feels insulting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Not only am I here, but I am here in spite of what feels to me like a very large presence of spiteful presences. I have found my method of dealing with problems here. I have a system that involves levels of response, levels of ignoring, and final lines for just flat out blocking people. At no point have I determined that just because people feel I'm wrong and get very angry at me about it have I decided that I need to so securely sever my relationship with these forums that I need to be banned. If it becomes too much, I can take a break. If it stops feeling worth it, I can just leave. I do not demand that everyone shut up and listen to what I say, because I know very well that these are not my forums and that I do not have infinite power here. I try to live in some form of acceptable harmony with the people around me. Sometimes, that means speaking passionately about my viewpoints. Othertimes, that means listening and learning.<br /> <br /> At all times, it means hedging my bets on whether I am going to become a better person through the conversation who not only learns something about the game, but about other people and the world, or if the conversation, due to my involvement or others is just going to ruin my day or someone else's. Because these are not my forums, but it is my communication, and my communication is how I break the barriers between people and actually connect.<br /> <br /> As for Promethean not being mine, you are also correct. Promethean belongs to Promethean, and therefore deserves attempts at understanding and respect just as much as any person here. It is it's own thing first and foremost, both as a product and as a compilation of the efforts and experiences of the writers and developers of it, all of whom had a vision to communicate. Promethean's existence, in all honesty, has more value in it than any post here, because the creative process has time and money and sleepless hours and headaches and coffee and wine runs and more put into it-more than any one person. Even if you do not like what it is, it must be accorded a certain amount of respect first, by the sheer miracle of it's existence. Any finished product is worth more for that reasons. Even Genius, which I am currently reading and raving to high fucking hell about, deserves the respect of what it is, the culmination of dreams.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm going to ignore my usual philosophy and continue that train. The biggest problem with the theme hackers of Promethean has often not been the fact that they want to change the game utterly and completely-it has been that they have wanted to do so with no respect for the people who enjoy it or the effort that went into it in the first place. These topics have not merely been a desire for a different vision-they have been a platform for people to express hatred for the game, it's makers, and it's fans, who have <i>zero</i> respect for how this game, as it is, might have affected the lives of those who have read it. As a counter example, WyrdHamster, for all his problems with it, has always been very thoughtful of the fact that other people enjoy Promethean as it is. While he has been insistent upon his own treatment, he has been very willing to openly and honestly accept that people do not agree with him. It's a reason why his thread on the subject is actually moderately successful. But the majority are often nothing but engines of spite and malice. As we have stated before, small wonder it's a topic that raises hackles.<br /> <br /> So, no, Promethean's not mine. But it sure as fuck doesn't belong to anyone who's got an axe to grind, whose primary purpose is to hurt and to exclude, to persecute those who do not share in the message. No game belongs to a person like that.<br /> <br /> Finally, the deepest problem, the one that seems to get missed over and over again, is that the the whole synthesis of the game revolves around a theme you all don't like. It's not enough to merely change surface elements, or even craft elements, but deep structural and idiomatic pieces. To change a game like this into what you all want is to honestly just create another game. This is why general discussion on the subject leans towards finding another game. It's genuinely, deeply, too much. Promethean will fight anyone trying to do this at every turn, and the game you have at the end is not it's own distinct thing. You might as well slice up a person's brain and put them into a robot suit, regardless of whether they wanted to or not. It's crass-vulgar. Useless, really. Better to just find a different game. When we say that, we're thinking of the people asking as much as we are thinking about the game.<br /> <br /> Kindly take your attitude and burn it in a fire. We're not your fucking enemies here, however much you might want us to be.<br /> <br /> I am so very, very tired.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>OK, really trying to make myself clear without ruffling any feathers. Here is what I, and I can only hope I understand my fellow Hackers well enough to speak for them, have a problem with:<br /> <br /> THERE IS NO &quot;OTHER GAME&quot; THAT USES THE THEMES OF ALCHEMY AND ARTIFIAL LIFE. We don't have somewhere else to go and discus what that game should be. Most of the ideas we would like to use for that game are already a part of this one. I can only speak for myself, but I sincerely mean no harm to a game that clearly means a lot to you. I wish you well, and I apologize for having derailed this thread; it was just that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> had so eloquently described the issues I have with the game, namely it's focus being a bit TOO narrow for my very small gaming group.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, and knowing that Promethean isn't for everyone, it would be nice if, when you see someone is working on a hack, you just walk away. The game you love will still be there, safe and sound and exactly as intended; we're just using some...leftover clay. An ember or two of stolen fire. To put it another way, think of us as trying to build our own creature, but we don't even have a proper lab or castle, and all the local graveyards are very well guarded. You are correct, we are NOT enemies, and I don't want to be. But please don't tell me to take anything of mine and burn it. My attitude, at least the one I hold in my heart, but may not convey well in text form, is one of wanting to work on a project in peace, but having seen far too many labs set ablaze. I really do think Onyx Path trapped lightning in a bottle, and I want some of that lightning for myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-16-2016, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:16:10-07:00","id":951768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951755#post951755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THERE IS NO &quot;OTHER GAME&quot; THAT USES THE THEMES OF ALCHEMY AND ARTIFIAL LIFE.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Demon? They're looking for the meaning of their existence (Cipher), live stolen lives (Covers) and seek to ascend to their own idea of a better life (their own Hell). Most Gadgets can easily be alchemical weirdness-ed. They can try and become as human as they can or they can be proud of the thing they are.<br /> <br /> You could also wait for Deviant and see what's possible with it. Hell you could probably achieve what you're looking for with only the Core Mortal book and a willing ST.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's a matter of perspective. It's easier to play a Vampire in a Changelings game than a Changeling in a Vampire game, because you can easily create a Vampire Kith, but can't easily create a Changelings Clan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:21:34-07:00","id":951771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951731#post951731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-insensate alchemists certainly use less alchemy, since they don't use vitriol to give themselves powers or merits, or harvest outside sources for refueling, but being able to store up to 9 points and regenerate without actually doing anything 3 points a week is certainly better than some minor templates have gotten, which is the niche alchemist fills beyond antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI was not aware of this; thank you for the information. I was just going on what's been said in this thread. With that mind, yes, I think Alchemists COULD be allies for Prometheans, but it would require either:<br /> \u200b1) A great deal of trust/precautions on the Promethean's part.<br /> 2) Alternative sources of Vitriol?<br /> I don't know if I ever brought this up, but I had this idea about a Promethean, or maybe a Redeemed, going around deliberately hunting Pandorans and destroying them, as a way to &quot;clean up&quot; mistakes that have been made with the Divine Fire. (Calling Pandorans &quot;mistakes&quot; is ok, right? That's pretty much what the books call them?) The second part of that idea was that the remains of those Pandorans might be rendered into something... <i>useful</i> through an alchemical process. Maybe squeeze a little Pyros out of them? Boil them down into small amounts of Vitriol?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:25:36-07:00","id":951773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951771#post951771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI was not aware of this; thank you for the information. I was just going on what's been said in this thread. With that mind, yes, I think Alchemists COULD be allies for Prometheans, but it would require either:<br /> \u200b1) A great deal of trust/precautions on the Promethean's part.<br /> 2) Alternative sources of Vitriol?<br /> I don't know if I ever brought this up, but I had this idea about a Promethean, or maybe a Redeemed, going around deliberately hunting Pandorans and destroying them, as a way to &quot;clean up&quot; mistakes that have been made with the Divine Fire. (Calling Pandorans &quot;mistakes&quot; is ok, right? That's pretty much what the books call them?) The second part of that idea was that the remains of those Pandorans might be rendered into something... <i>useful</i> through an alchemical process. Maybe squeeze a little Pyros out of them? Boil them down into small amounts of Vitriol?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1- Yes, they are mistakes. I think everyone will agree.<br /> 2- You might be able to gather some Pyros out of them, but not Vitriol since there's not a trace of it in them. Vitriol is created by a Promethean and when a Pandoran gets its claws on it, it consumes it and mutates almost instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:34:43-07:00","id":951779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951643#post951643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't around when VtR came out, so I can't speak much about that. But regarding Alchemists, I haven't seen anyone complaining that they're not playable. Most people who dislike their presentation dislike it because they don't see their motivations as antagonists being believable enough.Others (such as myself) are merely opposed to the suggestion that the divide is as dichotomous as &quot;playable Alchemists&quot; and &quot;Insatiate Alchemists&quot;. Them being antagonists is fine, but must all antagonist Alchemests be unsympathetic?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair? Nobody afflicted by Disquiet (whom Insatiate are bound to be) seems like a good representation of &quot;themselves&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:08:52-07:00","id":951802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951768#post951768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like Demon? They're looking for the meaning of their existence (Cipher), live stolen lives (Covers) and seek to ascend to their own idea of a better life (their own Hell). Most Gadgets can easily be alchemical weirdness-ed. They can try and become as human as they can or they can be proud of the thing they are.<br /> <br /> You could also wait for Deviant and see what's possible with it. Hell you could probably achieve what you're looking for with only the Core Mortal book and a willing ST.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's a matter of perspective. It's easier to play a Vampire in a Changelings game than a Changeling in a Vampire game, because you can easily create a Vampire Kith, but can't easily create a Changelings Clan</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI see what you're saying, but there are definitely reasons why D@3m0n won't work:<br /> 1. I absolutely reject the premise that the G-M is actually God, or even <i>a</i> god; it's clearly the Weaver, having somehow survived the death of the OWoD.<br /> 2. At least one of the players at my table is super freaked out by demons of any description.<br /> 3. Another $20 PDF I might never get any use out of. If I can't thumb through a book at my local game/comic store, I'm not buying it. Bad enough my copies of W:tF1e and P:tC just sit around gathering dust, no sense cluttering up my hard drive.<br /> <br /> Maybe Deviant will work better for my group. I certainly hope so.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:22:39-07:00","id":951807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951526#post951526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No... the text is actually fairly explicit that it's because the Alchemists getting the focus are supposed to be <i>antagonists</i>. Even with the various details on specific Insatiate Alchemists in the write up there are characters you can sympathize with (even some of the more monstrous ones).<br /> <br /> &quot;Good&quot; Alchemists aren't given a reason to interact with the PCs (and are actually given reasons to largely avoid the PCs) because that doesn't serve any narrative niche for the stories Promethean is aimed at creating. Having these Alchemists successfully seek out Prometheans to for working relations with them runs counter to a lot of the thematic elements of the game, so that's not something the base-line game encourages. Having them as antagonists doesn't really work if they're not actually antagonizing the PCs.<br /> <br /> The Insatiate Alchemists have a niche to fill as antagonists. So that's the focus the text takes.<br /> <br /> Why, exactly, is that a problem? After all this I still don't see why that choice, beyond personal preference, is <i>bad</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> His rather large body of work (including a number of writing credits on CofD books dedicated to antagonists) would suggest this isn't the case. So it seems more appropriate to give him a bit more charity in the reading about how the editorial choice to make the antagonists in PtC 2e the way they are was for a design reason rather than some deficiency in his skills.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, for example, the focus is on things that want to kill Prometheans (and it isn't just the Alchemists, who don't really want to kill Prometheans as much as killing them is a side effect of what they really want) is because part of the core themes of the game are how the Created are outsiders that are supernaturally rejected by the world around them. That isolation and alienation is a large part of their drive to seek out the Great Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a good Alchemist who just really needs some juice from a Promethean so she can do something the audience would find important, like save her daughter? Or a good alchemist who just didn't get the memo that Prometheans are bad news and wants to study one, before falling to Disquiet? Why doesn't the text support telling those stories? I mean, the text itself is kind of confused, in that it goes on rants about how all 'Black' alchemists are evil, then presents a rather sympathetic Alchemist as a sample character.<br /> <br /> And relatively friendly Alchemists won't damage the themes of the book. After all, they'd still fall victim to disquiet, and start wanting to cut up the Promethean or whatever.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951528#post951528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note on the entire &quot;Matt can't write antagonists beyond 'these guys want to kill you' front&quot;, you are talking about the man who is responsible for every bit of information we have on fetches in Changeling the Lost.<br /> <br /> You might want to reconsider your position.</div> </div> </div> </div>And his Heroes and Alchemists have been completly devoid of what makes a good antagonist beyond 'they want to kill you.' So either he's always had trouble making good antagonists, and has thus far been moderated by other writers, or he's forgotten how to make good antagonists.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951592#post951592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Regardless of whether or not I know how to write antagonists (YMMV), alchemists were written <i>before</i> Heroes, and I didn't get either of them &quot;wrong.&quot; You just don't like them.<br /> <br /> (But, as others point out, shockingly the alchemists in the antagonists section are meant to be antagonists. I can't remember, when <b>VtR</b> first came out, were there big threads complaining about how the book didn't support playing VII?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the first kind of hard to believe seeing as how the Alchemists got a sidebar of 'there are good alchemists, you'll just never see them,' just like heroes did. And the Heroes sidebar was in reaction to massive fan backlash. I'll just file this alongside the 'Beasts aren't meant to be a metaphor for minorities.'<br /> <br /> And alchemists and heroes both share the problem of having the text attempt to shove their evils down the readers throat, evils that aren't really borne out in a deeper reading, leading to increased confusion.<br /> <br /> And you do realize that you can have sympathetic antagonists, right? Like, the Seers, the Pure, Belials Brood, VII, even Loyalists can be sympathetic figures. In fact, being on some level sympathetic is part of what makes an antagonist good. However, you seem to fear that making them at all sympathetic will ruin the game or something. (And anyways, keep tilting at that windmill of people wanting playable alchemists. There's been like two people that have been saying that, and neither of them's been paticularly loud). The real problems with alchemists are how hard you try to make them unsympathetic, the ableism, and the fact that the text is rather confused as to wether or not alchemists can be sympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","user":"notanautomaton","date":". 08-16-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:28:28-07:00","id":951813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951802#post951802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI see what you're saying, but there are definitely reasons why D@3m0n won't work:<br /> 1. I absolutely reject the premise that the G-M is actually God, or even <i>a</i> god; it's clearly the Weaver, having somehow survived the death of the OWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing that's not the premise of Demon, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951802#post951802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. At least one of the players at my table is super freaked out by demons of any description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a competely legit reason not to play it. That's a bummer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951802#post951802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Another $20 PDF I might never get any use out of. If I can't thumb through a book at my local game/comic store, I'm not buying it. Bad enough my copies of W:tF1e and P:tC just sit around gathering dust, no sense cluttering up my hard drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can buy it PoD if you aren't into PDFs. If you refuse to buy any product that isn't on game store shelves though, you're never going to be able to buy CofD products. We'll see what White Wolf does with WoD though, who knows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951802#post951802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Deviant will work better for my group. I certainly hope so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviant looks <i>awesome</i> from what's been teased so far, hopefully it'll suit your needs. You do know it's going to be PDF and PoD too though, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:21:08-07:00","id":951858,"title":"","content":"When I said find a different game, I didn't necessarily mean a ChroD game. There's a whole universe of games beyond ChroD that can fit your niche. If I have time between my game today and parsing more of Genius, I might even drop some examples that I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:28:26-07:00","id":951860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=950986#post950986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy, these last few pages sure were an interesting ride...<br /> I don't really understand the hate for alchemists. That whole section kind of feels like Matt didn't want to rehash the backlash for the first draft version of Heroes, so he decided to preempt it by putting in several #NotAllAlchemist bits himself. Almost every subsection has a bit about how not all alchemists are driven to madness and hatred, and that they can even do good. And yet apparently people keep telling me that the whole section is filled with how all alchemists are evil and you can never have a sympathetic one.<br /> <br /> Then again, people also think that Centimani are great and shouldn't be considered bad guys, mostly because they forget that to be <i>trans</i>human, you first have to be <i>human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> is their any links I could have so I could see the backlash you speak of? <br /> <br /> I think Playable alchemists would be an interesting option though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:32:20-07:00","id":951864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951807#post951807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And his Heroes and Alchemists have been completly devoid of what makes a good antagonist beyond 'they want to kill you.' So either he's always had trouble making good antagonists, and has thus far been moderated by other writers, or he's forgotten how to make good antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Take a week off for ignoring my warning.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http:/