ll me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:57:20-07:00","id":951893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951813#post951813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can buy it PoD if you aren't into PDFs. If you refuse to buy any product that isn't on game store shelves though, you're never going to be able to buy CofD products. We'll see what White Wolf does with WoD though, who knows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Deviant looks <i>awesome</i> from what's been teased so far, hopefully it'll suit your needs. You do know it's going to be PDF and PoD too though, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even a question of liking or disliking PDFs, it's not wanting to WASTE money on a book I can't use. POD costs even more. The only reason my group has a copy of V20 is that we got it <u>used</u> from our Local Comics Shop(LCS). I REALLY hope White Wolf goes back to actually printing books to put on store shelves. Buying something without being able to really examine it has been a big mistake before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:16:04-07:00","id":951907,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you want to discuss the merits of PoD, PDF and/or having inventory taking space on retail shelves create a new thread about it. This thread seems to have run its course, if the off topic posts continue it will be closed.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:56:23-07:00","id":951994,"title":"","content":"you know, I'm looking at all of those 21 pages of the thread, and I really don't understand what all the fuss is about- is it because the only alchemists found in the antagonists section wants to kill you? Matt has said a number of times it is mostly out of word count, and if he'll have a chance he'll expand them at a Player Guide. Is it because every alchemist who wants to be inhuman is said to be crazy? Most people who are considered to be sane don't use weird occult rites in order to transform themselves into inhuman being. Is it because in Promethean being human is said to be something good and that you should aspire to it? It was the stated to be the case in the Open Development, so we all should have had enough time to prepare for it. If you love some aspects of the game, instead of using all of the word count in complaining about it and blaming the writers and devs, use that free time to hack the game (not &quot;fix&quot;- fix means that there is a fundamental problem in the game's premise, which is kinda insulting to the game' fans and writers since it is the game's point).<br /> <br /> seriously, if you want to play a transhumanist Promethean setting, make a transhumanist Promethean setting. No one is going to stop you, and no one is going to write it for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:13:20-07:00","id":952015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know, I'm looking at all of those 21 pages of the thread, and I really don't understand what all the fuss is about</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember the last few days correctly, it's about the confused writing of the Alchemists which paint them as murderous-irredeemable-crazy-inhuman monsters unworthy of sympathy while at the same time saying #NotAllAlchemists. Some people have problems with such a writing and (I assume) would like a few lines to be corrected before the final release, such as the association of madness = evil and the idea that harvesting a Promethean in order to save your cancerous 8-year old daughter is inherently evil (both of which aren't written textually in the Alchemist section, mind)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:25:02-07:00","id":952025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952015#post952015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I remember the last few days correctly, it's about the confused writing of the Alchemists which paint them as murderous-irredeemable-crazy-inhuman monsters unworthy of sympathy while at the same time saying #NotAllAlchemists. Some people have problems with such a writing and (I assume) would like a few lines to be corrected before the final release, such as the association of madness = evil and the idea that harvesting a Promethean in order to save your cancerous 8-year old daughter is inherently evil (both of which aren't written textually in the Alchemist section, mind)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I personally didn't got that picture from the write up- I've just assumed that considering that it is a game about prometheans, I would see alchemists from how a promethean would see them- a threat, someone who wants to harvest their organs and stuff them into small vials. For a promethean, it doesn't matter if the alchemists does it in order to live forever, or to save a 8 years old child. The alchemist would still kill her, and as such, a threat to deal with. But I assume it is a matter of word count and personal taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:48:24-07:00","id":952045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951755#post951755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THERE IS NO &quot;OTHER GAME&quot; THAT USES THE THEMES OF ALCHEMY AND ARTIFIAL LIFE. We don't have somewhere else to go and discus what that game should be. Most of the ideas we would like to use for that game are already a part of this one. I can only speak for myself, but I sincerely mean no harm to a game that clearly means a lot to you. I wish you well, and I apologize for having derailed this thread; it was just that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> had so eloquently described the issues I have with the game, namely it's focus being a bit TOO narrow for my very small gaming group.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, and knowing that Promethean isn't for everyone, it would be nice if, when you see someone is working on a hack, you just walk away. The game you love will still be there, safe and sound and exactly as intended; we're just using some...leftover clay. An ember or two of stolen fire. To put it another way, think of us as trying to build our own creature, but we don't even have a proper lab or castle, and all the local graveyards are very well guarded. You are correct, we are NOT enemies, and I don't want to be. But please don't tell me to take anything of mine and burn it. My attitude, at least the one I hold in my heart, but may not convey well in text form, is one of wanting to work on a project in peace, but having seen far too many labs set ablaze. I really do think Onyx Path trapped lightning in a bottle, and I want some of that lightning for myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said I was out of this thread, but I do feel a need to come back and echo Mangle for a moment: Can people stop telling posters who want to change a game or disagree with some core concept to &quot;find another game&quot;? It's condescending and, frankly, only serves to make people double down on their opinions. I know the intentions are good, but to someone who is displeased with all or part of a book it comes off more like, &quot;Your ideas are wrong, go away&quot;.<br /> <br /> Shifting systems isn't always the easy sideways shuffle its made out to be. For starters there are costs, finding a new game can require a lot of time, money and effort. And, in all likelihood, the same amount of hacking it into desired shape as one would have to put into Promethean (or whatever game they take issue with). In the end there might not even be another game that comes closer to the desired intent, and if there is it might be strictly inferior in quality. Onyx Path sets a pretty high bar which can be hard for other games to match. Then there is the matter of teaching a group (and oneself) a brand new system and learning all the little quirks and traits not immediately apparent in the system. Anyone who has ever GM'd a less than system savvy group will not want to go through that process too often.<br /> <br /> Individually, there may also be the matter of world continuity. I, for instance, run all my ChroD games in a shared universe, which makes switching games functionally impossible (or at least a heap-load of work). I suspect I'm not alone in that, and that many theme hackers want to maintain their own vision of an overarching world of darkness. And that's a good thing, I don't think ChroD would be half as successful if players only ever stuck to one line.<br /> <br /> Theme hacking comes from a place of love. A person does not delve that deep into a game they couldn't give two shits about. What sort of love can vary, perhaps its a love of the Chronicles of Darkness as a whole or maybe just some small facet of a splat that snagged the heart strings. Telling someone to abandon that thing they love, that they are wrong, that it wasn't made for them...what can you honestly expect to happen? Are they going to say &quot;oh, I get it&quot; and walk away? No, you'll be met with bitterness and staunch resolution, which helps no one.<br /> <br /> So please, you don't have to acquiesce to every complaint and assertion, just don't tell posters to find another game.<br /> <br /> That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:11:57-07:00","id":952062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952045#post952045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you'll be met with bitterness and staunch resolution, which helps no one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that &quot;met with&quot; has generally meant &quot;started with&quot; and that the issue has literally never been &quot;this person is working on a hack&quot; in isolation.<br /> <br /> As has been highlighted multiple times despite Mangle's direct ignorance of those occasions, it's the associated attitude brought along as baggage from Day 1 of the arguments. Data rightly observes that it's wholly doable to ask about adjusting the game to change a central or pervasive element without antagonizing the base game.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with attempting to hack the material, but listen: a &quot;place of love&quot; that leads a person to persistently shit-talk the things they don't like in the course of purporting to try and make something that better suits their needs, compare people who take issue with that shit-talking to an angry mob, and refuse to comprehend the relevance of an analogy comparing the carrying of a volatile force of supernatural change in your being to constantly undergoing one of the most recognizable and irrevocable chemical reactions while simultaneously applying that metaphor as the banner under which they have enfolded everyone who disagrees with their behavior in aggregate? That place needs serious housecleaning, renovating, and redecorating, because it does not invite passersby to have a pleasant chat and help its proprietor figure out what to do with the space.<br /> <br /> You don't have to find another game by any stretch, but if you're going to make a mess in the common area then you're going to get your share of complaints from the neighbors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:43:29-07:00","id":952096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know, I'm looking at all of those 21 pages of the thread, and I really don't understand what all the fuss is about- is it because the only alchemists found in the antagonists section wants to kill you?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's that the reasons the alchemists want to kill you lack nuance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt has said a number of times it is mostly out of word count, and if he'll have a chance he'll expand them at a Player Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the people he has said that two have responded multiple times that their issue with the presentation of alchemists is not with the fact that they're not playable out of the gate (in fact, they're pretty easy to play with some pretty minor hacking). It's that the book is presenting a dichotomy between playable alchemists and completely irredeemable antagonists. No word count needs to be spent to cover playable Alchemists, it's totally understandable that that isn't possible. But it would have been nice if the sections that attempt to acknowledge that they're only covering antagonist alchemists hadn't equated antagonist alchemists with psychopathic murderers and non-antagonist alchemists with reasonable people. Ally &lt;-----&gt; Antagonist and Swell Guy &lt;-----&gt; Cold-Blooded murderer should be two different spectrums. And it's ok to focus on one end of either or both spectrums, but it's frustrating to imply that the position on one is intrinsically linked with the position on the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it because every alchemist who wants to be inhuman is said to be crazy?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a separate, but related issue to the above, but yes, it is a problem to some.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people who are considered to be sane don't use weird occult rites in order to transform themselves into inhuman being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's helpful to associate &quot;insane&quot; with &quot;morally reprehensible&quot; and that's all I'm going to say on that subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it because in Promethean being human is said to be something good and that you should aspire to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, for some people, it is. I don't understand that complaint, as it is such a core conceit of Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951994#post951994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was the stated to be the case in the Open Development, so we all should have had enough time to prepare for it. If you love some aspects of the game, instead of using all of the word count in complaining about it and blaming the writers and devs, use that free time to hack the game (not &quot;fix&quot;- fix means that there is a fundamental problem in the game's premise, which is kinda insulting to the game' fans and writers since it is the game's point).<br /> <br /> seriously, if you want to play a transhumanist Promethean setting, make a transhumanist Promethean setting. No one is going to stop you, and no one is going to write it for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:45:47-07:00","id":952097,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's fair to ask for, &quot;why not just try a different game,&quot; off the table. Sometimes that is the right answer. Hell, that's how I got started with the WoD back in the day (my other options at the time were WEG Star Wars and D&amp;D... so you can imagine a lot of itches were left unscratched). I wanted something that would have been not worth hacking what I had, compared to the effort of starting with something new.<br /> <br /> Trying a different game doesn't have to mean leaving the CofD either (and Onyx Path has started putting a lot more free preview material out there which reduces the cost/risk issue). Between the other major game lines, and the rather large number of official, semi-official, and fan-made minor templates, I have a ton of material to work with if something isn't suiting me. CtL is practically a go-to game for lots of people I know for, &quot;instead of a crossover mess, just make everything with Seeming/Kith combos and creative Durances,&quot; since the Seeming/Kith combinations cover almost anything you can imagine, and you can put any window dressing you want on it. Victor Frakenstein actually works surprisingly well as a Keeper who takes humans for &quot;raw ingredients&quot; and makes them into Creations in his Arcadian laboratory, only to never be satisfied with them and toss them aside for his next attempt; scattering his realm with various Creations stuck in a loop of hatred and longing for acceptance from him, while a rare few regain the agency to leave and set out on their own. With 2e's Court systems, you can have a setting were the local Courts actually encourage individuals to try out different Courts over time to explore their nature (mirroring changing Refinements). And I haven't had to house-rule anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:58:31-07:00","id":952105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952096#post952096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. It's that the reasons the alchemists want to kill you lack nuance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this position is difficult for some of us to get, because Alchemists want to kill you for Vitriol. That's it. The nuance is in what they're going to do with it once they get it. &quot;I want to save my 8 year old child with a terminal disease,&quot; vs. &quot;I want to live forever,&quot; are not why they're killing Prometheans. It's why they want Vitriol. Vitriol is, unfortunately for Prometheans, something that can only be gained by harvesting it from the Promethean.<br /> <br /> Killing the Prometheans is, essentially, incidental to the Alchemist. It's not where anything needs nuance, because it's simply a metaphysical fact of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's that the book is presenting a dichotomy between playable alchemists and completely irredeemable antagonists. </div> </div> </div>I haven't really seen anyone try to respond with or engage with my point about addiction regarding this. To me if feels like a bit of a cop out to ignore a reason to make this a dichotomy and just insist that making it a dichotomy is inherently a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:03:01-07:00","id":952110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952105#post952105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this position is difficult for some of us to get, because Alchemists want to kill you for Vitriol. That's it. The nuance is in what they're going to do with it once they get it. &quot;I want to save my 8 year old child with a terminal disease,&quot; vs. &quot;I want to live forever,&quot; are not why they're killing Prometheans. It's why they want Vitriol. Vitriol is, unfortunately for Prometheans, something that can only be gained by harvesting it from the Promethean.<br /> <br /> Killing the Prometheans is, essentially, incidental to the Alchemist. It's not where anything needs nuance, because it's simply a metaphysical fact of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but it's the same issue, just with an extra degree of separation. The reasons Alchemists are said to want Vitriol lack nuance, and they can only get vitriol by killing you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952105#post952105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't really seen anyone try to respond with or engage with my point about addiction regarding this. To me if feels like a bit of a cop out to ignore a reason to make this a dichotomy and just insist that making it a dichotomy is inherently a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I did mean to respond to that, but I lost track of that in a lot of other stuff going on in this conversation and others. I'll go back and take a look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:28:50-07:00","id":952125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951351#post951351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still feel it's a bit of an unfair reading of the text. It feels far more like, &quot;I want Alchemists that aren't want the books did,&quot; is being allowed to bias the reading more than what the text actually says; esp. with the caveat the book makes in the beginning to not treat any absolute statements are anything more than, &quot;usually.&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, I think where the text is trying to make things binary, is different from the kind of spectrum people actually want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're talking past each other a bit here. I actually quite like the Alchemists as presented in the book. I just don't like the couple of places where it seems to me that the book actively attempts to quash the inherent potential for nuance that the Alchemists it presents do have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951351#post951351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I read it (and I've reread it a few times because of this thread), I get the impression that Alchemists are more like drug-users, and the Insatiate are addicts (I'm aware I'm vastly oversimplifying the factors that go into addiction in this). You're either addicted to something or you aren't. There's plenty of room for a spectrum of how that addiction impacts you life, but being one or not is binary. Alchemists that avoid the addiction of the Insatiate do so by having to avoid using Pyros too much, and pretty much avoid Vitriol completely. A non-Insatiate Alchemist hanging out with Prometheans is like a sober alcoholic going to bars all the time. It's a rare few might find power in the challenge and successful resistance, but most are just going to find it painful to be constantly tempted and seek to avoid such situations instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and as I've said before, I'm fine with &quot;Insatiate&quot; and &quot;not Insatiate&quot; being a binary thing. What I'm not fine with is implications that Insatiate alchemists must hate their humanity enough to abandon it altogether, cannot be sane and rational, must be more interested in power than knowledge, must be driven to commit atrocities against the Created out of self-hating obsession and despising of humanity, and must not &quot;know better&quot; than to seek the Divine Fire and Vitriol. If Insatiate alchemists are addicts, where are the addicts who know they have a problem but can't stop themselves? Where are the addicts that want to get clean <i>after this one last time</i>? Where are the people who do take Vitriol but have managed to stave off becoming addicted? Where are the people who are not yet Vitriol addicts, but have gotten way into the gateway drug, Pyros, and are one little push away from trying Vitriol?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951351#post951351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't really make that a spectrum, and that's where the division between the two seems to be intended to lie. Where you can put in a spectrum is really on all the different ways the Insatiate mentally cope with the fact that they're addicts to Vitriol. Do they try to justify it as serving some cause? Do they just not care? Etc. And I think the book does provide plenty of examples on that spectrum to illustrate that it should be highly varied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I only see one example of the spectrum you mention being explored. And I love her! She's a great example of what I like about the Alchemist writeup and wish I saw more of. However, I see far more examples of the book implying that such a spectrum doesn't exist for the Insatiate. And that's very frustrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-16-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:52:20-07:00","id":952133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952096#post952096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's helpful to associate &quot;insane&quot; with &quot;morally reprehensible&quot; and that's all I'm going to say on that subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>We need a Morality-Neutral term for a person who's mental state makes them a danger to themselves and others. Unbalanced? Unhinged? Unglued? Deranged?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:59:51-07:00","id":952137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952133#post952133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a Morality-Neutral term for a person who's mental state makes them a danger to themselves and others. Unbalanced? Unhinged? Unglued? Deranged?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we need to stop painting characters who's mental state makes them a danger to themselves and others as villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:12:56-07:00","id":952146,"title":"","content":"\u201cinsane\u201d is a morally neutral term. As for Morality, 2e doesn't have such a stat.<br /> <br /> All alchemists want Vitriol? Perhaps. But not all alchemists are willing to do what it takes to <i>get</i> Vitriol. Those alchemists who consider Prometheans to be people, out at least on par with animals, may well say \u201cif I have to cut open a person in order to get Vitriol, then I'm going do without it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not a very stable position to take: between the fact that alchemists are very driven individuals (you don't get too tap into the Divine Fire without something obsessive driving you) and that they're subject to Disquiet, it's arguably only a matter of time before the alchemist starts rationalizing that his needs outweigh the Promethean's, and that maybe the Promethean isn't really a person after all. Still, even if it is inevitable that every alchemist will end up that way, they don't necessarily start that way; and potentially friendly interactions can take place in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:17:25-07:00","id":952149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952137#post952137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we need to stop painting characters who's mental state makes them a danger to themselves and others as villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>And vice versa. I know there's a tendency to say that evil men are insane; but it's just not so: someone can be perfectly sane and evil \u2014 which is perhaps one of the most disturbing things about evil: being sane doesn't mean that you're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:19:58-07:00","id":952150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952137#post952137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we need to stop painting characters who's mental state makes them a danger to themselves and others as villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are victims too, after all. Even if they are cast as antagonists; after all, being an antagonists doesn't force you into being morally wrong, right or any other judgemental quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:22:32-07:00","id":952151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952062#post952062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been highlighted multiple times despite Mangle's direct ignorance of those occasions, it's the associated attitude brought along as baggage from Day 1 of the arguments. Data rightly observes that it's wholly doable to ask about adjusting the game to change a central or pervasive element without antagonizing the base game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for everyone, but my attitude is a direct reflection of how my point of view is treated. That's the last I will say about that here.<br /> <br /> So, without access to the book, I guess I really just found myself ranting in general, huh? Sorry about that, I've been stressed out about some other stuff, like how my gaming group has fallen apart. I think it's been about 7 months since even had a reason to pick up a character sheet. I try every week, but I can't even get most of the group together for any reason. With such a small group,(5 people) if two more don't show up, you can't play. Since escaping into games and fantasy worlds is my main coping mechanism for all the <i>other </i>\u200bsources of stress in my life, you can imagine how this effects me.<br /> <br /> So, what kind of stuff can Alchemists do? That would help to decide how interested I am in playing one. Yes, a know that reeks of &quot;Power Gaming&quot;, but let's be honest, <b><i><u>Kewl Powahs</u></i></b> are part of the appeal of any splat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:29:13-07:00","id":952156,"title":"","content":"As written, Alchemists can perform individual Distillations, but only in the form of alchemical concoctions that they prepare ahead of time and carry with them.<br /> <br /> Personally, that strikes me as problematic: there's a reason why Distillations are packaged together into Alembics, namely that which Distillations you get comes from how much Pyros to put into the Alembic. What I'd do would be to let alchemists learn Alembics, but increase the Pyros cost of everything by one: that is, the alchemist must spend one Pyros to get the \u201cfree\u201d effect for the scene, plus one Pyros to get the first Distillation, plus another to get the second Distillation, plus one more to get the third Distillation. Mix a little bit of reagents (materialized Pyros) into your concoction, and you get mild results; dump a lot in, and BOOM!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-16-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:31:47-07:00","id":952157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952149#post952149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And vice versa. I know there's a tendency to say that evil men are insane; but it's just not so: someone can be perfectly sane and evil \u2014 which is perhaps one of the most disturbing things about evil: being sane doesn't mean that you're good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:36:08-07:00","id":952161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952151#post952151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for everyone, but my attitude is a direct reflection of how my point of view is treated. That's the last I will say about that here.<br /> <br /> So, without access to the book, I guess I really just found myself ranting in general, huh? Sorry about that, I've been stressed out about some other stuff, like how my gaming group has fallen apart. I think it's been about 7 months since even had a reason to pick up a character sheet. I try every week, but I can't even get most of the group together for any reason. With such a small group,(5 people) if two more don't show up, you can't play. Since escaping into games and fantasy worlds is my main coping mechanism for all the <i>other </i>\u200bsources of stress in my life, you can imagine how this effects me.<br /> <br /> So, what kind of stuff can Alchemists do? That would help to decide how interested I am in playing one. Yes, a know that reeks of &quot;Power Gaming&quot;, but let's be honest, <b><i><u>Kewl Powahs</u></i></b> are part of the appeal of any splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Demon or Mummy? Those also work excellently with small and/or sporadic groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:42:02-07:00","id":952164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952146#post952146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Morality, 2e doesn't have such a stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant morally-neutral, sorry.<br /> <br /> I define &quot;villain&quot; as a person who does bad things on a regular basis, typically without very good reasons. Whether that person is Sane(legal term for &quot;Competent to Stand Trail&quot;) is irrelevant to that definition.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:42:07-07:00","id":952165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952149#post952149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And vice versa. I know there's a tendency to say that evil men are insane; but it's just not so: someone can be perfectly sane and evil \u2014 which is perhaps one of the most disturbing things about evil: being sane doesn't mean that you're good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I usually zoom out and slap myself each time I try to think about characters in terms of good or evil; they are characters. They perform actions. These actions are guided by reasons. *Sometimes* I find it useful to categorize these in terms of good and evil. But I try to judge acts, not characters, so to speak. And preferrably, not judge at all, just understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:52:22-07:00","id":952172,"title":"","content":"And that's usually (but not always) the right thing to do. Most of the time, you're not dealing with Hitler; so seeking to understand is laudible. Every so often, though, you run into a case where seeking to understand why someone regularly does bad things costs precious time that would be better spent stopping him. <br /> <br /> Unless you're running a profiling procedural chronicle, a la <i>Criminal Minds</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:54:11-07:00","id":952174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952151#post952151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for everyone, but my attitude is a direct reflection of how my point of view is treated. That's the last I will say about that here.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the treatment of your point of view is a direct reflection of your attitude. At some point, someone needs to be the one to make the first step. How about this? Your dislike of some of the central themes of Promethean is valid. You are more than welcome to hold those opinions. If you seek help in trying to change those things in your own homebrew, I will gladly leave you to do so in peace. If you attack the themes of Promethean I enjoy, I will defend them, but otherwise I am happy to live and let live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952151#post952151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what kind of stuff can Alchemists do? That would help to decide how interested I am in playing one. Yes, a know that reeks of &quot;Power Gaming&quot;, but let's be honest, <b><i><u>Kewl Powahs</u></i></b> are part of the appeal of any splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a sort of mini power stat called Magnitude that goes from 1 to 5, determines how much Pyros they can store at a time (in the form of potions, powders, salves, etc, called &quot;preparations&quot;) and how many they can spend per turn, how much Pyros they can generate (generally a small amount per week), and how many Distillations they can know (a Distillation is an individual power from a Transmutation). They can also steal Vitriol (which is like Promethean's version of Arcane Experience from Mage) from Prometheans and use them to buy Merits that represent physical changes to the body or brain chemistry without having to meet the prerequisites. That means even supernatural Merits and Merits that normally require a specific supernatural template are fair game, as long as they represent physical changes, not specialized training. So, Giant Size is fine even though it's normally character creation only, but a Fighting Style wouldn't really work. Finally, they can also spend Vitriol to buy Dread Powers that are normally available to Pandorans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-16-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:00:15-07:00","id":952177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952125#post952125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't like the couple of places where it seems to me that the book actively attempts to quash the inherent potential for nuance that the Alchemists it presents do have.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's my point. &quot;..it seems to me...&quot; but why does it seem that way to you? I'm reading the same text, and I'm not getting that intent. So the reasonable assumption is that we're bringing different' biases/preconceptions to the text that need to be separated from the text, rather than just insisting that &quot;...it seems to me...&quot; be sufficient without challenge or analysis of how much weight that feeling should be given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Insatiate alchemists are addicts, where are the addicts who know they have a problem but can't stop themselves? Where are the addicts that want to get clean <i>after this one last time</i>? Where are the people who do take Vitriol but have managed to stave off becoming addicted? Where are the people who are not yet Vitriol addicts, but have gotten way into the gateway drug, Pyros, and are one little push away from trying Vitriol? </div> </div> </div>In a supplement with the space to get into all this detail? I mean, lets say each of those gets ~3 pages of material between general discussion and example characters. That's 9 pages worth of material (and I'd say you'd have to a very good writer to hit every note you really should to thoroughly explore those in just that much space). Where is that coming out of the core book?<br /> <br /> The text is clear Alchemists are truncated in presentation to focus on their primary function in the game (the Insatiate antagonists harvesting you for Vitriol), and Matt's made it clear that he's up for expanding on Alchemists in future supplements...<br /> <br /> I just don't see the reasonable nature of this aspect of the complaint. I can't think of a single CofD core book that doesn't have an antagonist in the antagonist section that couldn't use a lot of expansion, but clearly was cut to the minimum of what the ST is going to need to use them for their primary purpose in the core game. This only really works if you agree with the reading of the text as saying, &quot;these don't exist,&quot; instead of saying, &quot;these exist but aren't the focus so we're not getting into them.&quot;<br /> <br /> At a certain point in all this, I think we need to start seeing actual citations. Dancing around vague issues with unspecified statements can only get us so far as a discussion. I can't try to explain why I see a different spin on something if I don't know exactly which wordings are bugging you when you read them.<br /> <br /> Though the specific, &quot;Where are the people who do take Vitriol but have managed to stave off becoming addicted,&quot; might not exist on purpose. Vitriol isn't a chemical drug. It's distilled divine power. Being able to &quot;dabble&quot; in Vitriol is very likely not something that's going to be included because it's too mind-warping for the human mind to handle without being permanently affected by it. Which also explains why the Insatiate descriptions are heavily weighted towards the one style you want to see more contrasts to; it's not something you can &quot;safely&quot; take one hit of and decide to never do again, or say &quot;just one more,&quot; without being delusional about the amount of control it has on you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:01:40-07:00","id":952180,"title":"","content":"Their mechanics sounds actually pretty cool. Sounds flavorful and crunchy in good balance!<br /> <br /> As for wasting time to stop Them Evildoers- well, when I'm a wrtier / storyteller, I'm not stopping anyone, I'm giving birth to them : P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:40:59-07:00","id":952193,"title":"","content":"I admit when I read the part about alchemist, the first thing which came to my mind was <i>&quot;Baccano!&quot;.</i> I wonder if the author used the anime as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:47:11-07:00","id":952194,"title":"","content":"would have asked what the hell you were talking about but im watching it and bo ku ra no as part of my towns anime club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:02:46-07:00","id":952203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's my point. &quot;..it seems to me...&quot; but why does it seem that way to you? I'm reading the same text, and I'm not getting that intent. So the reasonable assumption is that we're bringing different' biases/preconceptions to the text that need to be separated from the text, rather than just insisting that &quot;...it seems to me...&quot; be sufficient without challenge or analysis of how much weight that feeling should be given.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bias here is that I understand wordcount is limited and assume that they aren't going to waste it on alchemists that don't pose a threat to the Promethean protagonists. So when I see a sidebar using wordcount to talk about why they didn't use wordcount to talk about alchemists that aren't antagonistic towards Prometheans, I find it a little silly. And then when it goes on to describe the differences between the alchemists it does deem worthy of spending wordcount on and the ones it doesn't, and in doing so paints the group it doesn't talk about as reasonable people and the group it does talk about as unsympathetic monsters, it strikes me as setting up a dichotomy between &quot;good alchemists&quot; and &quot;bad alchemists&quot; instead of leaving room for nuance and interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a supplement with the space to get into all this detail? I mean, lets say each of those gets ~3 pages of material between general discussion and example characters. That's 9 pages worth of material (and I'd say you'd have to a very good writer to hit every note you really should to thoroughly explore those in just that much space). Where is that coming out of the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care about those Alchemists getting wordcount dedicated to them in this book, I care about this book dedicating wordcount to explaining that there are two types of alchemists: &quot;Sane, rational alchemists (who) are unlikely to come into a Promethean story&quot; and alchemists who &quot;hate their humanity enough to try to abandon it altogether&quot;, aren't &quot;more interested in knowledge than power&quot;, have a &quot;self-hating obsession&quot;, &quot;despise their own humanity&quot;, and don't &quot;know better&quot; than to seek the Divine Fire. If I come up with a concept for an Alchemist who has reason to seek Vitriol, is willing to kill Prometheans to get it, but is not a power-hungry misanthrope, I don't need three pages dedicated to telling me how to do that. But then the &quot;The Great Work&quot; sidebar lumps him in with the Alchemists who are unlikely to come into a Promethean story. That makes it feel to me like the book is trying to limit me in what kinds of Alchemist characters I bring into the game. I would feel <i>far less</i> constrained if the sidebar was simply removed, or better yet if it was shortened to only mention that Alchemists who don't kill Prometheans aren't likely to come up in a Promethean story and leave out the discussion of <i>why</i> the Alchemists who are likely to come up in a Promethean story kill Prometheans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text is clear Alchemists are truncated in presentation to focus on their primary function in the game (the Insatiate antagonists harvesting you for Vitriol), and Matt's made it clear that he's up for expanding on Alchemists in future supplements...</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I appreciate that. I wish it was done in a way that didn't close the door on Alchemists who are both Insatiate and nuanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see the reasonable nature of this aspect of the complaint. I can't think of a single CofD core book that doesn't have an antagonist in the antagonist section that couldn't use a lot of expansion, but clearly was cut to the minimum of what the ST is going to need to use them for their primary purpose in the core game. This only really works if you agree with the reading of the text as saying, &quot;these don't exist,&quot; instead of saying, &quot;these exist but aren't the focus so we're not getting into them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor I, but I usually don't take issue with them because they don't tell me the more complex characters were left out because they aren't likely to come up in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a certain point in all this, I think we need to start seeing actual citations. Dancing around vague issues with unspecified statements can only get us so far as a discussion. I can't try to explain why I see a different spin on something if I don't know exactly which wordings are bugging you when you read them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually gave direct quotes in the previous post, and again in this one. Here's the section in full context:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Some alchemists walk the line between obsession and madness.</b> Although sufficiently frustrated with the limitations of the human condition that they seek to push those boundaries, <b>they don\u2019t hate their humanity enough to try to abandon it altogether</b>.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Sane, rational, and cautious alchemists are unlikely to come into a Promethean story</b>, however. Because <b>they are more interested in knowledge than power</b>, they are generally content with lesser alchemical workings and don\u2019t have the same hunger for Pyros and Vitriol as the mad alchemists described here. <b>Without the self-hating obsession of those who despise their own humanity, they are not driven to commit atrocities against the Created. </b></i><br /> <br /> <i>Most importantly, <b>sane alchemists just know better.</b> Chasing Prometheans is a good way to end up insane, maimed, or dead. These <b>cautious alchemists rarely enter into the lives of Prometheans</b>, and when they do, it\u2019s usually because the Prometheans sought them out, hoping for guidance. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Alchemists who avoid Prometheans sometimes call those who hunt them down for their humors \u201cthe Insatiate,\u201d referring to their endless hunger for Pyros. Alchemists who hunt the Created simply call more cautious alchemists fools or weaklings, when they bother to refer to them at all.</i><br /> <br /> Bolded the most relevant bits for emphasis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though the specific, &quot;Where are the people who do take Vitriol but have managed to stave off becoming addicted,&quot; might not exist on purpose. Vitriol isn't a chemical drug. It's distilled divine power. Being able to &quot;dabble&quot; in Vitriol is very likely not something that's going to be included because it's too mind-warping for the human mind to handle without being permanently affected by it. Which also explains why the Insatiate descriptions are heavily weighted towards the one style you want to see more contrasts to; it's not something you can &quot;safely&quot; take one hit of and decide to never do again, or say &quot;just one more,&quot; without being delusional about the amount of control it has on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-16-2016, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:39:39-07:00","id":952218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there's my point. &quot;..it seems to me...&quot; but why does it seem that way to you? I'm reading the same text, and I'm not getting that intent. So the reasonable assumption is that we're bringing different' biases/preconceptions to the text that need to be separated from the text, rather than just insisting that &quot;...it seems to me...&quot; be sufficient without challenge or analysis of how much weight that feeling should be given.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> At a certain point in all this, I think we need to start seeing actual citations. Dancing around vague issues with unspecified statements can only get us so far as a discussion. I can't try to explain why I see a different spin on something if I don't know exactly which wordings are bugging you when you read them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, how heavy is the burden of proof here? A piece of writing is an inherently subjective experience. Does this fact mean you can dismiss negative reactions on the basis of those reactions being determined in some way by the nature of the reader? I don't really think so. We can't really have a constructive discussion if some &quot;burden of proof&quot; is required, because the closest thing to it has already been offered.<br /> <br /> Then you take Charlaquin to task for relying on their feelings and ask for actual citations, but multiple quotes and passages have been provided over the course of this thread that have been cited as the reason for these feelings.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> -The biggest offender that has been cited here is the sidebar &quot;The Great Work&quot; on page 257. We see the sharp divide between sane and insane alchemists. Those who don't hunt Prometheans are described as &quot;knowing better&quot;. There's not a lot of wiggle room left for a spectrum of Alchemists with a variety of reasons for doing what they do. You hunt a Promethean? You're insane, insatiate, a &quot;black alchemist&quot;.<br /> -On the same page, the &quot;Playing God&quot; section talks of &quot;Alchemists are ambitious by nature&quot; and implicitly assumes that only those who hate their human limitations would be driven to the darker side of alchemy.<br /> -The examples given of an Alchemist who might not want to kill a Promethean straight away are of Alchemists who are just playing the Prometheans until they get an opportunity to kill them (page 261). Also note the reoccurring language. &quot;Black alchemists are obsessives, addicts, users, and abusers&quot;.<br /> <br /> These sections all give the impression that there is only one type of antagonistic Alchemist, when the reality is that the spectrum of human behaviour and possible justifications for reprehensible acts are so broad that you don't need to think long to come up with more interesting takes on Alchemists than what the book is pushing. The abolutist language used doesn't help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a supplement with the space to get into all this detail? I mean, lets say each of those gets ~3 pages of material between general discussion and example characters. That's 9 pages worth of material (and I'd say you'd have to a very good writer to hit every note you really should to thoroughly explore those in just that much space). Where is that coming out of the core book?<br /> <br /> The text is clear Alchemists are truncated in presentation to focus on their primary function in the game (the Insatiate antagonists harvesting you for Vitriol), and Matt's made it clear that he's up for expanding on Alchemists in future supplements...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I would argue that you could make Alchemists more nuanced by <i>removing</i> word count. You need a simple sentence saying &quot;Alchemists hunt Prometheans for a variety of reasons, ranging from the need to help a loved one or escape a physical ailment to a burning desire for power&quot;. You can then remove a lot of the text used that actively <i>shuts down</i> these interpretations, most notably the example sections I listed above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952177#post952177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see the reasonable nature of this aspect of the complaint. I can't think of a single CofD core book that doesn't have an antagonist in the antagonist section that couldn't use a lot of expansion, but clearly was cut to the minimum of what the ST is going to need to use them for their primary purpose in the core game. This only really works if you agree with the reading of the text as saying, &quot;these don't exist,&quot; instead of saying, &quot;these exist but aren't the focus so we're not getting into them.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Though the specific, &quot;Where are the people who do take Vitriol but have managed to stave off becoming addicted,&quot; might not exist on purpose. Vitriol isn't a chemical drug. It's distilled divine power. Being able to &quot;dabble&quot; in Vitriol is very likely not something that's going to be included because it's too mind-warping for the human mind to handle without being permanently affected by it. Which also explains why the Insatiate descriptions are heavily weighted towards the one style you want to see more contrasts to; it's not something you can &quot;safely&quot; take one hit of and decide to never do again, or say &quot;just one more,&quot; without being delusional about the amount of control it has on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a nutshell, the objection is not that the Alchemist section is too short, that they're not playable, or even that they could be expanded upon to be more interesting. The problem is that some of the limited word count available was used to describe Alchemists in a way that feels that it explicitly limits possible options, curtails alternate interpretations, and means a Storyteller actually has fewer possibilities to play with than if they were working from a similar chapter with reduced word count that didn't feel like there was only one possible type of antagonistic Alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:34:53-07:00","id":952253,"title":"","content":"Second edition was years in the making, suffered the driest spells of any of the forums, deeply beloved by a few, and the hot topic still a week after the release is that the book isn't fair to bit players meant as antagonists. There are more posts in this thread than there are threads in this sub-forum, over an omission we were told about, what, a year ago? All this time and energy could have been spent drafting homebrew rules for alchemy instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:40:19-07:00","id":952255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952253#post952253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second edition was years in the making, suffered the driest spells of any of the forums, deeply beloved by a few, and the hot topic still a week after the release is that the book isn't fair to bit players meant as antagonists. There are more posts in this thread than there are threads in this sub-forum, over an omission we were told about, what, a year ago? All this time and energy could have been spent drafting homebrew rules for alchemy instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* not much to say about the parts I like. I like them.<br /> <br /> For the record though, the omission of playable alchemists? The part that we were told about a year ago? I was braced for that. In fact, I was pleasantly surprised by how close to playable alchemists are as-written. That has nothing to do with my critique of the section, and this thread would be a <i>lot</i> shorter if I and those who share my opinion didn't have to re-explain that every fifth post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:48:28-07:00","id":952259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952253#post952253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second edition was years in the making, suffered the driest spells of any of the forums, deeply beloved by a few, and the hot topic still a week after the release is that the book isn't fair to bit players meant as antagonists. There are more posts in this thread than there are threads in this sub-forum, over an omission we were told about, what, a year ago? All this time and energy could have been spent drafting homebrew rules for alchemy instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't have a problem with any of the rules of Alchemists. I don't intend to offer playable Alchemists to my players. I intend them to be solely the province of NPCs. And their mechanics are fine. I'd go so far as to say great in places.<br /> <br /> It's just their treatment in the text of the chapter that is disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:54:12-07:00","id":952260,"title":"","content":"I'm not calling you or anyone out in particular, just lamenting that in the wake of a revitalizing effort, the biggest, topmost discussion is an argument about a sideshow. I feel like we need more outreach, not another divisive topic akin to transhumanism to greet the curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:01:48-07:00","id":952262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952203#post952203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when I see a sidebar using wordcount to talk about why they didn't use wordcount to talk about alchemists that aren't antagonistic towards Prometheans, I find it a little silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>While valid, this doesn't really seem to be a driving part of any of this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then when it goes on to describe the differences between the alchemists it does deem worthy of spending wordcount on and the ones it doesn't, and in doing so paints the group it doesn't talk about as reasonable people and the group it doesn't talk about as unsympathetic monsters, it strikes me as setting up a dichotomy between &quot;good alchemists&quot; and &quot;bad alchemists&quot; instead of leaving room for nuance and interpretation. </div> </div> </div>Except, in the quote you cite fully later, it never says calls them unsympathetic monsters. It applies a lot of negative terminology to them, but I don't see where they go from &quot;bad guys,&quot; to, &quot;unsympathetic bad guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hating the human condition? That's sympathetic. Misanthropy is a long standing position of people that have become disillusioned with our supposed virtues in the face of all of our faults. It's not nice to transhumanism as a philosophy (but as long since covered an inherently humanist biased game is going to be harsh to transhumanism), but the core of transhumanism is the idea that we should be moving towards something better than our current state. While lots of people have positive motivations for following that philosophy, there's plenty of sympathetic reasons to as well. Things the book talks about, like fear and desperation.<br /> <br /> The desire for power? Again... this is a very sympathetic motivation. Think about all the talk of, &quot;I want to cure my child with cancer!&quot; that's not a pursuit of knowledge, that's a pursuit of power. That's not someone trying to learn how to cure cancer for everyone by understanding cancer and alchemy in order to find a functional cure. That's someone that's desperate for power they don't have, and is pursuing it to achieve a goal.<br /> <br /> This is where you lose me in this. It seems to be either taking negativity towards the Insatiate as meaning &quot;don't treat their motivations as sympathetic,&quot; which I don't see a reason to read into the text, or just not personally finding those things sympathetic regardless if they should be considered such in the abstract.<br /> <br /> Sorry if getting personal here isn't productive:<br /> <br /> I completely get the Insatiate. I'm stuck with a diagnosis that medical science throws its hands in the air and says, &quot;well, we tried a couple different pills, and those didn't work, so... you're just going to have to learn to cope with it. Have some happy pills to get by.&quot; It's not rational - and I say this in a clincal sense - but I would absolutely harm another living human being if someone managed to dupe me into believing it would relieve my symptoms, and I have to live with knowing that. I know that's irrational, that harming others can't possibly make me feel better, but I also know how much I want to not have to deal with this, and how it gnaws at me all the time until what's cautious, sane, or rational, behavior stops making sense to me. On bad days, I stop caring. Life time in jail is not rationally better than what I deal with, but those days I'd believe it would be worth it anyway.<br /> <br /> So yeah, just saying they're people that will do some extremely harmful shit to escape what they perceive as extremely shitty lives even if they really aren't that bad? That's sympathetic to me. Because if I believed doing that stuff would actually make this go away... that would be me. <br /> <br /> So yeah, in identifying my biases, there's a big one right there. The line between me and an Insatiate Alchemist is that Insatiate Alchemists are fictional. You point a descriptions of people and view them as unsympathetic monsters. I see the same descriptions and see, &quot;Oh hey, it's me off my meds after a major life trauma taken to it's most horrific extreme.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I come up with a concept for an Alchemist who has reason to seek Vitriol, is willing to kill Prometheans to get it, but is not a power-hungry misanthrope, I don't need three pages dedicated to telling me how to do that. But then the &quot;The Great Work&quot; sidebar lumps him in with the Alchemists who are unlikely to come into a Promethean story. </div> </div> </div>Or the text is trying to call into question about how much that character isn't seeking power and abandoning the human condition. I mean, in all of this thread, I haven't really seen examples of Alchemists that would go after Vitriol - and all that entails - where their attachment to humanity, and their motivations being altruistic over power driven is something to be taken as a certainty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wish it was done in a way that didn't close the door on Alchemists who are both Insatiate and nuanced. </div> </div> </div>Even with the quote, I'm not seeing the &quot;closed door,&quot; aspect of it. Esp. with the &quot;treat absolutes as 'usually'&quot; caveat of the book. I guess I'm not getting the connection between &quot;why&quot; and &quot;now I can't play around with different approaches.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can appreciate it. I've certainly felt that way before, but with things like the WoD metaplot where things are so over-explained and the setting is so full, I felt constrained by it all when it came to doing the stories I wanted to do. <br /> <br /> So, we have the quote there. How about a thorough example of how an idea you'd like to bring in, is being fought by that quote; though I'd request that the &quot;usually caveat&quot; be applied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor I, but I usually don't take issue with them because they don't tell me the more complex characters were left out because they aren't likely to come up in the game. </div> </div> </div>I honestly find this to be a putting the writers in a bit of a Catch-22. Antagonists with no hint of being more complex are often received negatively unless it's well setup that this is explicitly supposed to be the case (like say, zombies), and then people get the expansion book and fall in love with the antagonists because they feel &quot;real&quot; and &quot;flushed out&quot; instead of flat stereotypes from the core book. But... if you hint at there being more to them that will be expanded on later... now it's a problem because the author being transparent about where their focusing things is also a problem.<br /> <br /> What's the 3rd option that doesn't present &quot;boring&quot; antagonist that's just a stereotype with no indication of more to the group, and being transparent that the group is more complex but not the core focus of the game so not in the core book?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952218#post952218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, how heavy is the burden of proof here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really about a burden of proof. It's about trying to separate out what we're bring to the text, versus what the text is without those preconceptions. And please, I was careful to state this as something that goes both ways, not me just &quot;going to task&quot; on Char.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...implicitly assumes... </div> </div> </div>This is part of my issue. When you acknowledge that you're reading into implicit assumptions, you're acknowledging you're not talking about what's explicitly stated, but an interpretation you're opting to make. This is the kind of thing I want to isolate and discuss to suss out what's really the text, and what's just subjectivity at work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These sections all give the impression that there is only one type of antagonistic Alchemist, when the reality is that the spectrum of human behaviour and possible justifications for reprehensible acts are so broad that you don't need to think long to come up with more interesting takes on Alchemists than what the book is pushing. </div> </div> </div>Well... there is only one &quot;kind&quot; of common antagonistic Alchemist. They're just a lot more varied than I think they're being credited as being. Things like, &quot;mad,&quot; &quot;obsessive,&quot; &quot;ambitions,&quot; &quot;insane,&quot; &quot;power seeking,&quot; and so on, can express themselves in nearly countless ways. So &quot;one kind,&quot; doesn't translate into a lack of spectrum of characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The abolutist language used doesn't help. </div> </div> </div>Probably. But again, the text as a &quot;usually caveat&quot; that the text should be read with respect towards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly? I would argue that you could make Alchemists more nuanced by <i>removing</i> word count. You need a simple sentence saying &quot;Alchemists hunt Prometheans for a variety of reasons, ranging from the need to help a loved one or escape a physical ailment to a burning desire for power&quot;. You can then remove a lot of the text used that actively <i>shuts down</i> these interpretations, most notably the example sections I listed above. </div> </div> </div>But that's not why Alchemists hunt Prometheans. As I already covered, Prometheans are a source of materials. That's it. What the Alchemists do with Vitriol has a large variety of reasons, which is separate from the quotes you're focusing on for the most part. It feel like this is a regular sticking point. The text shuts down getting Vitriol outside of torturing a Promethean to death, which feels like it's getting conflated with saying there's only one reason to want Vitriol... which isn't present in what's getting cited.<br /> <br /> Where does the text actually say that, &quot;I want Vitriol to cure my kid's cancer,&quot; &quot;I want Vitriol to live for ever,&quot; and &quot;I want Vitriol to transcend the limitations of my human mind,&quot; aren't all different and valid reasons for an Alchemist to go down the Insatiate path?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that some of the limited word count available was used to describe Alchemists in a way that feels that it explicitly limits possible options, curtails alternate interpretations, and means a Storyteller actually has fewer possibilities to play with than if they were working from a similar chapter with reduced word count that didn't feel like there was only one possible type of antagonistic Alchemist. </div> </div> </div>And as someone that doesn't get that from reading the text, I'm trying to suss out where that disconnect is occurring, and why.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:04:57-07:00","id":952266,"title":"","content":"It is worth noting that this is the time period for last minute changes to 2e. So it is actually the right time for any nitpicking over a &quot;sideshow&quot; if that's the worst thing we found to nitpick in the book. There's time for Matt to be reading this, and decide to adjust the wording a bit before the book is finalized. Sure, some more positive stuff would be good for the forums as well, but this is appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:33:04-07:00","id":952281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is part of my issue. When you acknowledge that you're reading into implicit assumptions, you're acknowledging you're not talking about what's explicitly stated, but an interpretation you're opting to make. This is the kind of thing I want to isolate and discuss to suss out what's really the text, and what's just subjectivity at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be hesitant to call this kind of reading &quot;subjective&quot;. It's correct, because I make no claim to my own objectivity, but the term is used in arguments like this in a way that seems to ignore the innate subjectivity of the written word. All language is metaphor.<br /> <br /> Now, as to how I got to this reading, the text is quite clear that there are two types of Alchemist, and that the division between them is sharp. It goes so far as to split the Alchemist population down the middle and assign one half its own label. These two groups are defined against one another. One group are explicitly called out as greedy, ambitious, mad, and hunt and kill Prometheans. The other group is sane, seeks knowledge, &quot;knows better&quot; than their insatiate brethren.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... there is only one &quot;kind&quot; of common antagonistic Alchemist. They're just a lot more varied than I think they're being credited as being. Things like, &quot;mad,&quot; &quot;obsessive,&quot; &quot;ambitions,&quot; &quot;insane,&quot; &quot;power seeking,&quot; and so on, can express themselves in nearly countless ways. So &quot;one kind,&quot; doesn't translate into a lack of spectrum of characters.<br /> <br /> But that's not why Alchemists hunt Prometheans. As I already covered, Prometheans are a source of materials. That's it. What the Alchemists do with Vitriol has a large variety of reasons, which is separate from the quotes you're focusing on for the most part. It feel like this is a regular sticking point. The text shuts down getting Vitriol outside of torturing a Promethean to death, which feels like it's getting conflated with saying there's only one reason to want Vitriol... which isn't present in what's getting cited.<br /> <br /> Where does the text actually say that, &quot;I want Vitriol to cure my kid's cancer,&quot; &quot;I want Vitriol to live for ever,&quot; and &quot;I want Vitriol to transcend the limitations of my human mind,&quot; aren't all different and valid reasons for an Alchemist to go down the Insatiate path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think this is where your own subjectivity is playing a part. I don't understand the distinction you're drawing between an Alchemist's desire for Vitriol and an Alchemist's desire to hunt Prometheans. You are describing a very specific attitude on the Alchemist's part, one wherein they see Prometheans as a resource to be mined. I don't think there's enough infrastructure in place for an individual to easily create that divide in their mind. If Vitriol could be bought at a supermarket then I could understand that mentality. When I want to buy a steak that doesn't mean I want to go out and slaughter a cow. But when you're as close to the source as an Alchemist almost necessarily is, those lines blur. The act of hunting is the task that gets you what you want. As you say, there's no alternative. The text assumes that you have to be insane to undertake that task, but for an end this valuable you could justify the means in so many ways. And to an extent I disagree that we're conflating the one mean of getting Vitriol with the one reason to want Vitriol. The presentation of those Alchemists willing to obtain it <br /> <br /> Now, I'll concede that there's variation in the expression of &quot;mad&quot;, &quot;obsessive&quot;, and &quot;ambitious&quot;. But that's almost beside the point. The use of those adjectives restrict us from a wider pool to a smaller pool. Whether that pool is wide from an objective standpoint is besides the point. There is potential for violent, antagonistic Alchemists that fall outside rather mundane frame presented by the text. A far more interesting, relatable kind of antagonistic than whatever spin on the madman offered by the book.<br /> <br /> In real life humans kill for stupid, ridiculous reasons. Some of us maim and harm those closest to us for reasons that might be abhorrent, but don't necessitate that the perpetrator be insane. The book doesn't seem to understand that. It presents us with non-human protagonists who are hated by the world to begin with and seems to think only the insane would try to kill them for the vast reward they promise. It's almost cute, now that I think about it, adorably naive to the world at large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as someone that doesn't get that from reading the text, I'm trying to suss out where that disconnect is occurring, and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno man. We've provided quotes. I don't feel like I'm reading particularly deeply to get the interpretation I'm getting. Can you show quotes where you think the text expressly refutes our points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:58:40-07:00","id":952301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While valid, this doesn't really seem to be a driving part of any of this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I haven't really brought it up because it's a minor nitpick, and I respect what the sidebar is trying to do, even if I don't care for the way it does it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, in the quote you cite fully later, it never says calls them unsympathetic monsters. It applies a lot of negative terminology to them, but I don't see where they go from &quot;bad guys,&quot; to, &quot;unsympathetic bad guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hating the human condition? That's sympathetic. Misanthropy is a long standing position of people that have become disillusioned with our supposed virtues in the face of all of our faults. It's not nice to transhumanism as a philosophy (but as long since covered an inherently humanist biased game is going to be harsh to transhumanism), but the core of transhumanism is the idea that we should be moving towards something better than our current state. While lots of people have positive motivations for following that philosophy, there's plenty of sympathetic reasons to as well. Things the book talks about, like fear and desperation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hating humanity and/or the human condition is not something that I sympathize with. I guess some people do, but as you observe, the game doesn't present that perspective in a positive light. If humanity as a desirable state is part of the buy-in for Promethean, then not sympathizing with those who hate their humanity and want to throw it away is also part of the buy-in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The desire for power? Again... this is a very sympathetic motivation. Think about all the talk of, &quot;I want to cure my child with cancer!&quot; that's not a pursuit of knowledge, that's a pursuit of power. That's not someone trying to learn how to cure cancer for everyone by understanding cancer and alchemy in order to find a functional cure. That's someone that's desperate for power they don't have, and is pursuing it to achieve a goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really call that desire for knowledge or for power. More like a desire for safety, security for their child.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where you lose me in this. It seems to be either taking negativity towards the Insatiate as meaning &quot;don't treat their motivations as sympathetic,&quot; which I don't see a reason to read into the text, or just not personally finding those things sympathetic regardless if they should be considered such in the abstract.<br /> <br /> Sorry if getting personal here isn't productive:<br /> <br /> I completely get the Insatiate. I'm stuck with a diagnosis that medical science throws its hands in the air and says, &quot;well, we tried a couple different pills, and those didn't work, so... you're just going to have to learn to cope with it. Have some happy pills to get by.&quot; It's not rational - and I say this in a clincal sense - but I would absolutely harm another living human being if someone managed to dupe me into believing it would relieve my symptoms, and I have to live with knowing that. I know that's irrational, that harming others can't possibly make me feel better, but I also know how much I want to not have to deal with this, and how it gnaws at me all the time until what's cautious, sane, or rational, behavior stops making sense to me. On bad days, I stop caring. Life time in jail is not rationally better than what I deal with, but those days I'd believe it would be worth it anyway.<br /> <br /> So yeah, just saying they're people that will do some extremely harmful shit to escape what they perceive as extremely shitty lives even if they really aren't that bad? That's sympathetic to me. Because if I believed doing that stuff would actually make this go away... that would be me.<br /> <br /> So yeah, in identifying my biases, there's a big one right there. The line between me and an Insatiate Alchemist is that Insatiate Alchemists are fictional. You point a descriptions of people and view them as unsympathetic monsters. I see the same descriptions and see, &quot;Oh hey, it's me off my meds after a major life trauma taken to it's most horrific extreme.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the desire to cure one's self of disease as a motivation that the sidebar allows for. Or at least, not without also having a hatred of humanity, desire for power, and lack of knowing better than to go after Prometheans for Vitriol.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the text is trying to call into question about how much that character isn't seeking power and abandoning the human condition. I mean, in all of this thread, I haven't really seen examples of Alchemists that would go after Vitriol - and all that entails - where their attachment to humanity, and their motivations being altruistic over power driven is something to be taken as a certainty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that could be what it's trying to do? If so, it doesn't get that point across to me as-written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with the quote, I'm not seeing the &quot;closed door,&quot; aspect of it. Esp. with the &quot;treat absolutes as 'usually'&quot; caveat of the book. I guess I'm not getting the connection between &quot;why&quot; and &quot;now I can't play around with different approaches.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can appreciate it. I've certainly felt that way before, but with things like the WoD metaplot where things are so over-explained and the setting is so full, I felt constrained by it all when it came to doing the stories I wanted to do.<br /> <br /> So, we have the quote there. How about a thorough example of how an idea you'd like to bring in, is being fought by that quote; though I'd request that the &quot;usually caveat&quot; be applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's actually the intent behind the &quot;treat absolutes as 'usually'&quot; caveat. The quote in question says:<br /> <br /> <i>When reading this book, any time you see a declarative statement about the Created, please mentally append \u201cusually\u201d to the statement. Prometheans cannot sire or bear children\u2026 usually. Prometheans cause Disquiet in human beings\u2026usually. Prometheans become human at the end of the Pilgrimage\u2026usually. <b>Promethean </b>relies on strange, unique circumstances and once-in-a-billion occurrences, though, so if something happens in your chronicles that breaks the rules, that\u2019s entirely in keeping with the game\u2019s intent. </i><br /> <br /> This passage, to me, seems to be talking about the fact that nothing is certain when it comes to Prometheans, because Prometheans are creatures that inherently resist being pinned down by absolutes. It's not an excuse for the writing being constraining because you were supposed to assume all the &quot;usuallys&quot;, especially when the subject matter isn't Prometheans.<br /> <br /> But, to give a specific example of what I'm talking about, just look at Karen Degalle. She's explicitly motivated by fear, although she pretends it's ambition. She doesn't seem, by my reading, to hate her humanity, or to desire power, or to be consumed by self-hating obsession. It would seem, based on my reading of the The Great Work sidebar, that she would be unlikely to come into a Promethean story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952262#post952262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly find this to be a putting the writers in a bit of a Catch-22. Antagonists with no hint of being more complex are often received negatively unless it's well setup that this is explicitly supposed to be the case (like say, zombies), and then people get the expansion book and fall in love with the antagonists because they feel &quot;real&quot; and &quot;flushed out&quot; instead of flat stereotypes from the core book. But... if you hint at there being more to them that will be expanded on later... now it's a problem because the author being transparent about where their focusing things is also a problem.<br /> <br /> What's the 3rd option that doesn't present &quot;boring&quot; antagonist that's just a stereotype with no indication of more to the group, and being transparent that the group is more complex but not the core focus of the game so not in the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 3rd option is to have that sidebar focus on the Alchemist's actions, not their motivations. Go ahead and say that alchemists who aren't addicted to Vitriol aren't covered here because they aren't likely to come into a Promethean story, and leave me to decide for myself why the Alchemists I include in my games are addicted to Vitriol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-17-2016, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:24:15-07:00","id":952316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952161#post952161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about Demon or Mummy? Those also work excellently with small and/or sporadic groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b1. Don't have either.<br /> 2. I'm not fond of what I've seen of either.<br /> 3. Of the 5 of us, the married couple are the ones who almost never show up, and the other player who shows up most of the time refuses to have anything to do with any form of demon.<br /> That leaves me and the ST.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:27:30-07:00","id":952317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952281#post952281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be hesitant to call this kind of reading &quot;subjective&quot;. It's correct, because I make no claim to my own objectivity, but the term is used in arguments like this in a way that seems to ignore the innate subjectivity of the written word. All language is metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry... but it's really hard to take this as anything other than, &quot;subjectivity matters when it helps me, and doesn't when it doesn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because that's sort of how you're using it. You say subjective and backs you up, I say it... and it's just me ignoring stuff. It's really hard to give this a charitable reading of good faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One group are explicitly called out as greedy, ambitious, mad, and hunt and kill Prometheans. The other group is sane, seeks knowledge, &quot;knows better&quot; than their insatiate brethren. </div> </div> </div>Technically, all Alchemists are called out as ambitious, and nothing says non-Insatiate Alchemists are good people that lack attributes as greed. They just recognize that chasing Vitriol isn't a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand the distinction you're drawing between an Alchemist's desire for Vitriol and an Alchemist's desire to hunt Prometheans. </div> </div> </div>Insatiate Alchemists desire is for Vitriol. If they could get it from an easier source than hunting Prometheans, they most likely would. Some Alchemists might get a kick out of hunting Prometheans as well, but the ultimate defining motivation is obtaining Vitriol, not killing Prometheans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are describing a very specific attitude on the Alchemist's part, one wherein they see Prometheans as a resource to be mined. </div> </div> </div>No.. I'm describing an objective fact of the setting laid out in the text. Alchemists need Vitriol to do things they can't do with just their access to Pyros. The only source of Vitriol is harvesting it from Prometheans. That's how the game is set up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think there's enough infrastructure in place for an individual to easily create that divide in their mind. </div> </div> </div>There's enough for Alchemists to learn their art, which implies there's enough for this distinction to be understood in-character. Just hunting a Promethean doesn't get you Vitriol. You have to actively take it from them by force. There's nothing that stops an Alchemist from stealing a captured Promethean from a rival Alchemist to take it's Vitriol first, and thus avoiding the need to hunt (paranoia about this is indicated as one of the reasons Alchemists have trouble forming groups to pursue their goals).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I'll concede that there's variation in the expression of &quot;mad&quot;, &quot;obsessive&quot;, and &quot;ambitious&quot;. But that's almost beside the point. The use of those adjectives restrict us from a wider pool to a smaller pool. Whether that pool is wide from an objective standpoint is besides the point. There is potential for violent, antagonistic Alchemists that fall outside rather mundane frame presented by the text. A far more interesting, relatable kind of antagonistic than whatever spin on the madman offered by the book. </div> </div> </div>This is kind of... nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Which is it? Do things things not matter, or are they restrictive? It seems like you're trying to say both at the same time those are mutually exclusive positions.<br /> <br /> I really can't agree with this. If something restricts you from 2 million options to 1 million options, is the 50% decrease in options even significant when you're probably never going to explore more than 1% of them? Yeah, the objective size of the pool matters if one of the core elements of the complaints about the text is that it's restricting the pool to an overly restrictive point.<br /> <br /> And, again, what can't you make? Not vague terms. Give me an example of something that the text outright restricts in its language about the Insatiate (and not restricts from other things, like you can't make an Alchemist that doesn't torture Prometheans to get Vitriol, that's not the language about the Insaiate, that's the rules of how Alchemy works).<br /> <br /> There's been a heck of a lot of repetition of the them of, &quot;the text restricts me from using Alchemists in X fashion,&quot; which exceedingly little specifics to demonstrate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In real life humans kill for stupid, ridiculous reasons. Some of us maim and harm those closest to us for reasons that might be abhorrent, but don't necessitate that the perpetrator be insane. </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly big false equivalence to this. Human on human violence is unfortunately common, and comes in a spectrum of reasons. But that doesn't compare to hunting people to kill them for ingredients in magical potions. Even if someone doing that is not technically insane, most people would be fine with calling them that in a no technical sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It presents us with non-human protagonists who are hated by the world to begin with and seems to think only the insane would try to kill them for the vast reward they promise. </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't? That's the Insatiate Alchemist thing. Hunters, which are referenced in the Alchemist section no less, can and do hunt Prometheans without the madness that comes with being touched by the Divine Flame (something that's skipped in your analysis here, is that one of the reasons they're &quot;mad&quot; is the mind altering magical stuff they're messing with).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you show quotes where you think the text expressly refutes our points? </div> </div> </div>You're asking me to quote the text saying something, when my position is it when I read it, I don't get what you're reading. What can I quote to show that what you cite as restrictive communicates nothing especially restrictive to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:04:11-07:00","id":952335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952301#post952301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hating humanity and/or the human condition is not something that I sympathize with. I guess some people do, but as you observe, the game doesn't present that perspective in a positive light. If humanity as a desirable state is part of the buy-in for Promethean, then not sympathizing with those who hate their humanity and want to throw it away is also part of the buy-in.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a massive equivocation. When people talk about sympathetic characters, they usually don't mean, &quot;people I like and want to be like,&quot; they mean, &quot;people I can understand the motivations of.&quot; Sympathetic antagonists don't have to be likeable, and the text doesn't have to paint them as even having a good point, the audience just needs to be able to appreciate that despite being the antagonist you can feel how they got to be who they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't really call that desire for knowledge or for power. More like a desire for safety, security for their child. </div> </div> </div>But providing that requires power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see the desire to cure one's self of disease as a motivation that the sidebar allows for. Or at least, not without also having a hatred of humanity, desire for power, and lack of knowing better than to go after Prometheans for Vitriol. </div> </div> </div>A drive to cure yourself of a disease taken to the point of being willing hunt, torture, and kill a living feeling communicative being. That's kind of lost here. If you're willing to do all that, how are you not already at the point of being willing to throw away your humanity in the process of a cure? Even if it isn't &quot;hate&quot; it's at least indifference to maintaining a semblance of humane behavior just to live longer. It's also a desire for power in the form of control over your body to assuage the fear and desperation of your disease. As for lack of knowing better... well... people do really dangerous things without hunting Prometheans in the real world when medicine fails them and their body's imminent failure is shoved in their face. I have seen people poison themselves slowly to &quot;cure&quot; cancer because that's &quot;how chemo works,&quot; without knowing better than to use drugs that can't kill cancer without killing everything else too. And they got idea from a website that advocated taking baths in the same chemicals. So yeah, people will absolutely do things with the &quot;lack of knowing better,&quot; when desperate in the face of a terminal disease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, it doesn't get that point across to me as-written. </div> </div> </div>I think if that's the intent, it should be stated more directly. However it makes more sense to me as how to interpret the text than reading it as intending to be the restrictive wall you are describing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that's actually the intent behind the &quot;treat absolutes as 'usually'&quot; caveat. </div> </div> </div>I don't think the fact that the caveat is specifically applied to Prometheans is meant to mean it doesn't apply to Promethean specific antagonists. And even then, it seems far more reasonable to treat it as broadly as possible rather than ignore it for one of the antagonists.<br /> <br /> If nothing is certain about the Created, what is certain about anything else touched by the Divine Flame?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, to give a specific example of what I'm talking about, just look at Karen Degalle. She's explicitly motivated by fear, although she pretends it's ambition. She doesn't seem, by my reading, to hate her humanity, or to desire power, or to be consumed by self-hating obsession. It would seem, based on reading The Great Work sidebar, that she would not be unlikely to come into a Promethean story. </div> </div> </div>I obviously disagree, which is why I'm looking for examples from you (and others) rather than the book.<br /> <br /> To me, Karen just frames that my interpretation of the sidebar should be preferred over the more restrictive one. That these words should be treated as vague and broad descriptors that can take multiple forms, not mandates from Matt on the One True Way of Insatiate Alchemists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 3rd option is to have that sidebar focus on the Alchemist's actions, not their motivations. Go ahead and say that alchemists who aren't addicted to Vitriol aren't covered here because they aren't likely to come into a Promethean story, and leave me to decide for myself why the Alchemists I include in my games are addicted to Vitriol. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the sidebar doesn't accomplish this. It doesn't say why Alchemists went down the rabbit hole into Insatiate status, it says what the process turns them into. The sidebar doesn't say, &quot;this is what Insatiate Alchemists were like before they got started,&quot; it says what they're like once they're set on the path far enough to earn the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:12:16-07:00","id":952339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry... but it's really hard to take this as anything other than, &quot;subjectivity matters when it helps me, and doesn't when it doesn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because that's sort of how you're using it. You say subjective and backs you up, I say it... and it's just me ignoring stuff. It's really hard to give this a charitable reading of good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I was trying to convey is that the &quot;subjective&quot; argument is ridiculous. It benefits no one. We can only discuss our various interpretations of the text, but when it gets brought up in these discussions it's almost invariably used as if it somehow undermines a given interpretation. I was just trying to get you to stop bringing it up. It's just words without meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insatiate Alchemists desire is for Vitriol. If they could get it from an easier source than hunting Prometheans, they most likely would. Some Alchemists might get a kick out of hunting Prometheans as well, but the ultimate defining motivation is obtaining Vitriol, not killing Prometheans.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I'm describing an objective fact of the setting laid out in the text. Alchemists need Vitriol to do things they can't do with just their access to Pyros. The only source of Vitriol is harvesting it from Prometheans. That's how the game is set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>...so? What's the point?<br /> <br /> I honestly don't care whether or not you see Promethean involvement to this whole thing as inconsequential or not. The objective is pretty much irrelevant. If the book said that the only Alchemists who picked flowers were the insane ones then that would have about as much bearing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much clearer I can get. My problem is <i>why</i> Alchemists do what they do. And to make it clear which &quot;why&quot; I'm concerned with, it is not &quot;Why do they hunt Prometheans? They hunt Prometheans so they can get Vitriol&quot;, it is, &quot;They they hunt Prometheans/Vitriol/whatever because they're bonkers&quot;. It's the character motivations, not the mechanics of what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kind of... nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Which is it? Do things things not matter, or are they restrictive? It seems like you're trying to say both at the same time those are mutually exclusive positions.<br /> <br /> I really can't agree with this. If something restricts you from 2 million options to 1 million options, is the 50% decrease in options even significant when you're probably never going to explore more than 1% of them? Yeah, the objective size of the pool matters if one of the core elements of the complaints about the text is that it's restricting the pool to an overly restrictive point.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> Alright. Clearly we need to go aaaaaaall the way down to basics.<br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I want to make an Alchemist NPC. The book is limited to only talking about Alchemists as antagonists. That's <i>fine</i>. I want an antagonist. But when I present this antagonist to my players, I may need to justify why they do what they do. In all honesty, I should probably do that anyway just so that their actions in game are internally consistent.<br /> <br /> At this point, Promethean tells me that my antagonists are insane. That they are doing something that no one could justify. That they are driven by greed and self-hatred and a poor grasp on reality.<br /> <br /> That's not &quot;1 million&quot; options. That is, in general narrative terms, one.<br /> <br /> Reverse the situation. Imagine Insatiate Alchemists were the playable characters and Prometheans NPCs. Imagine the text said that, as a player, you could only make an insane, power-hungry character. You understand how freaking limiting that is? Sure, you and your three friends might make four different insane characters, but that doesn't mean that you're not limited in archetype to the point of frustration.<br /> <br /> I like making NPCs. I don't like the idea of an entire class of NPCs confined to a single broad concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, what can't you make? Not vague terms. Give me an example of something that the text outright restricts in its language about the Insatiate (and not restricts from other things, like you can't make an Alchemist that doesn't torture Prometheans to get Vitriol, that's not the language about the Insaiate, that's the rules of how Alchemy works).<br /> <br /> There's been a heck of a lot of repetition of the them of, &quot;the text restricts me from using Alchemists in X fashion,&quot; which exceedingly little specifics to demonstrate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, we have given you quotes. We can ignore those quotes. I will ignore those quotes when I make Alchemists for the game. But don't you ignore the quotes and say they don't mean anything. Give me some specifics as to how those quotes aren't representative of the book's approach to Alchemists. We're at the point where you're the one making general claims without providing specifics. I've quoted phrases, sentences from the book to make my point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fairly big false equivalence to this. Human on human violence is unfortunately common, and comes in a spectrum of reasons. But that doesn't compare to hunting people to kill them for ingredients in magical potions. Even if someone doing that is not technically insane, most people would be fine with calling them that in a no technical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where I think you're blinded by what the text itself is telling you. The potions don't have to be <i>why</i> the Prometheans are being killed, that's just what the book says. The Prometheans could instead be being killed for perfectly human reasons. That full spectrum could be implied, not pushed to the background or ruled out.<br /> <br /> A human kills a human to save another's life. Because their ideology demands it. Because they wanted what the other had. Because they were desperate, it was their only chance of survival. Because they needed to right a wrong. The fact that killing a Promethean can give a human power should by rights make other justifications <i>more</i> likely, not less. It's so much easier to rationally justify violence when there's an incentive.<br /> <br /> When you add to all of the above the fact that Prometheans <i>aren't even human</i> it's actually kind of baffling how the writers got to the position that the Insatiate need to be insane in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it doesn't? That's the Insatiate Alchemist thing. Hunters, which are referenced in the Alchemist section no less, can and do hunt Prometheans without the madness that comes with being touched by the Divine Flame (something that's skipped in your analysis here, is that one of the reasons they're &quot;mad&quot; is the mind altering magical stuff they're messing with).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've addressed this point before. Suffice to say that I don't find an in-text justification for a problem with said text to be entirely satisfactory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952317#post952317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're asking me to quote the text saying something, when my position is it when I read it, I don't get what you're reading. What can I quote to show that what you cite as restrictive communicates nothing especially restrictive to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that states how an Alchemist can hunt a Promethean without being insane would be a start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:15:25-07:00","id":952368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952339#post952339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just trying to get you to stop bringing it up. It's just words without meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but no.<br /> <br /> I can't continue this at things stand. I am not going to take, &quot;I'm trying to get you to stop using a word you never used until I inserted into the conversation,&quot; as anything but a message you are not entering this in good faith. My ability to read this charitably is officially burnt up.<br /> <br /> 24 pages. You brought up the subjectivity of language. I never even used the word once in 24 fucking pages until you did, and I need to stop bringing it up? Yeah. Right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:50:52-07:00","id":952376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952368#post952368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry but no.<br /> <br /> I can't continue this at things stand. I am not going to take, &quot;I'm trying to get you to stop using a word you never used until I inserted into the conversation,&quot; as anything but a message you are not entering this in good faith. My ability to read this charitably is officially burnt up.<br /> <br /> 24 pages. You brought up the subjectivity of language. I never even used the word once in 24 fucking pages until you did, and I need to stop bringing it up? Yeah. Right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha. Did I? Oops. That's embarassing. Sorry dude, I'm so sick and tired (as in ill) that I'm honestly not surprised my fever-brain has me arguing against myself by the end of it. Cogent thoughts are hard to come by right now.<br /> <br /> Still, this has brightened up my day immeasurably, so I'll chalk that up as a win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T03:03:54-07:00","id":952407,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't blame Matt for having checked out of this thread a long time ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T04:00:42-07:00","id":952415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952407#post952407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't blame Matt for having checked out of this thread a long time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I look at it every couple of pages, but it's pretty much gone into the same pile as &quot;why doesn't PtC support my transhuman desires!&quot; <br /> <br /> Maybe my skin is made of paper or some shit and I can't take criticism, man, I dunno. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T04:45:14-07:00","id":952427,"title":"","content":"Just read the Charlaquin-Azahul-Heavy Arms conversation and you can safely ignore the rest (other than initial PenDragon talk until he checked out), as they laser focus the issue without being offensive, rude or judgemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:43:11-07:00","id":952508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952316#post952316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b1. Don't have either.<br /> 2. I'm not fond of what I've seen of either.<br /> 3. Of the 5 of us, the married couple are the ones who almost never show up, and the other player who shows up most of the time refuses to have anything to do with any form of demon.<br /> That leaves me and the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. You don't have Promethean either, from the sound of it earlier. What do you have to work with?<br /> 2. Oh? A pity - they're some of the CofD's best work.<br /> 3. That's tough. Is dramatic rebranding possible? &quot;Demons&quot; are rife throughout the CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:01:38-07:00","id":952581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952415#post952415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I look at it every couple of pages, but it's pretty much gone into the same pile as &quot;why doesn't PtC support my transhuman desires!&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe my skin is made of paper or some shit and I can't take criticism, man, I dunno. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I've largely been defending the text as is, I think the key thing you could benefit from in regards to what is feasible to change at this point in the process is a few wording issues in the Alchemist section, and perhaps the &quot;usually caveat&quot; to make it clear that it applies more universally to anything playing with the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> I think what would improve the section the most, would be to go into the Great Work side-bar, and make it a bit more clear that the madness of Insatiate Alchemists is more the product of going through with harvesting Vitriol, rather than the instigator of it. I think the most constructive points on improving the text center on the issue that in describing them in various negative terms, it comes off a bit like they had to start off the deep-end before they even got to hunting down a Promethean, instead of finally snapping being the end result of choosing that path instead of recognizing the multilayered risks it entails as being not worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:16:50-07:00","id":952630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a massive equivocation. When people talk about sympathetic characters, they usually don't mean, &amp;quot;people I like and want to be like,&amp;quot; they mean, &amp;quot;people I can understand the motivations of.&amp;quot; Sympathetic antagonists don't have to be likeable, and the text doesn't have to paint them as even having a good point, the audience just needs to be able to appreciate that despite being the antagonist you can feel how they got to be who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. Maybe &quot;sympathetic&quot; isn't really the best word for what I'm trying to describe. Or, rather, I desire a wider range of sympathetic motivations for Alchemists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But providing that requires power.<br /> <br /> A drive to cure yourself of a disease taken to the point of being willing hunt, torture, and kill a living feeling communicative being. That's kind of lost here. If you're willing to do all that, how are you not already at the point of being willing to throw away your humanity in the process of a cure? Even if it isn't &amp;quot;hate&amp;quot; it's at least indifference to maintaining a semblance of humane behavior just to live longer. It's also a desire for power in the form of control over your body to assuage the fear and desperation of your disease. As for lack of knowing better... well... people do really dangerous things without hunting Prometheans in the real world when medicine fails them and their body's imminent failure is shoved in their face. I have seen people poison themselves slowly to &amp;quot;cure&amp;quot; cancer because that's &amp;quot;how chemo works,&amp;quot; without knowing better than to use drugs that can't kill cancer without killing everything else too. And they got idea from a website that advocated taking baths in the same chemicals. So yeah, people will absolutely do things with the &amp;quot;lack of knowing better,&amp;quot; when desperate in the face of a terminal disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, some people will. Some people will also so dangerous things despite knowing better out of desperation. For some people the fear trumps the self-hate. It's not that I don't see the motivations presented in the sidebar as reasonable, it's that I don't want them to be the only motivations that the book grants it's blessing to as &quot;likely to come into a Promethean story&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if that's the intent, it should be stated more directly. However it makes more sense to me as how to interpret the text than reading it as intending to be the restrictive wall you are describing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the text is <i>intending</i> to be restrictive, I just think it <i>is</i> restrictive, possibly counter to intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the fact that the caveat is specifically applied to Prometheans is meant to mean it doesn't apply to Promethean specific antagonists. And even then, it seems far more reasonable to treat it as broadly as possible rather than ignore it for one of the antagonists.<br /> <br /> If nothing is certain about the Created, what is certain about anything else touched by the Divine Flame?</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* seems pretty clear to me that it's referring to Prometheans specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I obviously disagree, which is why I'm looking for examples from you (and others) rather than the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Let's say I've got an alchemist who is well aware of the dangers of hunting Prometheans for Vitriol. He knows it is not a safe or &quot;sane&quot; thing to do. For years he has been content to avoid Prometheans and perform his experiments using his own Pyros alone. Now, he's on the edge of a breakthrough that he thinks could benefit humanity as a whole - let's say, a cure for cancer. But, he has also been recently diagnosed with a terminal illness - let's say, ALS. He has tried to complete his work before his muscles reach the point where he won't be physically capable of continuing, but the disease is advancing more rapidly than his progress. At this point, he's beginning to realize that the only way he'll be able to complete his work is if he uses Vitriol to repair his deteriorating nerves. He has convinced himself that he would be justified in killing one Promethean for the sake of his research that could save countless humans, and has convinced himself that it will just be this once. Whether or not it will in fact just be this once remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, Karen just frames that my interpretation of the sidebar should be preferred over the more restrictive one. That these words should be treated as vague and broad descriptors that can take multiple forms, not mandates from Matt on the One True Way of Insatiate Alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas to me, Karren looks like an indication that there were conflicting desires at work that lead to the Alchemist section we have it now - a desire for Alchemists to be believable, sympathetic antagonists, and a desire to admonish Alchemists for being anti-humanist, and they lead to an inconsistent writeup overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952335#post952335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the sidebar doesn't accomplish this. It doesn't say why Alchemists went down the rabbit hole into Insatiate status, it says what the process turns them into. The sidebar doesn't say, &amp;quot;this is what Insatiate Alchemists were like before they got started,&amp;quot; it says what they're like once they're set on the path far enough to earn the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it says that Alchemists who aren't like that (usually) aren't likely to come into a Promethean story, which says to me that alchemists who are just starting down the rabbit hole are also (usually) not likely to come into a Promethean story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:24:27-07:00","id":952634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952581#post952581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I've largely been defending the text as is, I think the key thing you could benefit from in regards to what is feasible to change at this point in the process is a few wording issues in the Alchemist section, and perhaps the &amp;quot;usually caveat&amp;quot; to make it clear that it applies more universally to anything playing with the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> I think what would improve the section the most, would be to go into the Great Work side-bar, and make it a bit more clear that the madness of Insatiate Alchemists is more the product of going through with harvesting Vitriol, rather than the instigator of it. I think the most constructive points on improving the text center on the issue that in describing them in various negative terms, it comes off a bit like they had to start off the deep-end before they even got to hunting down a Promethean, instead of finally snapping being the end result of choosing that path instead of recognizing the multilayered risks it entails as being not worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The Great Work sidebar, and the examples of tragic alchemist who don't start out wanting to kill the throng in the Alchemists in their Prey section, which do seem to start out wanting to kill the throng and don't strike me as tragic are really the key points of my critique. They could both easily be adjusted with some minor rewording. I am otherwise quite happy with the way Alchemists turned out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:36:16-07:00","id":952790,"title":"","content":"Honestly if you want to play a transhumanist, play a Changeling with the right merit and your immortal and physically 18 years old forever by Wyrd 5, resistant to disease, toxins, but not so high wyrd that you end up with frailities. <br /> <br /> Then you can spend forever building up contracts, goblin vows, and other goodies.<br /> <br /> Promeathan isn't a good choice for transhumanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:42:56-07:00","id":952793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952634#post952634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. The Great Work sidebar, and the examples of tragic alchemist who don't start out wanting to kill the throng in the Alchemists in their Prey section, which do seem to start out wanting to kill the throng and don't strike me as tragic are really the key points of my critique. They could both easily be adjusted with some minor rewording. I am otherwise quite happy with the way Alchemists turned out.</div> </div> </div> </div>By and large where I'm coming from as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:46:08-07:00","id":952796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952790#post952790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly if you want to play a transhumanist, play a Changeling with the right merit and your immortal and physically 18 years old forever by Wyrd 5, resistant to disease, toxins, but not so high wyrd that you end up with frailities. <br /> <br /> Then you can spend forever building up contracts, goblin vows, and other goodies.<br /> <br /> Promeathan isn't a good choice for transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think most people in this thread care about playing transhumanist characters. I sure don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:56:36-07:00","id":952803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952790#post952790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly if you want to play a transhumanist, play a Changeling with the right merit and your immortal and physically 18 years old forever by Wyrd 5, resistant to disease, toxins, but not so high wyrd that you end up with frailities.<br /> <br /> Then you can spend forever building up contracts, goblin vows, and other goodies.<br /> <br /> Promeathan isn't a good choice for transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Charlaquin, I've got zero interest in playable Alchemists. I just think there are sections of the write-up that aren't written particularly well and almost seem like an attempt to curtail sympathetic antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:16:58-07:00","id":952861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952508#post952508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. You don't have Promethean either, from the sound of it earlier. What do you have to work with?<br /> 2. Oh? A pity - they're some of the CofD's best work.<br /> 3. That's tough. Is dramatic rebranding possible? &quot;Demons&quot; are rife throughout the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have the Core book for P:tC 1e.<br /> Rebranding might work, I'm not a fan of the whole &quot;Techgnostic&quot; angle, anyway. Ditch any trace of religious symbolism, and rebrand the whole thing as rogue Matrix programs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-17-2016, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:41:13-07:00","id":952881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952861#post952861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI have the Core book for P:tC 1e.<br /> Rebranding might work, I'm not a fan of the whole &amp;quot;Techgnostic&amp;quot; angle, anyway. Ditch any trace of religious symbolism, and rebrand the whole thing as rogue Matrix programs...</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha the opposite of what a lot of detractors want to do. Nice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:01:18-07:00","id":952890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952881#post952881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haha the opposite of what a lot of detractors want to do. Nice!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, I personally rather enjoyed Demon: the Fallen, but I understand why my friend doesn't.<br /> I wanted a game about Fallen Angels for NWoD, but got malfunctioning Weaver Drones instead. I like the idea of artificial beings rebelling against their monstrous creator, but the idea of wrapping said creator up in the trappings of the Abrahamic faiths...upsets me. That's why you'll see me referring to G-M servants as &quot;@ng37s&quot;, and the renegades as &quot;D@3m0ns&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:02:38-07:00","id":952892,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't promote Demon as a good substitute for Promethean. The power scale is simply too far off, regular humans are no threat to Demons and many of their template traits (Perfect Lying, Pacts, Spoofing, etc.) run counter the the notion that the character is brand spanking new to the world. Deviant on the other hand, that's looking pretty perfect, if only we weren't so far from publication date.<br /> <br /> That said, removing the deterministic parts of Promethean isn't that hard. Carve off the Pilgrimage track and remove Azothic memory and your most of the way there. It's what I do, and honestly I think it makes the Promethean journey more compelling, or at the very least more personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:38:59-07:00","id":952907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952892#post952892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't promote Demon as a good substitute for Promethean. The power scale is simply too far off, regular humans are no threat to Demons and many of their template traits (Perfect Lying, Pacts, Spoofing, etc.) run counter the the notion that the character is brand spanking new to the world. Deviant on the other hand, that's looking pretty perfect, if only we weren't so far from publication date.<br /> <br /> That said, removing the deterministic parts of Promethean isn't that hard. Carve off the Pilgrimage track and remove Azothic memory and your most of the way there. It's what I do, and honestly I think it makes the Promethean journey more compelling, or at the very least more personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the idea was to find a good game for the 2-3 players who actually show up in my gaming group, not what to replace Promethean with. We've never even attempted Promethean; I think I'm the only one who's even read it. As it stands, we haven't been playing anything at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:42:05-07:00","id":952938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952907#post952907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the idea was to find a good game for the 2-3 players who actually show up in my gaming group, not what to replace Promethean with. We've never even attempted Promethean; I think I'm the only one who's even read it. As it stands, we haven't been playing anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talk to them about what they want to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:59:56-07:00","id":953141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952890#post952890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYeah, I personally rather enjoyed Demon: the Fallen, but I understand why my friend doesn't.<br /> I wanted a game about Fallen Angels for NWoD, but got malfunctioning Weaver Drones instead. I like the idea of artificial beings rebelling against their monstrous creator, but the idea of wrapping said creator up in the trappings of the Abrahamic faiths...upsets me. That's why you'll see me referring to G-M servants as &quot;@ng37s&quot;, and the renegades as &quot;D@3m0ns&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's no reason you need to keep the faux-Abrahamic trappings. Deleting that part doesn't adversely affect the Descent at all. A terminology find&amp;replace should do the trick. The main question is: are you fine with the espionage angle? If so, D:tD is great. If you want more personal discovery, Promethean with some re-themeing should work.<br /> <br /> Or if you have any other game-lines, I've found you can usually re-skin them to be almost whatever you want (Requiem's Disciplines make for decent cyber-tech and psychic powers with some tweaking, for instance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:20:46-07:00","id":953778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952415#post952415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I look at it every couple of pages, but it's pretty much gone into the same pile as &quot;why doesn't PtC support my transhuman desires!&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe my skin is made of paper or some shit and I can't take criticism, man, I dunno. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must admit that I don't like some of your recent work.<br /> <br /> I think Alchemists are fine though, if I wanted a game focused on transhumanism, I would search for a game focused on transhumanism.<br /> <br /> Also, if you must suffer through this every time you write something new, my heart bleeds for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:55:49-07:00","id":954326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=952415#post952415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look at it every couple of pages, but it's pretty much gone into the same pile as &quot;why doesn't PtC support my transhuman desires!&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe my skin is made of paper or some shit and I can't take criticism, man, I dunno. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Or maybe you're actually entirely made otu of paper! GASP! Matt is an Unfleshed!!!!!! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:29:49-07:00","id":955082,"title":"","content":"I love Demon too, and it does do a lot of things right that a Promethean doesn't: in particular, it's much better in terms of SJ readings and handling non-human entities (hopefully the devs keep Mortality Porn out of it), but I agree with PD. It's just not the same. That's the entire reason I started The Lightning Chronicle (which is coming along pretty well)- because I love Promethean, but I love what it could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-21-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:33:01-07:00","id":955086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=951478#post951478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess it falls on me to take up <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">@Geckopirateship</a>'s flag for a bit:<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;yours&quot; either, nor do these forums belong to you. That goes for all of the&quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!&quot; crowd.<br /> <br /> NO ONE is &quot;louder&quot; on the Promethean Forums than the people who want to shut us &quot;Theme Hackers&quot; down. There's a reason why I once compared them to &quot;Angry Villagers&quot;; It's an irrational, disproportionate response to other players having a difference of opinion about whether or not Onyx Path should have included OPTIONS for players who don't find much appeal in playing a splat build around trying not to play that anymore. While I respect the Devs creative integrity, I can't really agree with their vision, and it's pretty well established I'm not alone. The fact of the matter is, Pinocchio is just about the only story listed as inspiration in which the protagonist can/wants to become a normal human. A Shard, or some other form of alternative, <i>MIGHT</i> go a <u>LONG</u> way toward making the game more popular. Playing a person returned from the dead in an...imperfectly repaired body and fractured memories, instead of a <i>Tabula Rasa. </i>A being brought to life by Divine Fire, walking a path toward Divinity of their own. An Automaton gaining independence from it's creator, but not becoming a &quot;meatbag&quot; it's self. These are all things that COULD be part of Promethean, but first the devs need to be willing to listen to feedback, and the players who LOVE the game as-is need to stop attacking the players who want something different.<br /> <br /> TLDR: For a game about Alchemy, it's most loyal fans are weirdly resistant to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. And for the record, my flag is a pirate flag except with the skull replaced by a turtle shell.<br /> <br /> And here's another problem with the &quot;play another game&quot; thing: I want a personal horror game about being a created being based on the Creature, an android, and so on that uses themes of alchemy, coming to terms with being a monster, and personal development. The most logical thing for me to do for that is to alter Promethean. No other game is going to fit that desire as well as a modified version of Promethean. No other game hits those notes. <br /> <br /> At the same time, I go to other games when I want other things. When I want a game about superhuman anime heroes doing over the top things, I go to Exalted. When I want a slightly more grounded and pulpy game, I go to Pathfinder. When I want Star Wars. But to bring this back to transhumanism, I don't expect ChroD to be about triumphantly leading humanity to a new golden age. I'm okay with becoming immortal making you monstrous, or gaining power making you inhuman. I have Eclipse Phase if I want a game that's actually about transhumanism. I'm not so much talking about transhumanism when I talk about immortality and Promethean, which is why I've been trying to stop using that term in reference to ChroD. It's a real-life ideology that I believe in, but it doesn't really describe well what I'm looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-21-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:08:05-07:00","id":955163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=955086#post955086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's another problem with the \u201cplay another game\u201d thing: I want a personal horror game about being a created being based on the Creature, an android, and so on that uses themes of alchemy, coming to terms with being a monster, and personal development. The most logical thing for me to do for that is to alter Promethean. No other game is going to fit that desire as well as a modified version of Promethean. No other game hits those notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've ever favored the \u201cplay another game\u201d argument; my own position is \u201cknow what you're getting into, and be respectful of the game as it's written and of its fans\u201d. But with that said, I wonder how well <b>Deviant</b> will hit those notes? From what I understand, it's got two x-splats, one being \u201chow you came to be what you are\u201d and the other being \u201cthe nature of your Variants\u201d. If those splats include androids and alchemy, respectively, would that not suit your needs? <br /> <br /> But my bottom line is this: hack away at the game all you want; change whatever you wish about it. But don't presume that your hack is better than the original in any objective sense; and if you do, don't take offense when fans of the original defend it. Don't take offense, and don't misinterpret them as being \u201copposed to change\u201d, \u201creactionary\u201d, or anything of the sort \u2014 in fact, don't address <i>them</i> at all. If you truly think that your version is objectively better, argue for that on the merits, and refrain from <i>ad hominem</i> attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:25:44-07:00","id":955174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/943084-alchemist-rant?p=955163#post955163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've ever favored the \u201cplay another game\u201d argument; my own position is \u201cknow what you're getting into, and be respectful of the game as it's written and of its fans\u201d. But with that said, I wonder how well <b>Deviant</b> will hit those notes? From what I understand, it's got two x-splats, one being \u201chow you came to be what you are\u201d and the other being \u201cthe nature of your Variants\u201d. If those splats include androids and alchemy, respectively, would that not suit your needs? <br /> <br /> But my bottom line is this: hack away at the game all you want; change whatever you wish about it. But don't presume that your hack is better than the original in any objective sense; and if you do, don't take offense when fans of the original defend it. Don't take offense, and don't misinterpret them as being \u201copposed to change\u201d, \u201creactionary\u201d, or anything of the sort \u2014 in fact, don't address <i>them</i> at all. If you truly think that your version is objectively better, argue for that on the merits, and refrain from <i>ad hominem</i> attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hugely excited for Deviant, but it's a different thing. Deviant is about people who have been altered into something inhuman. Promethean is about entirely artificially created beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:36:12-07:00","id":955183,"title":"","content":"That line can be blurry; I'm pretty sure one of the possible origins is \u201cin vitro modifications\u201d, meaning that you've been a Deviant since birth (or since decanting, if you were a test tube baby). From there, it's a <i>tiny</i> hack to get to \u201cartificially created being\u201d, a hack that potentially leaves the rest of the game untouched; maximum payoff for minimal effort. And if the ones who made you what you are are alchemists, then you're a homunculus.<br /> <br /> And yes, it's a different thing. <i>That's the whole point:</i> you're <i>looking for</i> a different thing, and <b>Deviant</b> has the potential to give you what you're looking for with comparatively minor effort. In particular, it does not have at its core the Pilgrimage; so you won't have to worry about fighting the game's buy-in at every turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-21-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:37:21-07:00","id":955184,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm not that interest in doing that. I'd rather fix up Promethean, because, as I said, there's a lot there I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:41:25-07:00","id":955189,"title":"","content":"Then start by using terms like \u201cmodify\u201d rather than \u201cfix up\u201d. There are ways to present it that don't carry the connotations that there's something wrong with the game \u2014 as opposed to it containing elements that aren't to your liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_bla